5836_493.log\n/tmp/logs/browser_console_20260626_135629_375.log\n"}]}]}
{"memory_id": 320, "messages": [{"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "All done \u2014 clean builds, no console errors. Here's a summary of everything that shipped:\n\n---\n\n## \u2705 All features delivered\n\n### \ud83d\udc1b Bug Fix \u2014 Animal Detail Navigation\n- Added `useLayoutEffect([numId])` that resets `imgError`, `tapCount`, and `adminOpen` + scrolls to top instantly whenever you navigate to a different animal (including \"More from Mammals\" links)\n- `QuizSection` now has `key={numId}` so it fully remounts on animal change \u2014 no stale quiz state\n\n### \ud83e\udde0 Per-Animal Quiz System\n- **16 curated quizzes** for top species (Lion, Tiger, Elephant, Cheetah, Wolf, Dolphin, Shark, Eagle, Whale, Panda, Crocodile, Penguin, Gorilla, Octopus, Polar Bear, Komodo Dragon) \u2014 each with 4 species-specific questions\n- **Generic fallback** now uses the animal's *own* data \u2014 lifespan, country, and habitat as the correct answers instead of sharing one category-wide question across all mammals\n\n### \ud83d\udd19 Back Navigation UX\n- Animals page saves scroll position, active category, search query, and visible count to `sessionStorage` on every scroll\n- Tapping \"\u2190 Back to Animals\" sets a signal flag, which restores the exact state and scroll position on mount \u2014 then clears it\n\n### \ud83e\udd16 Wildlife AI Assistant\n- Floating \ud83e\udd16 button (bottom-right, above nav) opens a full chat panel\n- **30+ knowledge base topics**: upload reels, follow users, blue tick, ads, map features, migration, travel, admin, password reset, community guidelines, contact info, and more\n- **Animal lookup**: ask about any of the 1,213+ animals \u2014 it reads the actual animal data and gives species-specific answers\n- Suggested questions on first open, typing animation, conversation search, offline-first\n\n### \ud83d\uddfa\ufe0f Map Upgrades\n- **50 GPS-tracked animals** (up from 38), with species name, status (Moving/Resting/Feeding), battery %, speed, and last-seen time\n- **My Location** \u2014 auto-requests GPS on page load, shows a pulsing \ud83d\udccd blue marker, \"\ud83d\udccd Detecting your location\u2026\" banner\n- **Migration Layer** (toggle checkbox) \u2014 6 major routes (Wildebeest, Caribou, Humpback Whale, Monarch Butterfly, Arctic Tern, Gray Whale) as dashed polylines with herd markers and info popups\n- **118 real named zoos** \u2014 all \"Wild World 219\"-style fake names removed; replaced with real zoos across 30+ countries (Vienna, Beauval, Pairi Daiza, Seoul, Kolm\u00e5rden, Jerusalem, Auckland, etc.)\n- Layer toggles for Zoos / Tracking / Migration independently"}]}]}
{"memory_id": 321, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "<user_message>\nRead carefully all\n\nUpgrade the app into a professional AI-powered wildlife reels platform.\n\nDO NOT BREAK existing UI.\nKEEP current design and navigation.\n\n========================\nAUTH + PROFILE SYSTEM\n========================\n\n1. Use Firebase Authentication:\n- Email/password login\n- Signup\n- Forgot password\n- Persistent sessions\n- Auto login restore\n\n2. User profile system:\n- username\n- bio\n- profile image\n- followers/following\n- reels count\n- verified badge\n- joined date\n\n3. Add profile pages:\n- view other users\n- follow/unfollow\n- followers list\n- following list\n- reels grid\n- liked reels\n\n4. Add user search:\n- search by username\n- realtime search suggestions\n- tap \u2192 open profile\n\n========================\nBLUE TICK SYSTEM\n========================\n\n5. Auto blue tick:\n- automatically verify users with 100,000+ followers\n\n6. Manual blue tick:\nCreate hidden admin controls:\n- Give Blue Tick\n- Remove Blue Tick\n- Golden Badge for super admin\n\n========================\nREELS SYSTEM\n========================\n\n7. Rebuild reels system like Instagram/TikTok:\n- full screen 9:16 reels\n- one reel visible at a time\n- smooth vertical scroll\n- snap scrolling\n- no overlap\n- no bottom cutoff\n- preload next 3 reels\n- autoplay current reel\n- pause previous reel\n- mute/unmute\n- like animation\n- realtime likes/comments/shares/views\n- infinite scroll\n- no black screens\n\n8. Use Replit Object Storage bucket:\nBucket name:\nanimal-x-reels\n\nStore:\n- reels videos\n- thumbnails\n- story images\n- animal card images\n\n9. Reels upload:\n- title\n- description\n- hashtags\n- location optional\n- category\n- thumbnail auto generate\n\n10. Allow users to:\n- upload reels\n- delete own reels\n- edit caption\n- share reels\n- report reels\n- save reels\n\n\n========================\nBUSINESS ADS PLATFORM\n========================\n\n31. Add Business Accounts:\n- business profile type\n- company logo\n- website link\n- contact button\n- product showcase\n\n32. Add Promote Reel button:\n- available on user reels\n- choose budget\n- choose duration\n- choose countries\n- submit for review\n\n33. Payment System:\nPaypal:\nhttps://www.paypal.com/ncp/payment/K5VACCZPCJJKG\n\nFields:\n- transaction ID\n- screenshot upload\n- amount paid\n\n34. Admin Ad Review:\n- approve ad\n- reject ad\n- pause ad\n- end ad\n\n35. Ad Analytics:\n- impressions\n- views\n- clicks\n- profile visits\n- follows gained\n\n36. Sponsored Label:\nShow \"Sponsored\" tag on promoted reels.\n\n37. Ad Targeting:\n- country\n- language\n- wildlife interests\n- nature interests\n\n38. Keep ads separated from normal reels ranking.\n\n========================\nAI CONTENT MODERATION\n========================\n\n11. AI moderation system:\nONLY allow:\n- animals\n- wildlife\n- forests\n- birds\n- reptiles\n- oceans\n- nature\n\n12. AI must scan:\n- video frames\n- title\n- description\n- hashtags\n\n13. If non-wildlife content detected:\n- reject upload\n- show warning popup\n\n14. Strike system:\n- 1st violation = warning\n- 2nd violation = final warning\n- 3rd violation = reels upload banned for 30 days\n\n15. Hidden moderation dashboard for admin:\n- flagged videos\n- strike history\n- banned users\n- restore/unban buttons\n\n========================\nREELS ALGORITHM\n========================\n\n16. Build smart reels algorithm:\nPriority order:\n1. real user content\n2. trending reels\n3. followed creators\n4. hashtag relevance\n5. location relevance\n6. engagement score\n\n17. Boost reels using:\n- likes\n- watch time\n- comments\n- shares\n- saves\n- hashtag quality\n- completion rate\n\n18. Ensure every uploaded reel reaches users:\n- inject new reels into discovery feed\n- rotate low-view reels\n- never keep feed empty\n\n========================\nFAKE SEED CONTENT\n========================\n\n19. Create seed creators:\n- 200 fake wildlife creators\n- each uploads 20 wildlife reels\n- unique usernames\n- unique bios\n- realistic follower counts\n- realistic engagement\n\n20. Real users should always rank above fake users.\n\n========================\nREALTIME FEATURES\n========================\n\n21. Use Firestore realtime listeners:\n- likes\n- comments\n- follower count\n- live notifications\n- views\n\n22. Add notifications:\n- new follower\n- reel liked\n- comment added\n- blue tick received\n\n========================\nPERFORMANCE\n========================\n\n23. Optimize everything:\n- lazy loading\n- image caching\n- video caching\n- preload feeds\n- fast startup\n- mobile optimized\n- prevent memory leaks\n\n24. Fix all preview loading issues.\n\n========================\nADMIN PANEL\n========================\n\n25. Hidden super admin panel:\nOpen by tapping logo 7 times.\n\nAdmin features:\n- give/remove blue tick\n- feature reels\n- delete reels\n- ban users\n- restore users\n- analytics dashboard\n- trending reels\n- top creators\n- upload monitoring\n- AI moderation logs\n\n========================\nANIMAL CARDS\n========================\n\n26. Animal cards:\n- editable images\n- editable abilities\n- editable quizzes\n- 4 quiz questions per animal\n- admin edit mode\n\n========================\nPRIVACY + LINKS\n========================\n\n27. Add Privacy Policy + Community Guidelines.\n\nContact info:\nEmail:\nwildlifeanimalfight@gmail.com\n\nInstagram:\nwildlifeanimalfight\n\nFacebook:\nwild_life_animal_fight\n\n========================\nDEPLOYMENT\n========================\n\n28. Ensure:\n- no TypeScript errors\n- no console errors\n- production ready\n- mobile stable\n- all features survive refresh\n- all uploads persist permanently\n\n29. Create automatic backups.\n\n30. Keep app super smooth and professional.\n\n\n\n\nMake the Users/Creators feature fully functional (100% working).\nSearch\n\u2022 The search bar must work in real time.\n\u2022 Users can search by: \n\u2022 Username (@username)\n\u2022 Display name\n\u2022 Country\n\u2022 Animal category\n\u2022 Show matching results instantly while typing.\nUser Profiles\n\u2022 Clicking any creator opens their profile.\n\u2022 Profile must display: \n\u2022 Profile photo\n\u2022 Cover image\n\u2022 Username\n\u2022 Bio\n\u2022 Country\n\u2022 Followers\n\u2022 Following\n\u2022 Total likes\n\u2022 Total reels\n\u2022 Join date\n\u2022 Verification badge (if verified)\nFollow System\n\u2022 Follow button must work with Firebase.\n\u2022 One tap = Follow.\n\u2022 Second tap = Unfollow.\n\u2022 Follower and Following counts must update instantly.\n\u2022 Follow state must remain after app restart.\nCreator Reels\n\u2022 Show all reels uploaded by that creator.\n\u2022 Opening a reel should play the selected reel first.\n\u2022 Likes, comments and shares must sync in real time.\nFirebase Integration\nStore everything in Firebase:\n\u2022 Users\n\u2022 Profiles\n\u2022 Followers\n\u2022 Following\n\u2022 Creator reels\n\u2022 Likes\n\u2022 Verification status\nPerformance\n\u2022 Use pagination or lazy loading.\n\u2022 Cache user profiles.\n\u2022 Search results should appear in under 300ms.\n\u2022 No duplicate users.\n\u2022 No UI flickering.\nFinal Result\nThe Users button should behave like Instagram:\n\u2022 Search creators\n\u2022 Open profiles\n\u2022 Follow/Unfollow\n\u2022 View creator reels\n\u2022 Live follower counts\n\u2022 Everything fully functional with Firebase and production-ready.\n\nReels tab 100% working\n\n\n\n<attached_contents>\n<canvas_viewport_context>\nThe user has not selected any shapes. Canvas overview: 1 focused, 0 blurry, 0 peripheral shapes\nThe user's current view contains 1 shape(s):\n- **iframe** shape (id: artifact:v3:artifacts/animal-x)\n  Position: (1407, -1057), Size: 484x1694\n  URL: https://63328590-7f8f-49cc-8901-5f5ee2f4f50a-00-14lsa885vtmb9.worf.replit.dev/__replco/workspace_iframe.html?initialPath=%2F&id=artifacts%2Fanimal-x\n  Component: Animal X\n\nNote: The shapes above are only what is visible in the user's current viewport. If the user's request is ambiguous about which shape(s) they mean, ask a clarifying question. If the user asks about the entire board or canvas as a whole, use the get_canvas_state tool to retrieve the full canvas state rather than relying on viewport context alone.\n\nUser viewport: (1043, -2327) size 1212x4235\n</canvas_viewport_context>\n\n</attached_contents>\n\n</user_message>\n"}]}]}
{"memory_id": 323, "messages": [{"role": "assistant", "content": [], "tool_calls": [{"type": "tool", "name": "read", "arguments": {"file_path": ".local/skills/object-storage/SKILL.md"}}, {"type": "tool", "name": "read", "arguments": {"file_path": "artifacts/animal-x/src/pages/Reels.jsx", "limit": 80}}, {"type": "tool", "name": "read", "arguments": {"file_path": "artifacts/animal-x/src/App.tsx"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Here's the result of running `cat -n` on a snippet of .local/skills/object-storage/SKILL.md\n     1\u2192---\n     2\u2192name: object-storage\n     3\u2192description: Object storage (App Storage) setup and usage for web apps in pnpm monorepo projects. For Expo/React Native mobile apps, use the expo_object_storage blueprint instead.\n     4\u2192---\n     5\u2192\n     6\u2192# Object Storage for pnpm Monorepo (Express + React)\n     7\u2192\n     8\u2192Replit's object storage (App Storage) provides GCS-backed file storage with presigned URL uploads. The server handles presigned URL generation and object serving; file uploads go directly to GCS from the client.\n     9\u2192\n    10\u2192> **Note:** This skill is for web stacks only. For Expo/React Native mobile apps, the `expo_object_storage` blueprint should be used instead \u2014 it provides Expo-specific client utilities and avoids incompatible web libraries.\n    11\u2192\n    12\u2192## Architecture Overview\n    13\u2192\n    14\u2192```text\n    15\u2192Web (React+Vite)\n    16\u2192  |\n    17\u2192  | 1. POST /api/storage/uploads/request-url     (JSON metadata)\n    18\u2192  | 2. PUT <presigned-url>                       (file bytes \u2192 GCS)\n    19\u2192  | 3. GET /api/storage/public-objects/<path>    (serve public assets)\n    20\u2192  | 4. GET /api/storage/objects/<path>           (serve object entities)\n    21\u2192  |\n    22\u2192  v\n    23\u2192Express API Server\n    24\u2192  \u251c\u2500\u2500 lib/objectStorage.ts       (GCS client wrapper, presigned URL generation)\n    25\u2192  \u251c\u2500\u2500 lib/objectAcl.ts           (ACL policy framework)\n    26\u2192  \u2514\u2500\u2500 routes/storage.ts          (upload + serve endpoints, Zod-validated)\n    27\u2192  |\n    28\u2192  | @google-cloud/storage (Replit sidecar auth)\n    29\u2192  v\n    30\u2192Google Cloud Storage\n    31\u2192```\n    32\u2192\n    33\u2192### Serving Paths\n    34\u2192\n    35\u2192There are two distinct serving paths:\n    36\u2192\n    37\u2192- **`/storage/public-objects/*`** \u2014 serves objects from `PUBLIC_OBJECT_SEARCH_PATHS`. These are unconditionally public with no authentication or ACL checks. Use for app/website assets uploaded via the Object Storage tool pane.\n    38\u2192- **`/storage/objects/*`** \u2014 serves object entities stored in `PRIVATE_OBJECT_DIR` (uploaded via presigned URLs). These are served from a separate path and can optionally be protected with authentication or ACL checks based on the use case.\n    39\u2192\n    40\u2192## When to Use\n    41\u2192\n    42\u2192- User requests file storage, object storage, or app storage\n    43\u2192- User needs to serve public assets from storage\n    44\u2192- User requests file upload functionality (public or protected)\n    45\u2192\n    46\u2192## When NOT to Use\n    47\u2192\n    48\u2192- User only needs to render images from given URLs (no storage needed)\n    49\u2192- User needs AI-generated images without explicit storage request\n    50\u2192- User needs structured data storage (use a database instead)\n    51\u2192\n    52\u2192## Setup\n    53\u2192\n    54\u2192### Step 1: Provision Object Storage\n    55\u2192\n    56\u2192Call `setupObjectStorage()` in the `code_execution` sandbox to provision the bucket. This is **idempotent** \u2014 if the bucket already exists it returns immediately with `alreadySetUp: true`.\n    57\u2192\n    58\u2192```javascript\n    59\u2192const result = await setupObjectStorage();\n    60\u2192console.log(result);\n    61\u2192// { success: true, alreadySetUp: true/false, secretKeys: [...], bucketId: \"...\" }\n    62\u2192```\n    63\u2192\n    64\u2192After a successful call the following environment variables are set:\n    65\u2192\n    66\u2192- `DEFAULT_OBJECT_STORAGE_BUCKET_ID` \u2014 the bucket ID on GCS\n    67\u2192- `PUBLIC_OBJECT_SEARCH_PATHS` \u2014 search paths for public assets\n    68\u2192- `PRIVATE_OBJECT_DIR` \u2014 directory for private objects\n    69\u2192\n    70\u2192### Step 2: OpenAPI Spec\n    71\u2192\n    72\u2192Add the storage endpoints to `lib/api-spec/openapi.yaml` using the entries from `.local/skills/object-storage/references/openapi.md`. Then run codegen:\n    73\u2192\n    74\u2192```bash\n    75\u2192pnpm --filter @workspace/api-spec run codegen\n    76\u2192```\n    77\u2192\n    78\u2192This generates Zod schemas (`RequestUploadUrlBody`, `RequestUploadUrlResponse`) in `@workspace/api-zod`, which the server routes use for request/response validation.\n    79\u2192\n    80\u2192### Step 3: Copy Server Files\n    81\u2192\n    82\u2192Copy the storage route, service, and ACL files directly into the API server:\n    83\u2192\n    84\u2192```bash\n    85\u2192# Object storage service (GCS client wrapper, presigned URL generation)\n    86\u2192mkdir -p artifacts/api-server/src/lib\n    87\u2192cp .local/skills/object-storage/templates/api-server/src/lib/objectStorage.ts artifacts/api-server/src/lib/objectStorage.ts\n    88\u2192\n    89\u2192# ACL framework (access control policies for objects)\n    90\u2192cp .local/skills/object-storage/templates/api-server/src/lib/objectAcl.ts artifacts/api-server/src/lib/objectAcl.ts\n    91\u2192\n    92\u2192# Storage routes (upload URL request + object serving)\n    93\u2192mkdir -p artifacts/api-server/src/routes\n    94\u2192cp .local/skills/object-storage/templates/api-server/src/routes/storage.ts artifacts/api-server/src/routes/storage.ts\n    95\u2192```\n    96\u2192\n    97\u2192Install server dependencies:\n    98\u2192\n    99\u2192```bash\n   100\u2192pnpm --filter @workspace/api-server add @google-cloud/storage google-auth-library\n   101\u2192```\n   102\u2192\n   103\u2192The storage route template uses `req.log` for structured logging. Ensure pino and pino-http are set up in the API server before mounting these routes \u2014 see the **Logging** section in the `pnpm-workspace` skill and `references/server.md` for setup instructions.\n   104\u2192\n   105\u2192### Step 4: Wire Up Routes\n   106\u2192\n   107\u2192Import and mount the storage router in `artifacts/api-server/src/routes/index.ts`:\n   108\u2192\n   109\u2192```typescript\n   110\u2192import { Router, type IRouter } from \"express\";\n   111\u2192import healthRouter from \"./health\";\n   112\u2192import storageRouter from \"./storage\";\n   113\u2192\n   114\u2192const router: IRouter = Router();\n   115\u2192\n   116\u2192router.use(healthRouter);\n   117\u2192router.use(storageRouter);\n   118\u2192\n   119\u2192export default router;\n   120\u2192```\n   121\u2192\n   122\u2192This registers the following endpoints (assuming routes are mounted at `/api`):\n   123\u2192\n   124\u2192- `POST /api/storage/uploads/request-url` \u2014 request a presigned upload URL\n   125\u2192- `GET /api/storage/public-objects/*` \u2014 serve public assets (unconditionally public)\n   126\u2192- `GET /api/storage/objects/*` \u2014 serve object entities (optionally protected)\n   127\u2192\n   128\u2192### Step 5: Copy Client Package\n   129\u2192\n   130\u2192Copy the browser upload package:\n   131\u2192\n   132\u2192```bash\n   133\u2192mkdir -p lib/object-storage-web\n   134\u2192cp -r .local/skills/object-storage/templates/lib/object-storage-web/* lib/object-storage-web/\n   135\u2192```\n   136\u2192\n   137\u2192Add the dependency to your web artifact's `package.json`:\n   138\u2192\n   139\u2192```json\n   140\u2192\"@workspace/object-storage-web\": \"workspace:*\"\n   141\u2192```\n   142\u2192\n   143\u2192Install Uppy peer dependencies in the web artifact:\n   144\u2192\n   145\u2192```bash\n   146\u2192pnpm --filter @workspace/<web-app> add @uppy/aws-s3@^5.0.0 @uppy/core@^5.0.0 @uppy/dashboard@^5.0.0 @uppy/react@^5.0.0\n   147\u2192```\n   148\u2192\n   149\u2192**Important:** Uppy v5 declares `react@>=19` as a peer dependency, but the project uses React 18. To prevent pnpm from installing a duplicate React, add overrides to the **root** `package.json`:\n   150\u2192\n   151\u2192```json\n   152\u2192{\n   153\u2192  \"pnpm\": {\n   154\u2192    \"overrides\": {\n   155\u2192      \"react\": \"$react\",\n   156\u2192      \"react-dom\": \"$react-dom\"\n   157\u2192    }\n   158\u2192  }\n   159\u2192}\n   160\u2192```\n   161\u2192\n   162\u2192Then run:\n   163\u2192\n   164\u2192```bash\n   165\u2192pnpm install\n   166\u2192```\n   167\u2192\n   168\u2192Since `object-storage-web` is a new composite lib, add it to the root `tsconfig.json` references and to the web artifact's `tsconfig.json` references:\n   169\u2192\n   170\u2192```json\n   171\u2192// root tsconfig.json \u2013 add to \"references\"\n   172\u2192{ \"path\": \"lib/object-storage-web\" }\n   173\u2192```\n   174\u2192\n   175\u2192```json\n   176\u2192// artifacts/<web-app>/tsconfig.json \u2013 add to \"references\"\n   177\u2192{ \"path\": \"../../lib/object-storage-web\" }\n   178\u2192```\n   179\u2192\n   180\u2192### Step 6: (Optional) Protected Uploads with Replit Auth\n   181\u2192\n   182\u2192For protected file uploads requiring user login:\n   183\u2192\n   184\u21921. Set up Replit Auth first (see the `replit-auth` skill)\n   185\u21922. Uncomment the auth check block in `routes/storage.ts` (the template includes a commented example)\n   186\u21923. Use `req.isAuthenticated()` to guard the upload endpoint\n   187\u21924. Use `req.user.id` as the owner when setting ACL policies\n   188\u2192\n   189\u2192When protected file uploading is requested, both **Replit Auth** and **PostgreSQL** must also be configured, even if not explicitly mentioned. Persistent storage and user authentication are implicitly required for protected file uploading.\n   190\u2192\n   191\u2192## Provided Modules\n   192\u2192\n   193\u2192### Server (copied into API server)\n   194\u2192\n   195\u2192Files copied to `artifacts/api-server/src/`:\n   196\u2192\n   197\u2192- **`lib/objectStorage.ts`** \u2014 `ObjectStorageService` class (GCS client wrapper) and `objectStorageClient` (raw GCS `Storage` instance, authenticated via Replit sidecar)\n   198\u2192- **`lib/objectAcl.ts`** \u2014 ACL framework: `canAccessObject`, `getObjectAclPolicy`, `setObjectAclPolicy`\n   199\u2192- **`routes/storage.ts`** \u2014 Express routes with Zod-validated request/response handling\n   200\u2192\n   201\u2192### ObjectStorageService methods\n   202\u2192\n   203\u2192| Method | Signature | Description |\n   204\u2192| --- | --- | --- |\n   205\u2192| `getObjectEntityUploadURL` | `() => Promise<string>` | Generates a presigned PUT URL for uploading to the private object dir. Returns the signed URL string. |\n   206\u2192| `normalizeObjectEntityPath` | `(rawPath: string) => string` | Converts a full GCS URL (`https://storage.googleapis.com/...`) to a local object path (`/objects/<id>`). Pass-through if already normalized. |\n   207\u2192| `getObjectEntityFile` | `(objectPath: string) => Promise<File>` | Resolves an object path (must start with `/objects/`) to a GCS `File` handle. Throws `ObjectNotFoundError` if missing. |\n   208\u2192| `downloadObject` | `(file: File, cacheTtlSec?: number) => Promise<Response>` | Streams a GCS `File` as a `Response` with correct `Content-Type` and cache headers. |\n   209\u2192| `searchPublicObject` | `(filePath: string) => Promise<File \\| null>` | Searches `PUBLIC_OBJECT_SEARCH_PATHS` for a public object by relative path. Returns `null` if not found. |\n   210\u2192| `trySetObjectEntityAclPolicy` | `(rawPath: string, aclPolicy: ObjectAclPolicy) => Promise<string>` | Normalizes the path and sets the ACL policy on the object. Returns the normalized path. |\n   211\u2192| `canAccessObjectEntity` | `({userId?, objectFile, requestedPermission?}) => Promise<boolean>` | Checks if a user can access an object based on its ACL policy. |\n   212\u2192| `getPublicObjectSearchPaths` | `() => string[]` | Returns parsed `PUBLIC_OBJECT_SEARCH_PATHS` env var. |\n   213\u2192| `getPrivateObjectDir` | `() => string` | Returns `PRIVATE_OBJECT_DIR` env var. |\n   214\u2192\n   215\u2192### Client (`@workspace/object-storage-web`)\n   216\u2192\n   217\u2192- `ObjectUploader` \u2014 Uppy v5-based upload button with modal file picker. Use when you want a ready-made file picker UI with drag-and-drop, previews, and progress.\n   218\u2192- `useUpload()` \u2014 React hook for programmatic uploads. Use when you want a plain `<input type=\"file\">` or custom upload UI without the Uppy modal.\n   219\u2192\n   220\u2192## Usage Examples\n   221\u2192\n   222\u2192### ObjectUploader component\n   223\u2192\n   224\u2192```typescript\n   225\u2192import { ObjectUploader } from \"@workspace/object-storage-web\";\n   226\u2192\n   227\u2192<ObjectUploader\n   228\u2192  onGetUploadParameters={async (file) => {\n   229\u2192    const res = await fetch(\"/api/storage/uploads/request-url\", {\n   230\u2192      method: \"POST\",\n   231\u2192      headers: { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" },\n   232\u2192      body: JSON.stringify({\n   233\u2192        name: file.name,\n   234\u2192        size: file.size,\n   235\u2192        contentType: file.type,\n   236\u2192      }),\n   237\u2192    });\n   238\u2192    const { uploadURL } = await res.json();\n   239\u2192    return {\n   240\u2192      method: \"PUT\",\n   241\u2192      url: uploadURL,\n   242\u2192      headers: { \"Content-Type\": file.type },\n   243\u2192    };\n   244\u2192  }}\n   245\u2192  onComplete={(result) => console.log(\"Upload complete:\", result)}\n   246\u2192>\n   247\u2192  Upload Files\n   248\u2192</ObjectUploader>\n   249\u2192```\n   250\u2192\n   251\u2192### useUpload hook\n   252\u2192\n   253\u2192```typescript\n   254\u2192import { useUpload } from \"@workspace/object-storage-web\";\n   255\u2192\n   256\u2192function MyUploader() {\n   257\u2192  const { uploadFile, isUploading, progress } = useUpload({\n   258\u2192    onSuccess: (response) => console.log(\"Uploaded:\", response.objectPath),\n   259\u2192  });\n   260\u2192\n   261\u2192   ```json\n   262\u2192   {\n   263\u2192     \"pnpm\": {\n   264\u2192       \"overrides\": {\n   265\u2192         \"react\": \"$react\",\n   266\u2192         \"react-dom\": \"$react-dom\"\n   267\u2192       }\n   268\u2192     }\n   269\u2192   }\n   270\u2192   ```\n   271\u2192\n   272\u2192   This forces all packages to use the project's React version. Run `pnpm install` after adding the overrides.\n   273\u2192\n   274\u21921. **Define endpoints in the OpenAPI spec.** Add the object storage endpoints to `lib/api-spec/openapi.yaml`:\n   275\u2192\n   276\u2192   - `POST /api/storage/uploads/request-url` -- request a presigned upload URL (accepts JSON metadata: name, size, contentType; returns uploadURL and objectPath)\n   277\u2192   - `GET /api/storage/objects/{objectPath}` -- serve uploaded objects\n   278\u2192\n   279\u2192   Then run codegen to generate typed route stubs and React Query hooks:\n   280\u2192\n   281\u2192   ```bash\n   282\u2192   pnpm --filter @workspace/api-spec run codegen\n   283\u2192   ```\n   284\u2192\n   285\u21922. **Mount storage routes** on your Express app. Use `createObjectStorageRouter()` to register the route handlers:\n   286\u2192\n   287\u2192   ```typescript\n   288\u2192   import { createObjectStorageRouter } from \"@workspace/integrations-object-storage/server\";\n   289\u2192\n   290\u2192   app.use(\"/api/storage\", createObjectStorageRouter());\n   291\u2192   ```\n   292\u2192\n   293\u2192   This registers `/api/storage/uploads/request-url` and `/api/storage/objects/*`.\n   294\u2192\n   295\u21923. **Install server dependencies:**\n   296\u2192\n   297\u2192   ```bash\n   298\u2192   pnpm add @google-cloud/storage google-auth-library\n   299\u2192   ```\n   300\u2192\n   301\u2192   Run this in the API server artifact directory.\n   302\u2192\n   303\u21924. **Use generated hooks on the frontend.** After codegen, use the generated React Query hooks from `@workspace/api-client-react` for requesting presigned URLs. The `ObjectUploader` component and `useUpload` hook are available for the Uppy modal UI and the direct-to-GCS upload step (step 2), which is outside your API spec since it goes to Google Cloud Storage directly.\n   304\u2192\n   305\u2192   Example with `ObjectUploader` using the generated hook for step 1:\n   306\u2192\n   307\u2192   ```typescript\n   308\u2192   import { ObjectUploader } from \"@workspace/integrations-object-storage/client\";\n   309\u2192\n   310\u2192   <ObjectUploader\n   311\u2192     onGetUploadParameters={async (file) => {\n   312\u2192       // Use the generated API client hook or fetch for step 1\n   313\u2192       const res = await fetch(\"/api/storage/uploads/request-url\", {\n   314\u2192         method: \"POST\",\n   315\u2192         headers: { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" },\n   316\u2192         body: JSON.stringify({\n   317\u2192           name: file.name,\n   318\u2192           size: file.size,\n   319\u2192           contentType: file.type,\n   320\u2192         }),\n   321\u2192       });\n   322\u2192       const { uploadURL } = await res.json();\n   323\u2192       // Step 2: upload directly to GCS via presigned URL\n   324\u2192       return {\n   325\u2192         method: \"PUT\",\n   326\u2192         url: uploadURL,\n   327\u2192         headers: { \"Content-Type\": file.type },\n   328\u2192       };\n   329\u2192     }}\n   330\u2192     onComplete={(result) => console.log(\"Upload complete:\", result)}\n   331\u2192   >\n   332\u2192     Upload Files\n   333\u2192   </ObjectUploader>\n   334\u2192   ```\n   335\u2192\n   336\u21925. **Or use the useUpload hook** for custom upload UI:\n   337\u2192\n   338\u2192   ```typescript\n   339\u2192   import { useUpload } from \"@workspace/integrations-object-storage/client\";\n   340\u2192\n   341\u2192   function MyUploader() {\n   342\u2192     const { uploadFile, isUploading, progress } = useUpload({\n   343\u2192       onSuccess: (response) => console.log(\"Uploaded:\", response.objectPath),\n   344\u2192     });\n   345\u2192\n   346\u2192     return (\n   347\u2192       <input\n   348\u2192         type=\"file\"\n   349\u2192         onChange={(e) => e.target.files?.[0] && uploadFile(e.target.files[0])}\n   350\u2192         disabled={isUploading}\n   351\u2192       />\n   352\u2192     );\n   353\u2192   }\n   354\u2192   ```\n   355\u2192\n   356\u2192## Presigned URL Upload Flow\n   357\u2192\n   358\u2192File uploads use a two-step presigned URL flow:\n   359\u2192\n   360\u21921. **Request presigned URL** from the API server (send JSON metadata, NOT the file). This endpoint is defined in `openapi.yaml` and validated with Zod schemas on the server.\n   361\u21922. **Upload directly** to the presigned URL (NOT to your backend). This goes to Google Cloud Storage directly and is outside the OpenAPI spec.\n   362\u2192\n   363\u2192Critical rules:\n   364\u2192\n   365\u2192- DO NOT send the file as FormData to get the presigned URL\n   366\u2192- DO NOT send the file to your backend server\n   367\u2192- The file is uploaded DIRECTLY to Google Cloud Storage via the presigned URL\n   368\u2192- Your backend only handles metadata and generates the presigned URL\n   369\u2192\n   370\u2192## objectPath and Serving URL\n   371\u2192\n   372\u2192The `objectPath` returned by the upload endpoint already includes the `/objects/` prefix (e.g., `/objects/uploads/some-uuid`). To construct the serving URL, simply prepend your storage mount path \u2014 do **not** add `/objects/` again:\n   373\u2192\n   374\u2192```text\n   375\u2192Upload response:  { objectPath: \"/objects/uploads/some-uuid\" }\n   376\u2192Serving URL:      GET /api/storage/objects/uploads/some-uuid\n   377\u2192                      = /api/storage + objectPath\n   378\u2192```\n   379\u2192\n   380\u2192Store `objectPath` in your database. To serve it: `fetch(\\`/api/storage\\${objectPath}\\`)`.\n   381\u2192\n   382\u2192For public assets (not user uploads), use the public-objects path instead:\n   383\u2192\n   384\u2192For protected file uploads requiring user login:\n   385\u2192\n   386\u2192- Use Replit Auth for user authentication (see the `replit-auth` skill)\n   387\u2192- Add the `isAuthenticated` middleware to the storage routes\n   388\u2192- Use ACL policies to control access (see `objectAcl.ts`)\n   389\u2192\n   390\u2192When protected file uploading is requested, both **Replit Auth** and **PostgreSQL** must also be configured, even if not explicitly mentioned. Persistent storage and user authentication are implicitly required for protected file uploading.\n   391\u2192\n   392\u2192If tracking upload metadata (which user uploaded what, file descriptions, etc.), define a Drizzle schema file in `lib/db/src/schema/` and push the schema with `pnpm --filter @workspace/db run push`\n   393\u2192\n   394\u2192## Public Asset Serving\n   395\u2192\n   396\u2192When the user wants to store app/website assets (not user uploads):\n   397\u2192\n   398\u2192- Set up object storage\n   399\u2192- Direct the user to upload files from the Object Storage tool pane\n   400\u2192- Serve assets via `GET /api/storage/public-objects/<file-path>` \u2014 this route searches `PUBLIC_OBJECT_SEARCH_PATHS` and serves files unconditionally with no authentication\n   401\u2192\n   402\u2192## Error Handling\n   403\u2192\n   404\u2192If you encounter errors containing \"App Storage service suspended\" from `setupObjectStorage()` or from object storage operations at runtime:\n   405\u2192\n   406\u21921. Inform the user that their cloud budget has been exceeded\n   407\u21922. Call the `notify_cloud_budget_exceeded` tool with `service_name=\"object_storage\"`\n   408\u2192\n   409\u2192This error handling is ONLY for budget exceeded errors from Object Storage. Do NOT use `notify_cloud_budget_exceeded` for any other errors.\n   410\u2192\n   411\u2192## Important\n   412\u2192\n   413\u2192- Do NOT modify the GCS client setup in `objectStorage.ts` \u2014 it uses Replit sidecar authentication which is auto-configured.\n   414\u2192- Do NOT modify the `objectAcl.ts` ACL framework unless adapting access group types for your use case.\n   415\u2192- Do NOT modify `ObjectUploader.tsx` or `use-upload.ts` \u2014 the Uppy v5 imports and CSS paths are already correct. Do not consult external Uppy docs to \"fix\" them.\n   416\u2192"}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Here's the result of running `cat -n` on a snippet of artifacts/animal-x/src/pages/Reels.jsx\n     1\u2192import React from 'react';\n     2\u2192\n     3\u2192export default function Reels() {\n     4\u2192  return (\n     5\u2192    <div className=\"flex flex-col items-center justify-center h-screen bg-[#0b141a] text-white p-6 text-center\">\n     6\u2192      <div className=\"backdrop-blur-md bg-[#1f2c34]/80 p-10 rounded-3xl border border-emerald-500/20 shadow-2xl max-w-sm m-auto transition-all duration-500 transform hover:scale-105\">\n     7\u2192        \n     8\u2192        {/* Animated Icon */}\n     9\u2192        <div className=\"text-6xl mb-4 animate-bounce duration-1000\">\ud83c\udfac</div>\n    10\u2192        \n    11\u2192        <h2 className=\"text-3xl font-extrabold mb-3 bg-gradient-to-r from-emerald-400 to-teal-300 bg-clip-text text-transparent tracking-wide\">\n    12\u2192          Wildlife Reels\n    13\u2192        </h2>\n    14\u2192        \n    15\u2192        <p className=\"text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-6\">\n    16\u2192          Our standard high-quality short video feed is under routine tuning. \n    17\u2192        </p>\n    18\u2192        \n    19\u2192        {/* Sleek Pulse Badge */}\n    20\u2192        <div className=\"relative inline-flex\">\n    21\u2192          <div className=\"absolute -inset-px bg-gradient-to-r from-emerald-500 to-teal-500 rounded-full blur-sm opacity-70 animate-pulse\"></div>\n    22\u2192          <button className=\"relative px-6 py-2.5 bg-emerald-500 text-[#0b141a] font-bold text-xs uppercase tracking-widest rounded-full shadow-lg\">\n    23\u2192            Coming Soon\n    24\u2192          </button>\n    25\u2192        </div>\n    26\u2192\n    27\u2192      </div>\n    28\u2192    </div>\n    29\u2192  );\n    30\u2192}\n    31\u2192"}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Here's the result of running `cat -n` on a snippet of artifacts/animal-x/src/App.tsx\n     1\u2192import { useState, useEffect, lazy, Suspense, startTransition } from \"react\";\n     2\u2192import { Switch, Route, Router as WouterRouter } from \"wouter\";\n     3\u2192import { QueryClient, QueryClientProvider } from \"@tanstack/react-query\";\n     4\u2192import { AuthProvider } from \"./context/AuthContext\";\n     5\u2192import { SocialProvider } from \"./context/SocialContext\";\n     6\u2192import { ThemeProvider } from \"./context/ThemeContext\";\n     7\u2192import Navbar from \"./components/Navbar\";\n     8\u2192import FirebaseStatusBanner from \"./components/FirebaseStatusBanner\";\n     9\u2192import AutoTickPopup from \"./components/AutoTickPopup\";\n    10\u2192import WildlifeAI from \"./components/WildlifeAI\";\n    11\u2192\n    12\u2192// Lazy load every page \u2014 each becomes its own JS chunk, loaded only when visited\n    13\u2192const Home        = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/Home\"));\n    14\u2192const Animals     = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/Animals\"));\n    15\u2192const AnimalDetail = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/AnimalDetail\"));\n    16\u2192const Map         = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/Map\"));\n    17\u2192const Reels       = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/Reels\"));\n    18\u2192const Travel      = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/Travel\"));\n    19\u2192const Chatbot     = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/Chatbot\"));\n    20\u2192const HelpDesk    = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/HelpDesk\"));\n    21\u2192const Auth        = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/Auth\"));\n    22\u2192const Profile     = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/Profile\"));\n    23\u2192const UserProfile = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/UserProfile\"));\n    24\u2192const Ads         = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/Ads\"));\n    25\u2192const Search      = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/Search\"));\n    26\u2192\n    27\u2192const queryClient = new QueryClient({\n    28\u2192  defaultOptions: {\n    29\u2192    queries: {\n    30\u2192      staleTime: 5 * 60 * 1000,\n    31\u2192      retry: 1,\n    32\u2192      refetchOnWindowFocus: false,\n    33\u2192    },\n    34\u2192  },\n    35\u2192});\n    36\u2192\n    37\u2192function PageFallback() {\n    38\u2192  return <div className=\"page-loading\">Loading</div>;\n    39\u2192}\n    40\u2192\n    41\u2192function NotFound() {\n    42\u2192  return (\n    43\u2192    <div style={{ textAlign: \"center\", padding: \"80px 20px\" }}>\n    44\u2192      <div style={{ fontSize: \"80px\" }}>\ud83d\udd0d</div>\n    45\u2192      <h2 style={{ fontSize: \"24px\", marginTop: \"16px\" }}>Page Not Found</h2>\n    46\u2192      <a href=\"/\" style={{ color: \"#22c55e\", marginTop: \"16px\", display: \"inline-block\" }}>\u2190 Go Home</a>\n    47\u2192    </div>\n    48\u2192  );\n    49\u2192}\n    50\u2192\n    51\u2192function SplashScreen() {\n    52\u2192  return (\n    53\u2192    <div className=\"splash\">\n    54\u2192      <div className=\"splash-inner\">\n    55\u2192        <div className=\"splash-icon\">\ud83d\udc3e</div>\n    56\u2192        <h1 className=\"splash-title\">Animal X</h1>\n    57\u2192        <p className=\"splash-sub\">Wildlife Explorer</p>\n    58\u2192        <div className=\"splash-loader\">\n    59\u2192          <div className=\"splash-dot\" />\n    60\u2192          <div className=\"splash-dot\" />\n    61\u2192          <div className=\"splash-dot\" />\n    62\u2192        </div>\n    63\u2192      </div>\n    64\u2192    </div>\n    65\u2192  );\n    66\u2192}\n    67\u2192\n    68\u2192function Router() {\n    69\u2192  return (\n    70\u2192    <div className=\"app-layout\">\n    71\u2192      <Navbar />\n    72\u2192      <AutoTickPopup />\n    73\u2192      <main className=\"app-main\">\n    74\u2192        <Suspense fallback={<PageFallback />}>\n    75\u2192          <Switch>\n    76\u2192            <Route path=\"/\" component={Home} />\n    77\u2192            <Route path=\"/animals\" component={Animals} />\n    78\u2192            <Route path=\"/animals/:id\" component={AnimalDetail} />\n    79\u2192            <Route path=\"/map\" component={Map} />\n    80\u2192            <Route path=\"/reels\" component={Reels} />\n    81\u2192            <Route path=\"/travel\" component={Travel} />\n    82\u2192            <Route path=\"/chat\" component={Chatbot} />\n    83\u2192            <Route path=\"/help\" component={HelpDesk} />\n    84\u2192            <Route path=\"/auth\" component={Auth} />\n    85\u2192            <Route path=\"/profile\" component={Profile} />\n    86\u2192            <Route path=\"/user/:userId\" component={UserProfile} />\n    87\u2192            <Route path=\"/ads\" component={Ads} />\n    88\u2192            <Route path=\"/search\" component={Search} />\n    89\u2192            <Route path=\"/live-tracking\" component={Map} />\n    90\u2192            <Route component={NotFound} />\n    91\u2192          </Switch>\n    92\u2192        </Suspense>\n    93\u2192      </main>\n    94\u2192      <WildlifeAI />\n    95\u2192      <FirebaseStatusBanner />\n    96\u2192    </div>\n    97\u2192  );\n    98\u2192}\n    99\u2192\n   100\u2192function App() {\n   101\u2192  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);\n   102\u2192\n   103\u2192  useEffect(() => {\n   104\u2192    // Reduced from 1500ms \u2192 400ms splash\n   105\u2192    const timer = setTimeout(() => {\n   106\u2192      startTransition(() => setLoading(false));\n   107\u2192    }, 400);\n   108\u2192    return () => clearTimeout(timer);\n   109\u2192  }, []);\n   110\u2192\n   111\u2192  if (loading) return <SplashScreen />;\n   112\u2192\n   113\u2192  return (\n   114\u2192    <QueryClientProvider client={queryClient}>\n   115\u2192      <ThemeProvider>\n   116\u2192        <AuthProvider>\n   117\u2192          <SocialProvider>\n   118\u2192            <WouterRouter base={import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\\/$/, \"\")}>\n   119\u2192              <Router />\n   120\u2192            </WouterRouter>\n   121\u2192          </SocialProvider>\n   122\u2192        </AuthProvider>\n   123\u2192      </ThemeProvider>\n   124\u2192    </QueryClientProvider>\n   125\u2192  );\n   126\u2192}\n   127\u2192\n   128\u2192export default App;\n   129\u2192"}]}]}
