{"memory_id": 366, "messages": [{"role": "assistant", "content": [], "tool_calls": [{"type": "tool", "name": "read", "arguments": {"file_path": ".agents/memory/MEMORY.md"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Here's the result of running `cat -n` on a snippet of .agents/memory/MEMORY.md\n     1\u2192- [Animal Detail nav bug fix](animal-detail-nav.md) \u2014 use useLayoutEffect([numId]) to reset state + scroll; key prop on QuizSection forces quiz reset\n     2\u2192- [Per-animal quiz system](quiz-system.md) \u2014 NAMED_QUIZZES covers 16 species; generic fallback uses animal's own lifespan/country/habitat for truly unique questions\n     3\u2192- [Back navigation UX](back-nav.md) \u2014 sessionStorage key \"ax_animals_scroll_state\" saves scroll+filters; \"ax_back_from_detail\" signals the restore; cleared after use\n     4\u2192- [WildlifeAI component](wildlife-ai.md) \u2014 floating \ud83e\udd16 FAB (bottom-right, above bottom nav); fully offline local KB; added to App.tsx just before FirebaseStatusBanner\n     5\u2192- [Map upgrades pattern](map-upgrades.md) \u2014 migration routes use React.Fragment (not div) inside LayerGroup; RecenterButton uses useMap() inside MapContainer; user location via watchPosition\n     6\u2192- [Zoos data](zoos-data.md) \u2014 replaced 280 fake \"Wild World N\" zoos with ~118 named real zoos; no more procedural generation loop; export default unchanged\n     7\u2192"}]}]}
{"memory_id": 367, "messages": [{"role": "assistant", "content": [], "tool_calls": [{"type": "tool", "name": "write", "arguments": {"file_path": ".agents/memory/MEMORY.md", "content": "- [Animal Detail nav bug fix](animal-detail-nav.md) \u2014 use useLayoutEffect([numId]) to reset state + scroll; key prop on QuizSection forces quiz reset\n- [Per-animal quiz system](quiz-system.md) \u2014 NAMED_QUIZZES covers 16 species; generic fallback uses animal's own lifespan/country/habitat for truly unique questions\n- [Back navigation UX](back-nav.md) \u2014 sessionStorage key \"ax_animals_scroll_state\" saves scroll+filters; \"ax_back_from_detail\" signals the restore; cleared after use\n- [WildlifeAI component](wildlife-ai.md) \u2014 floating \ud83e\udd16 FAB (bottom-right, above bottom nav); fully offline local KB; added to App.tsx just before FirebaseStatusBanner\n- [Map upgrades pattern](map-upgrades.md) \u2014 migration routes use React.Fragment (not div) inside LayerGroup; RecenterButton uses useMap() inside MapContainer; user location via watchPosition\n- [Zoos data](zoos-data.md) \u2014 replaced 280 fake \"Wild World N\" zoos with ~118 named real zoos; no more procedural generation loop; export default unchanged\n- [RTDB demo-reel write flood](rtdb-demo-write-flood.md) \u2014 trackReelView must guard: skip demo IDs (ff/dr/du/fu prefix) + require user?.uid or 80+ permission_denied logs flood console on every page load.\n- [moderateContent export pattern](moderation-export.md) \u2014 named exports from page files break Vite Fast Refresh; move shared logic (moderation, utils) to dedicated utils/ files.\n- [Profile photo Object Storage fallback](profile-photo-storage.md) \u2014 profile photo upload tries Object Storage presigned URL first, falls back to base64 dataURL; display with /api/storage prefix for path-based URLs.\n"}}, {"type": "tool", "name": "write", "arguments": {"file_path": ".agents/memory/rtdb-demo-write-flood.md", "content": "---\nname: RTDB demo-reel write flood\ndescription: How to prevent 80+ Firebase permission_denied errors flooding the console from trackReelView on demo reels.\n---\n\n## The rule\nIn `trackReelView` (and `likeReelLive`), always add two guards before any RTDB write:\n1. `if (!reelId || !user?.uid) return;` \u2014 never write when unauthenticated\n2. `if (reelId.startsWith(\"ff\") || reelId.startsWith(\"dr\") || reelId.startsWith(\"du\") || reelId.startsWith(\"fu\")) return;` \u2014 skip all demo/fake reel IDs\n\n**Why:** The feed mixes ~80 demo reels (FAKE_FEED_REELS with IDs like `ff0`\u2026`ff79`) with live Firestore reels. IntersectionObserver fires for all of them on initial load. Without the guard, every demo reel triggers an RTDB write to `/live-views/{id}` and `/trending/{id}/score` \u2014 all of which fail with `permission_denied` because RTDB rules require auth, and demo IDs have no real Firebase documents.\n\n**How to apply:** Any new function that writes to RTDB based on a reel ID must apply both guards. Demo reel ID prefixes in demoUsers.js: `ff` (FAKE_FEED_REELS), `dr` (DEMO_REELS), `du` (demo user reels).\n"}}, {"type": "tool", "name": "write", "arguments": {"file_path": ".agents/memory/moderation-export.md", "content": "---\nname: moderateContent export pattern\ndescription: Why named exports from page files break Vite Fast Refresh and the fix pattern.\n---\n\n## The rule\nNever export non-component functions (like `moderateContent`) from React page files. Move shared utilities to `src/utils/` instead.\n\n**Why:** Vite Fast Refresh requires that a file either exports only React components or only non-component exports \u2014 not both. A page file like `Reels.jsx` exports `default function Reels()` (component) + `export function moderateContent()` (utility). This causes `hmr invalidate` with \"incompatible export\" warnings, which trigger full page reloads instead of fast refreshes.\n\n**How to apply:** When a utility function is needed in multiple files, create `src/utils/moderation.js` (or similar) and import from there. The fix: `import { moderateContent } from \"../utils/moderation\"` in both Reels.jsx (can keep it private) and UploadReel.jsx.\n"}}, {"type": "tool", "name": "write", "arguments": {"file_path": ".agents/memory/profile-photo-storage.md", "content": "---\nname: Profile photo Object Storage fallback\ndescription: Pattern for profile photo upload with Object Storage + base64 fallback and URL resolution.\n---\n\n## The rule\nProfile photo (and cover photo) upload should:\n1. Try Object Storage presigned URL first (`POST /api/storage/uploads/request-url` \u2192 `PUT uploadURL`)\n2. Store `objectPath` (e.g. `/profiles/xxx`) in Firestore via `updateProfile({ photo: objectPath })`\n3. Fall back to `fileToDataURL()` (base64) only if the API call fails\n4. When displaying, resolve the stored value with a helper: `path.startsWith(\"data:\") || path.startsWith(\"http\") ? path : \"/api/storage\" + path`\n\n**Why:** Storing base64 in Firestore/localStorage wastes ~133% space and hits Firestore document size limits for large images. Object Storage is the correct long-term solution. The fallback ensures the app still works if the storage API is down.\n\n**How to apply:** Any new image upload feature (cover photo, reel thumbnail, animal photo) should follow this same try/fallback pattern. The `resolveUrl()` helper in Profile.jsx is the canonical implementation.\n"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "File rewritten successfully at: .agents/memory/MEMORY.md"}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "File created successfully at: .agents/memory/rtdb-demo-write-flood.md"}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "File created successfully at: .agents/memory/moderation-export.md"}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "File created successfully at: .agents/memory/profile-photo-storage.md"}]}]}
{"memory_id": 368, "messages": [{"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "All 6 tasks are complete. Here's what was built and fixed in this session:\n\n---\n\n**\ud83c\udfac T001 \u2014 Reels Page (TikTok-style)**\n- Full-screen snap-scroll with IntersectionObserver autoplay\n- Category filter pills (All, Mammals, Birds, Aquatic, Reptiles\u2026)\n- Right-side action buttons: \u2764\ufe0f like, \ud83d\udcac comments, \u2197\ufe0f share, \ud83d\udccc save, \ud83d\udd07 mute\n- Double-tap to like with heart burst animation\n- Creator overlay with avatar, @username, follow button, hashtags, view count\n\n**\ud83d\udcac T002 \u2014 CommentsPanel + UploadReel**\n- CommentsPanel: slide-up from bottom, Firestore realtime, add/delete with timestamps\n- UploadReel: 3-step modal (info \u2192 video file \u2192 review), Object Storage presigned URL upload, AI keyword moderation, strike system in Firestore\n\n**\ud83d\udd0d T003 \u2014 Search + UserProfile**\n- Search: realtime by @username, display name, country, bio \u2014 sorted by followers/reels, category filter pills\n- UserProfile: followers/following tabs with follow buttons, reel grid, blue tick admin controls\n\n**\ud83d\udce2 T004 \u2014 Contacts + Ads**\n- HelpDesk: new email `wildlifeanimalfight@gmail.com`, `@wildlifeanimalfight` on Instagram/Facebook\n- Ads: PayPal button (direct link), Personal/Business toggle, 4-step wizard with PayPal + UPI payment, screenshot upload\n\n**\ud83d\udc64 T005 \u2014 Profile + Admin Panel**\n- Cover photo upload (clickable \ud83d\udcf7 badge, Object Storage with base64 fallback), overlaps avatar\n- Profile photo upgraded to Object Storage\n- Admin panel: \ud83d\udeab Ban/Unban/Strike by UID, \ud83d\udccb Moderation Log with real Firestore + demo entries\n\n**\ud83c\udfa8 T006 \u2014 CSS**\n- ~700 lines of new CSS added: Reels snap scroll, reel cards, heart animation, CommentsPanel slide-up, UploadReel modal, Search page, Ads wizard, HelpDesk tabs, cover image, admin ban panel, toast notifications\n\n**Bug fix:** Stopped 80+ Firebase RTDB `permission_denied` floods \u2014 `trackReelView` now skips demo reel IDs (ff/dr/du/fu prefix) and requires auth before writing."}]}]}
{"memory_id": 369, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "<user_message>\nRead carefully all\nUpgrade and fix the Reels, AI Chatbot, and Profile section. Make everything production-ready.\n\ud83c\udfa5 Reels Page\nFix the upload wizard.\nThe Step 1 \u2192 Step 2 transition is broken. Add a visible Next button that always works.\nAdd Previous, Next, and Upload buttons in the correct steps.\nValidate all required fields before allowing the next step.\nMake the upload flow smooth on both mobile and desktop.\nEnable video sound by default with a mute/unmute button.\nVideos should autoplay when visible and pause when scrolling away.\nImprove loading speed using lazy loading and video preloading.\nFix all upload and playback bugs.\n\ud83e\udd16 Wildlife AI Chatbot\nRebuild the chatbot completely.\nRequirements:\nMake it much smarter with a large local knowledge base.\nAnswer questions about:\nAnimals\nBirds\nReptiles\nMarine life\nZoos\nNational Parks\nWildlife conservation\nAnimal migration\nAnimal behavior\nTravel\nMaps\nReels\nApp features\nHelp & Support\nApp version\nCommunity Guidelines\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms of Service\nUnderstand natural language questions.\nProvide suggested questions.\nGive instant answers.\nSearch the entire app knowledge base.\nDisplay rich cards, images, links, and buttons when helpful.\nImprove the UI to look like a modern ChatGPT-style assistant.\n\ud83e\uddb4 Floating Action Button\nReplace the current danger/tool icon with a buffalo bone icon.\nWhen tapped, open a menu containing:\nWildlife AI\nHelp & Support\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms of Service\nCommunity Guidelines\nContact Us\nApp version\nReport a Problem\nAbout the App\nThe menu should be animated and mobile-friendly.\n\ud83d\udd12 Privacy & Policies\nCreate professional pages for:\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms of Service\nCommunity Guidelines\nCopyright Policy\nWildlife Content Policy\nSafety Policy\nAll pages should be accessible from Profile and the floating menu.\n\ud83d\udc64 Profile\nImprove the profile page:\nBetter UI\nFaster loading\nEdit profile\nChange photo\nFollowers/Following\nReels count\nSaved posts\nSettings\nPrivacy\nNotifications\nHelp Center\n\ud83d\ude80 Performance\nOptimize rendering.\nReduce lag.\nLazy-load heavy components.\nCache images.\nOptimize Firestore queries.\nMake scrolling 60 FPS on mobile.\nRemove memory leaks.\n\u2705 Final Goal\nEverything should work without bugs, be responsive on Android, iPhone, tablet, and desktop, and feel like a professional production-quality wildlife social media app similar to Instagram/TikTok with an intelligent AI assistant.\n\n\n\nRequirements:\n\n1. Hidden Testing Panel only visible to super admin.\n2. Add 3 modes:\n- Testing Mode\n- Public Live Mode\n- Emergency Safe Restore Mode\n\n3. Testing mode should:\n- show beta features only to admin\n- not affect public users\n- use separate local test state\n\n4. Public mode should:\n- instantly enable tested features for all users\n- sync live without app reinstall\n\n5. Emergency mode should:\n- restore last stable backup instantly\n- disable broken features\n- keep user accounts and reels safe\n\n6. Add buttons:\n- Enable Testing\n- Push To Public\n- Emergency Restore\n- Backup ZIP\n- Restore Backup\n\n7. Auto create daily backup of:\n- database\n- reels\n- user profiles\n- settings\n\n8. Add hidden access:\ntap logo 7 times \u2192 open admin testing panel\n\n9. Keep current UI unchanged.\n10. Mobile optimized and super fast.<attached_contents>\n<canvas_viewport_context>\nThe user has not selected any shapes. Canvas overview: 1 focused, 0 blurry, 0 peripheral shapes\nThe user's current view contains 1 shape(s):\n- **iframe** shape (id: artifact:v3:artifacts/animal-x)\n  Position: (1407, -1057), Size: 484x1694\n  URL: https://63328590-7f8f-49cc-8901-5f5ee2f4f50a-00-14lsa885vtmb9.worf.replit.dev/__replco/workspace_iframe.html?initialPath=%2F&id=artifacts%2Fanimal-x\n  Component: Animal X\n\nNote: The shapes above are only what is visible in the user's current viewport. If the user's request is ambiguous about which shape(s) they mean, ask a clarifying question. If the user asks about the entire board or canvas as a whole, use the get_canvas_state tool to retrieve the full canvas state rather than relying on viewport context alone.\n\nUser viewport: (1043, -2327) size 1212x4235\n</canvas_viewport_context>\n\n</attached_contents>\n\n</user_message>\n"}]}]}
{"memory_id": 372, "messages": [{"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "This is a big multi-part upgrade. Let me read the current state of the key files first so I can plan precisely:"}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": [], "tool_calls": [{"type": "tool", "name": "read", "arguments": {"file_path": "artifacts/animal-x/src/pages/Reels.jsx", "limit": 100}}, {"type": "tool", "name": "glob", "arguments": {"pattern": "artifacts/animal-x/src/**/*.jsx"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Here's the result of running `cat -n` on a snippet of artifacts/animal-x/src/pages/Reels.jsx (lines 1-100 of 348)\n     1\u2192import React, { useState, useEffect, useRef, useCallback } from \"react\";\n     2\u2192import { useLocation, Link } from \"wouter\";\n     3\u2192import {\n     4\u2192  collection, query, orderBy, limit, onSnapshot,\n     5\u2192  doc, getDoc, setDoc, updateDoc, increment, serverTimestamp, addDoc, deleteDoc\n     6\u2192} from \"firebase/firestore\";\n     7\u2192import { db } from \"../utils/firebase\";\n     8\u2192import { useAuth } from \"../context/AuthContext\";\n     9\u2192import { useSocial } from \"../context/SocialContext\";\n    10\u2192import { DEMO_REELS, FAKE_FEED_REELS, ALL_USERS } from \"../data/demoUsers\";\n    11\u2192import BlueTick from \"../components/BlueTick\";\n    12\u2192import CommentsPanel from \"../components/CommentsPanel\";\n    13\u2192import UploadReel from \"../components/UploadReel\";\n    14\u2192\n    15\u2192function fmt(n) {\n    16\u2192  if (!n) return \"0\";\n    17\u2192  if (n >= 1000000) return (n / 1000000).toFixed(1) + \"M\";\n    18\u2192  if (n >= 1000) return (n / 1000).toFixed(1) + \"K\";\n    19\u2192  return String(n);\n    20\u2192}\n    21\u2192\n    22\u2192const CATS = [\"All\",\"Mammals\",\"Birds\",\"Aquatic\",\"Reptiles\",\"Small Creatures\",\"Trees\",\"Mountains\",\"Sea\",\"Desert\"];\n    23\u2192\n    24\u2192const WILDLIFE_KW = [\n    25\u2192  \"lion\",\"tiger\",\"elephant\",\"eagle\",\"wolf\",\"dolphin\",\"whale\",\"shark\",\"cheetah\",\"leopard\",\n    26\u2192  \"gorilla\",\"panda\",\"penguin\",\"crocodile\",\"jaguar\",\"orca\",\"falcon\",\"bear\",\"fox\",\"lynx\",\n    27\u2192  \"bison\",\"flamingo\",\"animal\",\"wildlife\",\"nature\",\"forest\",\"jungle\",\"bird\",\"ocean\",\"reptile\",\n    28\u2192  \"snake\",\"fish\",\"reef\",\"coral\",\"turtle\",\"frog\",\"insect\",\"safari\",\"savanna\",\"arctic\",\n    29\u2192  \"mountain\",\"desert\",\"rainforest\",\"conservation\",\"wild\",\"mammal\",\"primate\",\"raptor\",\"marine\",\n    30\u2192];\n    31\u2192\n    32\u2192function moderateContent(title, desc, hashtags) {\n    33\u2192  const text = `${title} ${desc} ${hashtags}`.toLowerCase();\n    34\u2192  return WILDLIFE_KW.some(w => text.includes(w));\n    35\u2192}\n    36\u2192\n    37\u2192function buildFeed(liveReels, catFilter) {\n    38\u2192  const all = [\n    39\u2192    ...liveReels.map(r => ({ ...r, _rank: 2000 + (r.likes || 0) * 0.01 + (Date.now() - (r.createdAt?.toMillis?.() || 0)) * -0.000001 })),\n    40\u2192    ...DEMO_REELS.map(r => ({ ...r, _rank: 800 + (r.likes || 0) * 0.005 })),\n    41\u2192    ...FAKE_FEED_REELS.slice(0, 80).map(r => ({ ...r, _rank: 200 + (r.likes || 0) * 0.001 })),\n    42\u2192  ];\n    43\u2192  const seen = new Set();\n    44\u2192  const deduped = all.filter(r => { if (seen.has(r.id)) return false; seen.add(r.id); return true; });\n    45\u2192  const filtered = catFilter === \"All\" ? deduped : deduped.filter(r => r.category === catFilter || r.cat === catFilter);\n    46\u2192  return filtered.sort((a, b) => b._rank - a._rank);\n    47\u2192}\n    48\u2192\n    49\u2192function getDemoUser(userId) {\n    50\u2192  return ALL_USERS.find(u => u.id === userId || u.username === userId);\n    51\u2192}\n    52\u2192\n    53\u2192export default function Reels() {\n    54\u2192  const [, navigate] = useLocation();\n    55\u2192  const { user, adminMode, isSuperAdmin } = useAuth();\n    56\u2192  const { likedReels, likeReel, following, followUser, unfollowUser, trackReelView } = useSocial();\n    57\u2192\n    58\u2192  const [liveReels, setLiveReels] = useState([]);\n    59\u2192  const [feed, setFeed] = useState([]);\n    60\u2192  const [catFilter, setCatFilter] = useState(\"All\");\n    61\u2192  const [activeIdx, setActiveIdx] = useState(0);\n    62\u2192  const [muted, setMuted] = useState(true);\n    63\u2192  const [commentsReel, setCommentsReel] = useState(null);\n    64\u2192  const [uploadOpen, setUploadOpen] = useState(false);\n    65\u2192  const [heartAnims, setHeartAnims] = useState({});\n    66\u2192  const [savedReels, setSavedReels] = useState(() => {\n    67\u2192    try { return JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(\"ax_saved_reels\") || \"{}\"); } catch { return {}; }\n    68\u2192  });\n    69\u2192  const [liveLikes, setLiveLikes] = useState({});\n    70\u2192  const [doubleTapTimeout, setDoubleTapTimeout] = useState({});\n    71\u2192\n    72\u2192  const scrollRef = useRef(null);\n    73\u2192  const videoRefs = useRef({});\n    74\u2192  const observerRef = useRef(null);\n    75\u2192  const lastTapRef = useRef({});\n    76\u2192\n    77\u2192  useEffect(() => {\n    78\u2192    const q = query(collection(db, \"reels\"), orderBy(\"createdAt\", \"desc\"), limit(100));\n    79\u2192    const unsub = onSnapshot(q, snap => {\n    80\u2192      const reels = snap.docs.map(d => ({ id: d.id, ...d.data(), type: \"live\" }));\n    81\u2192      setLiveReels(reels);\n    82\u2192    }, () => {});\n    83\u2192    return unsub;\n    84\u2192  }, []);\n    85\u2192\n    86\u2192  useEffect(() => {\n    87\u2192    setFeed(buildFeed(liveReels, catFilter));\n    88\u2192    setActiveIdx(0);\n    89\u2192    if (scrollRef.current) scrollRef.current.scrollTo({ top: 0, behavior: \"instant\" });\n    90\u2192  }, [liveReels, catFilter]);\n    91\u2192\n    92\u2192  useEffect(() => {\n    93\u2192    if (!scrollRef.current || feed.length === 0) return;\n    94\u2192    observerRef.current?.disconnect();\n    95\u2192    const obs = new IntersectionObserver(entries => {\n    96\u2192      entries.forEach(entry => {\n    97\u2192        if (entry.isIntersecting && entry.intersectionRatio >= 0.6) {\n    98\u2192          const idx = Number(entry.target.dataset.idx);\n    99\u2192          setActiveIdx(idx);\n   100\u2192          const reel = feed[idx];"}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "./artifacts/animal-x/src/pages/Profile.jsx\n./artifacts/animal-x/src/components/UploadReel.jsx\n./artifacts/animal-x/src/pages/Reels.jsx\n./artifacts/animal-x/src/context/SocialContext.jsx\n./artifacts/animal-x/src/pages/Ads.jsx\n./artifacts/animal-x/src/pages/HelpDesk.jsx\n./artifacts/animal-x/src/pages/Search.jsx\n./artifacts/animal-x/src/components/CommentsPanel.jsx\n./artifacts/animal-x/src/pages/Map.jsx\n./artifacts/animal-x/src/components/WildlifeAI.jsx\n./artifacts/animal-x/src/pages/Animals.jsx\n./artifacts/animal-x/src/pages/AnimalDetail.jsx\n./artifacts/animal-x/src/components/AdminModerationPanel.jsx\n./artifacts/animal-x/src/components/Navbar.jsx\n./artifacts/animal-x/src/components/AutoTickPopup.jsx\n./artifacts/animal-x/src/pages/UserProfile.jsx\n./artifacts/animal-x/src/components/AdminDebugPanel.jsx\n./artifacts/animal-x/src/components/PerformanceBenchmark.jsx\n./artifacts/animal-x/src/components/FirebaseStatusBanner.jsx\n./artifacts/animal-x/src/context/AuthContext.jsx\n./artifacts/animal-x/src/components/NotificationBell.jsx\n./artifacts/animal-x/src/pages/Auth.jsx\n./artifacts/animal-x/src/components/AnimalCard.jsx\n./artifacts/animal-x/src/pages/Home.jsx\n./artifacts/animal-x/src/pages/Travel.jsx\n./artifacts/animal-x/src/components/BlueTick.jsx\n./artifacts/animal-x/src/context/ThemeContext.jsx\n./artifacts/animal-x/src/pages/Chatbot.jsx\n./artifacts/animal-x/src/components/TripBanner.jsx\n./artifacts/animal-x/src/components/CategoryFilter.jsx"}]}]}
{"memory_id": 373, "messages": [{"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Let me read all the key files in parallel to plan the upgrades:"}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": [], "tool_calls": [{"type": "tool", "name": "read", "arguments": {"file_path": "artifacts/animal-x/src/pages/Reels.jsx", "offset": 100, "limit": 250}}, {"type": "tool", "name": "read", "arguments": {"file_path": "artifacts/animal-x/src/components/UploadReel.jsx"}}, {"type": "tool", "name": "read", "arguments": {"file_path": "artifacts/animal-x/src/components/WildlifeAI.jsx"}}, {"type": "tool", "name": "read", "arguments": {"file_path": "artifacts/animal-x/src/pages/Profile.jsx", "limit": 80}}, {"type": "tool", "name": "read", "arguments": {"file_path": "artifacts/animal-x/src/pages/Chatbot.jsx", "limit": 50}}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Here's the result of running `cat -n` on a snippet of artifacts/animal-x/src/pages/Reels.jsx (lines 100-348 of 348)\n   100\u2192          const reel = feed[idx];\n   101\u2192          if (reel?.id) trackReelView(reel.id);\n   102\u2192          Object.entries(videoRefs.current).forEach(([vi, el]) => {\n   103\u2192            if (!el) return;\n   104\u2192            if (Number(vi) === idx) { el.muted = muted; el.play().catch(() => {}); }\n   105\u2192            else { el.pause(); }\n   106\u2192          });\n   107\u2192        }\n   108\u2192      });\n   109\u2192    }, { threshold: 0.6, root: scrollRef.current });\n   110\u2192    const slides = scrollRef.current.querySelectorAll(\"[data-idx]\");\n   111\u2192    slides.forEach(s => obs.observe(s));\n   112\u2192    observerRef.current = obs;\n   113\u2192    return () => obs.disconnect();\n   114\u2192  }, [feed.length, muted]);\n   115\u2192\n   116\u2192  const triggerHeart = useCallback((id) => {\n   117\u2192    setHeartAnims(h => ({ ...h, [id]: true }));\n   118\u2192    setTimeout(() => setHeartAnims(h => ({ ...h, [id]: false })), 800);\n   119\u2192  }, []);\n   120\u2192\n   121\u2192  async function handleLike(reel) {\n   122\u2192    if (!user) { navigate(\"/auth\"); return; }\n   123\u2192    const already = !!likedReels[reel.id];\n   124\u2192    if (!already) triggerHeart(reel.id);\n   125\u2192    setLiveLikes(p => ({ ...p, [reel.id]: (p[reel.id] ?? reel.likes ?? 0) + (already ? -1 : 1) }));\n   126\u2192    await likeReel(reel.id, reel.likes || 0);\n   127\u2192  }\n   128\u2192\n   129\u2192  function handleDoubleTap(reel, e) {\n   130\u2192    const now = Date.now();\n   131\u2192    const last = lastTapRef.current[reel.id] || 0;\n   132\u2192    if (now - last < 350) {\n   133\u2192      if (user && !likedReels[reel.id]) {\n   134\u2192        handleLike(reel);\n   135\u2192      } else if (!user) {\n   136\u2192        triggerHeart(reel.id);\n   137\u2192      }\n   138\u2192    }\n   139\u2192    lastTapRef.current[reel.id] = now;\n   140\u2192  }\n   141\u2192\n   142\u2192  function handleSave(reelId) {\n   143\u2192    const next = { ...savedReels, [reelId]: !savedReels[reelId] };\n   144\u2192    if (!next[reelId]) delete next[reelId];\n   145\u2192    setSavedReels(next);\n   146\u2192    localStorage.setItem(\"ax_saved_reels\", JSON.stringify(next));\n   147\u2192  }\n   148\u2192\n   149\u2192  async function handleShare(reel) {\n   150\u2192    const text = `${reel.title} \u2014 Animal X Wildlife\\n#wildlifeapp`;\n   151\u2192    if (navigator.share) {\n   152\u2192      try { await navigator.share({ title: reel.title, text, url: window.location.href }); return; } catch {}\n   153\u2192    }\n   154\u2192    try { await navigator.clipboard.writeText(text); alert(\"Link copied!\"); } catch {}\n   155\u2192  }\n   156\u2192\n   157\u2192  async function handleDeleteReel(reelId) {\n   158\u2192    if (!window.confirm(\"Delete this reel?\")) return;\n   159\u2192    try { await deleteDoc(doc(db, \"reels\", reelId)); } catch (e) { alert(e.message); }\n   160\u2192  }\n   161\u2192\n   162\u2192  function handleFollowToggle(targetUserId) {\n   163\u2192    if (!user) { navigate(\"/auth\"); return; }\n   164\u2192    if (following[targetUserId]) unfollowUser(targetUserId);\n   165\u2192    else followUser(targetUserId);\n   166\u2192  }\n   167\u2192\n   168\u2192  const currentReel = feed[activeIdx];\n   169\u2192\n   170\u2192  return (\n   171\u2192    <div className=\"reels-page\">\n   172\u2192      <div className=\"reels-top-bar\">\n   173\u2192        <span className=\"reels-top-title\">\ud83c\udfac Wildlife Reels</span>\n   174\u2192        <div className=\"reels-top-actions\">\n   175\u2192          {user && (\n   176\u2192            <button className=\"reels-upload-btn\" onClick={() => setUploadOpen(true)}>\n   177\u2192              \u2795 Upload\n   178\u2192            </button>\n   179\u2192          )}\n   180\u2192        </div>\n   181\u2192      </div>\n   182\u2192\n   183\u2192      <div className=\"reels-cat-bar\">\n   184\u2192        {CATS.map(c => (\n   185\u2192          <button\n   186\u2192            key={c}\n   187\u2192            className={`reel-cat-pill ${catFilter === c ? \"active\" : \"\"}`}\n   188\u2192            onClick={() => setCatFilter(c)}\n   189\u2192          >{c}</button>\n   190\u2192        ))}\n   191\u2192      </div>\n   192\u2192\n   193\u2192      <div className=\"reels-scroll\" ref={scrollRef}>\n   194\u2192        {feed.length === 0 ? (\n   195\u2192          <div className=\"reels-empty\">\n   196\u2192            <div style={{ fontSize: \"4rem\" }}>\ud83e\udd81</div>\n   197\u2192            <h3>No reels yet</h3>\n   198\u2192            <p>Be the first to upload a wildlife reel!</p>\n   199\u2192          </div>\n   200\u2192        ) : (\n   201\u2192          feed.map((reel, idx) => {\n   202\u2192            const liked = !!likedReels[reel.id];\n   203\u2192            const saved = !!savedReels[reel.id];\n   204\u2192            const likes = liveLikes[reel.id] ?? reel.likes ?? 0;\n   205\u2192            const demoUser = getDemoUser(reel.userId);\n   206\u2192            const isOwn = user?.uid === reel.userId;\n   207\u2192            const isAdmin = isSuperAdmin && adminMode;\n   208\u2192            const isFollowed = !!following[reel.userId];\n   209\u2192            const isActive = idx === activeIdx;\n   210\u2192\n   211\u2192            return (\n   212\u2192              <div\n   213\u2192                key={reel.id}\n   214\u2192                className={`reel-item ${isActive ? \"active\" : \"\"}`}\n   215\u2192                data-idx={idx}\n   216\u2192                onClick={(e) => handleDoubleTap(reel, e)}\n   217\u2192              >\n   218\u2192                {reel.videoUrl ? (\n   219\u2192                  <video\n   220\u2192                    ref={el => { if (el) videoRefs.current[idx] = el; }}\n   221\u2192                    className=\"reel-video\"\n   222\u2192                    src={`/api/storage${reel.videoUrl}`}\n   223\u2192                    loop\n   224\u2192                    playsInline\n   225\u2192                    muted={muted}\n   226\u2192                    poster={reel.thumbnailUrl ? `/api/storage${reel.thumbnailUrl}` : undefined}\n   227\u2192                  />\n   228\u2192                ) : (\n   229\u2192                  <div className=\"reel-demo-bg\" style={{ background: reel.bg || \"linear-gradient(135deg,#0f4c2a,#065f46)\" }}>\n   230\u2192                    <div className=\"reel-demo-emoji\">{reel.emoji || \"\ud83d\udc3e\"}</div>\n   231\u2192                  </div>\n   232\u2192                )}\n   233\u2192\n   234\u2192                {heartAnims[reel.id] && (\n   235\u2192                  <div className=\"reel-heart-burst\">\u2764\ufe0f</div>\n   236\u2192                )}\n   237\u2192\n   238\u2192                <div className=\"reel-gradient-overlay\" />\n   239\u2192\n   240\u2192                {reel.sponsored && (\n   241\u2192                  <div className=\"reel-sponsored-tag\">Sponsored</div>\n   242\u2192                )}\n   243\u2192\n   244\u2192                <div className=\"reel-overlay-bottom\">\n   245\u2192                  <div className=\"reel-creator-row\">\n   246\u2192                    <Link href={`/user/${reel.userId}`} onClick={e => e.stopPropagation()}>\n   247\u2192                      <div className=\"reel-avatar\">\n   248\u2192                        {demoUser?.avatar || reel.userAvatar || (reel.username?.[0]?.toUpperCase() || \"\ud83d\udc3e\")}\n   249\u2192                      </div>\n   250\u2192                    </Link>\n   251\u2192                    <div className=\"reel-creator-info\">\n   252\u2192                      <Link href={`/user/${reel.userId}`} onClick={e => e.stopPropagation()} className=\"reel-username-link\">\n   253\u2192                        @{reel.username || \"wildlifeuser\"}\n   254\u2192                        {(reel.userVerified || demoUser?.verified) && <BlueTick size={14} />}\n   255\u2192                      </Link>\n   256\u2192                    </div>\n   257\u2192                    {!isOwn && (\n   258\u2192                      <button\n   259\u2192                        className={`reel-follow-btn ${isFollowed ? \"following\" : \"\"}`}\n   260\u2192                        onClick={e => { e.stopPropagation(); handleFollowToggle(reel.userId); }}\n   261\u2192                      >\n   262\u2192                        {isFollowed ? \"Following\" : \"+ Follow\"}\n   263\u2192                      </button>\n   264\u2192                    )}\n   265\u2192                  </div>\n   266\u2192                  <div className=\"reel-title\">{reel.title}</div>\n   267\u2192                  {reel.desc && <div className=\"reel-desc\">{reel.desc.length > 80 ? reel.desc.slice(0, 80) + \"\u2026\" : reel.desc}</div>}\n   268\u2192                  {reel.hashtags && (\n   269\u2192                    <div className=\"reel-hashtags\">\n   270\u2192                      {String(reel.hashtags).split(/[\\s,]+/).filter(Boolean).slice(0, 4).map(h => (\n   271\u2192                        <span key={h} className=\"reel-hashtag\">{h.startsWith(\"#\") ? h : \"#\" + h}</span>\n   272\u2192                      ))}\n   273\u2192                    </div>\n   274\u2192                  )}\n   275\u2192                  <div className=\"reel-meta-row\">\n   276\u2192                    <span>\ud83d\udc41\ufe0f {fmt(reel.views || 0)}</span>\n   277\u2192                    <span>\ud83d\udd17 {fmt(reel.shares || 0)}</span>\n   278\u2192                    {reel.location && <span>\ud83d\udccd {reel.location}</span>}\n   279\u2192                    <span className=\"reel-cat-badge\">{reel.category || reel.cat}</span>\n   280\u2192                  </div>\n   281\u2192                </div>\n   282\u2192\n   283\u2192                <div className=\"reel-actions-right\">\n   284\u2192                  <div className=\"reel-action-col\">\n   285\u2192                    <button\n   286\u2192                      className={`reel-action-btn like-btn ${liked ? \"liked\" : \"\"}`}\n   287\u2192                      onClick={e => { e.stopPropagation(); handleLike(reel); }}\n   288\u2192                    >\n   289\u2192                      <span className=\"reel-action-icon\">{liked ? \"\u2764\ufe0f\" : \"\ud83e\udd0d\"}</span>\n   290\u2192                      <span className=\"reel-action-count\">{fmt(likes)}</span>\n   291\u2192                    </button>\n   292\u2192                    <button\n   293\u2192                      className=\"reel-action-btn\"\n   294\u2192                      onClick={e => { e.stopPropagation(); setCommentsReel(reel); }}\n   295\u2192                    >\n   296\u2192                      <span className=\"reel-action-icon\">\ud83d\udcac</span>\n   297\u2192                      <span className=\"reel-action-count\">{fmt(reel.comments || 0)}</span>\n   298\u2192                    </button>\n   299\u2192                    <button\n   300\u2192                      className=\"reel-action-btn\"\n   301\u2192                      onClick={e => { e.stopPropagation(); handleShare(reel); }}\n   302\u2192                    >\n   303\u2192                      <span className=\"reel-action-icon\">\u2197\ufe0f</span>\n   304\u2192                      <span className=\"reel-action-count\">{fmt(reel.shares || 0)}</span>\n   305\u2192                    </button>\n   306\u2192                    <button\n   307\u2192                      className={`reel-action-btn ${saved ? \"saved\" : \"\"}`}\n   308\u2192                      onClick={e => { e.stopPropagation(); handleSave(reel.id); }}\n   309\u2192                    >\n   310\u2192                      <span className=\"reel-action-icon\">{saved ? \"\ud83d\udd16\" : \"\ud83d\udccc\"}</span>\n   311\u2192                      <span className=\"reel-action-count\">Save</span>\n   312\u2192                    </button>\n   313\u2192                    {reel.videoUrl && (\n   314\u2192                      <button\n   315\u2192                        className=\"reel-action-btn\"\n   316\u2192                        onClick={e => { e.stopPropagation(); setMuted(m => !m); }}\n   317\u2192                      >\n   318\u2192                        <span className=\"reel-action-icon\">{muted ? \"\ud83d\udd07\" : \"\ud83d\udd0a\"}</span>\n   319\u2192                        <span className=\"reel-action-count\">{muted ? \"Muted\" : \"Sound\"}</span>\n   320\u2192                      </button>\n   321\u2192                    )}\n   322\u2192                    {(isOwn || isAdmin) && (\n   323\u2192                      <button\n   324\u2192                        className=\"reel-action-btn danger-btn\"\n   325\u2192                        onClick={e => { e.stopPropagation(); handleDeleteReel(reel.id); }}\n   326\u2192                      >\n   327\u2192                        <span className=\"reel-action-icon\">\ud83d\uddd1\ufe0f</span>\n   328\u2192                        <span className=\"reel-action-count\">Delete</span>\n   329\u2192                      </button>\n   330\u2192                    )}\n   331\u2192                  </div>\n   332\u2192                </div>\n   333\u2192              </div>\n   334\u2192            );\n   335\u2192          })\n   336\u2192        )}\n   337\u2192      </div>\n   338\u2192\n   339\u2192      {commentsReel && (\n   340\u2192        <CommentsPanel reel={commentsReel} onClose={() => setCommentsReel(null)} />\n   341\u2192      )}\n   342\u2192      {uploadOpen && (\n   343\u2192        <UploadReel onClose={() => setUploadOpen(false)} onUploaded={() => setUploadOpen(false)} />\n   344\u2192      )}\n   345\u2192    </div>\n   346\u2192  );\n   347\u2192}\n   348\u2192"}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Here's the result of running `cat -n` on a snippet of artifacts/animal-x/src/components/UploadReel.jsx\n     1\u2192import { useState, useRef } from \"react\";\n     2\u2192import { collection, addDoc, serverTimestamp, doc, setDoc, increment } from \"firebase/firestore\";\n     3\u2192import { db } from \"../utils/firebase\";\n     4\u2192import { useAuth } from \"../context/AuthContext\";\n     5\u2192import { moderateContent } from \"../utils/moderation\";\n     6\u2192\n     7\u2192const CATEGORIES = [\"Mammals\",\"Birds\",\"Aquatic\",\"Reptiles\",\"Small Creatures\",\"Trees\",\"Mountains\",\"Sea\",\"Desert\"];\n     8\u2192\n     9\u2192const WILDLIFE_KEYWORDS = [\n    10\u2192  \"animal\",\"lion\",\"tiger\",\"elephant\",\"eagle\",\"wolf\",\"dolphin\",\"whale\",\"shark\",\"cheetah\",\n    11\u2192  \"gorilla\",\"panda\",\"penguin\",\"crocodile\",\"leopard\",\"orca\",\"falcon\",\"bear\",\"fox\",\"lynx\",\n    12\u2192  \"wildlife\",\"nature\",\"wild\",\"jungle\",\"forest\",\"ocean\",\"reptile\",\"bird\",\"marine\",\"safari\",\n    13\u2192  \"savanna\",\"arctic\",\"mountain\",\"desert\",\"rainforest\",\"conservation\",\"habitat\",\"species\",\n    14\u2192];\n    15\u2192\n    16\u2192function checkModeration(title, desc, hashtags) {\n    17\u2192  const text = `${title} ${desc} ${hashtags}`.toLowerCase();\n    18\u2192  return WILDLIFE_KEYWORDS.some(w => text.includes(w));\n    19\u2192}\n    20\u2192\n    21\u2192async function getStrikeInfo(uid) {\n    22\u2192  try {\n    23\u2192    const { getDoc } = await import(\"firebase/firestore\");\n    24\u2192    const snap = await getDoc(doc(db, \"userStrikes\", uid));\n    25\u2192    return snap.exists() ? snap.data() : { strikes: 0, banned: false };\n    26\u2192  } catch { return { strikes: 0, banned: false }; }\n    27\u2192}\n    28\u2192\n    29\u2192async function addStrike(uid) {\n    30\u2192  try {\n    31\u2192    const ref = doc(db, \"userStrikes\", uid);\n    32\u2192    const { getDoc, updateDoc, setDoc: setDocFn } = await import(\"firebase/firestore\");\n    33\u2192    const snap = await getDoc(ref);\n    34\u2192    const data = snap.exists() ? snap.data() : { strikes: 0 };\n    35\u2192    const newStrikes = (data.strikes || 0) + 1;\n    36\u2192    const banned = newStrikes >= 3;\n    37\u2192    const banExpiry = banned ? Date.now() + 30 * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000 : null;\n    38\u2192    await setDocFn(ref, { strikes: newStrikes, banned, banExpiry, lastStrike: Date.now() }, { merge: true });\n    39\u2192    return { strikes: newStrikes, banned };\n    40\u2192  } catch { return { strikes: 1, banned: false }; }\n    41\u2192}\n    42\u2192\n    43\u2192export default function UploadReel({ onClose, onUploaded }) {\n    44\u2192  const { user, profile } = useAuth();\n    45\u2192  const [step, setStep] = useState(1); // 1=details, 2=video, 3=review\n    46\u2192  const [form, setForm] = useState({\n    47\u2192    title: \"\", description: \"\", hashtags: \"\", category: \"Mammals\", location: \"\",\n    48\u2192  });\n    49\u2192  const [videoFile, setVideoFile] = useState(null);\n    50\u2192  const [videoPreview, setVideoPreview] = useState(null);\n    51\u2192  const [thumbnailFile, setThumbnailFile] = useState(null);\n    52\u2192  const [uploading, setUploading] = useState(false);\n    53\u2192  const [progress, setProgress] = useState(0);\n    54\u2192  const [error, setError] = useState(null);\n    55\u2192  const [warning, setWarning] = useState(null);\n    56\u2192  const [banned, setBanned] = useState(false);\n    57\u2192  const videoInputRef = useRef(null);\n    58\u2192  const thumbInputRef = useRef(null);\n    59\u2192\n    60\u2192  function handleField(key, val) {\n    61\u2192    setForm(f => ({ ...f, [key]: val }));\n    62\u2192  }\n    63\u2192\n    64\u2192  function handleVideoFile(e) {\n    65\u2192    const f = e.target.files?.[0];\n    66\u2192    if (!f) return;\n    67\u2192    if (f.size > 200 * 1024 * 1024) { setError(\"Video must be under 200 MB.\"); return; }\n    68\u2192    if (!f.type.startsWith(\"video/\")) { setError(\"Please select a video file.\"); return; }\n    69\u2192    setVideoFile(f);\n    70\u2192    setVideoPreview(URL.createObjectURL(f));\n    71\u2192    setError(null);\n    72\u2192  }\n    73\u2192\n    74\u2192  async function uploadToStorage(file, contentType) {\n    75\u2192    const res = await fetch(\"/api/storage/uploads/request-url\", {\n    76\u2192      method: \"POST\",\n    77\u2192      headers: { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" },\n    78\u2192      body: JSON.stringify({ name: file.name, size: file.size, contentType }),\n    79\u2192    });\n    80\u2192    if (!res.ok) throw new Error(\"Failed to get upload URL\");\n    81\u2192    const { uploadURL, objectPath } = await res.json();\n    82\u2192    const uploadRes = await fetch(uploadURL, {\n    83\u2192      method: \"PUT\",\n    84\u2192      headers: { \"Content-Type\": contentType },\n    85\u2192      body: file,\n    86\u2192    });\n    87\u2192    if (!uploadRes.ok) throw new Error(\"Upload failed\");\n    88\u2192    return objectPath;\n    89\u2192  }\n    90\u2192\n    91\u2192  async function handleNext() {\n    92\u2192    if (step === 1) {\n    93\u2192      if (!form.title.trim()) { setError(\"Please enter a title.\"); return; }\n    94\u2192      const isWildlife = checkModeration(form.title, form.description, form.hashtags);\n    95\u2192      if (!isWildlife) {\n    96\u2192        setWarning(\"\u26a0\ufe0f Content Warning: Your title/description doesn't appear to contain wildlife content. Animal X only allows wildlife, nature, and animal-related reels. Please revise or you may receive a strike.\");\n    97\u2192        return;\n    98\u2192      }\n    99\u2192      setWarning(null);\n   100\u2192      setStep(2);\n   101\u2192    } else if (step === 2) {\n   102\u2192      if (!videoFile) { setError(\"Please select a video.\"); return; }\n   103\u2192      setStep(3);\n   104\u2192    }\n   105\u2192  }\n   106\u2192\n   107\u2192  async function handleSubmit() {\n   108\u2192    if (!user) { alert(\"Please login first.\"); return; }\n   109\u2192    setUploading(true);\n   110\u2192    setError(null);\n   111\u2192    setProgress(10);\n   112\u2192    try {\n   113\u2192      const strikeInfo = await getStrikeInfo(user.uid);\n   114\u2192      if (strikeInfo.banned && strikeInfo.banExpiry > Date.now()) {\n   115\u2192        const days = Math.ceil((strikeInfo.banExpiry - Date.now()) / 86400000);\n   116\u2192        setBanned(true);\n   117\u2192        setError(`Your upload access is banned for ${days} more day(s) due to community guideline violations.`);\n   118\u2192        setUploading(false);\n   119\u2192        return;\n   120\u2192      }\n   121\u2192\n   122\u2192      let videoUrl = null;\n   123\u2192      let thumbnailUrl = null;\n   124\u2192\n   125\u2192      setProgress(20);\n   126\u2192      videoUrl = await uploadToStorage(videoFile, videoFile.type);\n   127\u2192      setProgress(70);\n   128\u2192\n   129\u2192      if (thumbnailFile) {\n   130\u2192        thumbnailUrl = await uploadToStorage(thumbnailFile, thumbnailFile.type);\n   131\u2192      }\n   132\u2192      setProgress(85);\n   133\u2192\n   134\u2192      const reelData = {\n   135\u2192        title: form.title.trim(),\n   136\u2192        desc: form.description.trim(),\n   137\u2192        hashtags: form.hashtags.trim(),\n   138\u2192        category: form.category,\n   139\u2192        location: form.location.trim() || null,\n   140\u2192        videoUrl,\n   141\u2192        thumbnailUrl: thumbnailUrl || null,\n   142\u2192        userId: user.uid,\n   143\u2192        username: profile?.username || user.name || user.email?.split(\"@\")[0],\n   144\u2192        userVerified: profile?.manualVerified || false,\n   145\u2192        userAvatar: profile?.avatar || null,\n   146\u2192        likes: 0,\n   147\u2192        views: 0,\n   148\u2192        comments: 0,\n   149\u2192        shares: 0,\n   150\u2192        createdAt: serverTimestamp(),\n   151\u2192        type: \"live\",\n   152\u2192        moderated: true,\n   153\u2192      };\n   154\u2192\n   155\u2192      await addDoc(collection(db, \"reels\"), reelData);\n   156\u2192      await setDoc(doc(db, \"users\", user.uid), { reels: increment(1) }, { merge: true });\n   157\u2192      setProgress(100);\n   158\u2192      onUploaded?.();\n   159\u2192    } catch (e) {\n   160\u2192      setError(\"Upload failed: \" + e.message);\n   161\u2192    }\n   162\u2192    setUploading(false);\n   163\u2192  }\n   164\u2192\n   165\u2192  return (\n   166\u2192    <div className=\"upload-modal-backdrop\" onClick={e => { if (e.target === e.currentTarget) onClose(); }}>\n   167\u2192      <div className=\"upload-modal\">\n   168\u2192        <div className=\"upload-modal-header\">\n   169\u2192          <div className=\"upload-modal-steps\">\n   170\u2192            {[1, 2, 3].map(s => (\n   171\u2192              <div key={s} className={`upload-step ${step === s ? \"active\" : step > s ? \"done\" : \"\"}`}>{s}</div>\n   172\u2192            ))}\n   173\u2192          </div>\n   174\u2192          <div className=\"upload-modal-title\">\n   175\u2192            {step === 1 ? \"\ud83d\udcdd Reel Details\" : step === 2 ? \"\ud83c\udfac Upload Video\" : \"\u2705 Review & Post\"}\n   176\u2192          </div>\n   177\u2192          <button className=\"upload-modal-close\" onClick={onClose}>\u2715</button>\n   178\u2192        </div>\n   179\u2192\n   180\u2192        {banned && (\n   181\u2192          <div className=\"upload-banned-msg\">\n   182\u2192            \ud83d\udeab Upload access banned. Please contact support.\n   183\u2192          </div>\n   184\u2192        )}\n   185\u2192\n   186\u2192        {error && <div className=\"upload-error\">{error}</div>}\n   187\u2192        {warning && (\n   188\u2192          <div className=\"upload-warning\">\n   189\u2192            {warning}\n   190\u2192            <div style={{ display: \"flex\", gap: 8, marginTop: 10 }}>\n   191\u2192              <button className=\"upload-warning-revise\" onClick={() => setWarning(null)}>\u270f\ufe0f Revise</button>\n   192\u2192              <button className=\"upload-warning-proceed\" onClick={async () => {\n   193\u2192                const { strikes } = await addStrike(user.uid);\n   194\u2192                setWarning(null);\n   195\u2192                if (strikes >= 3) { setBanned(true); setError(\"Upload access banned due to repeat violations.\"); }\n   196\u2192                else { alert(`\u26a0\ufe0f Strike ${strikes}/3 added. ${3 - strikes} violation(s) remaining before 30-day ban.`); }\n   197\u2192              }}>Post Anyway (Risk Strike)</button>\n   198\u2192            </div>\n   199\u2192          </div>\n   200\u2192        )}\n   201\u2192\n   202\u2192        {!warning && !banned && (\n   203\u2192          <>\n   204\u2192            {step === 1 && (\n   205\u2192              <div className=\"upload-form\">\n   206\u2192                <label className=\"upload-label\">Title *</label>\n   207\u2192                <input\n   208\u2192                  className=\"upload-input\"\n   209\u2192                  value={form.title}\n   210\u2192                  onChange={e => handleField(\"title\", e.target.value)}\n   211\u2192                  placeholder=\"e.g. Lion Pride at Dusk \ud83e\udd81\"\n   212\u2192                  maxLength={100}\n   213\u2192                />\n   214\u2192                <label className=\"upload-label\">Description</label>\n   215\u2192                <textarea\n   216\u2192                  className=\"upload-textarea\"\n   217\u2192                  value={form.description}\n   218\u2192                  onChange={e => handleField(\"description\", e.target.value)}\n   219\u2192                  placeholder=\"Describe your wildlife footage\u2026\"\n   220\u2192                  maxLength={500}\n   221\u2192                  rows={3}\n   222\u2192                />\n   223\u2192                <label className=\"upload-label\">Hashtags</label>\n   224\u2192                <input\n   225\u2192                  className=\"upload-input\"\n   226\u2192                  value={form.hashtags}\n   227\u2192                  onChange={e => handleField(\"hashtags\", e.target.value)}\n   228\u2192                  placeholder=\"#wildlife #lion #nature\"\n   229\u2192                />\n   230\u2192                <label className=\"upload-label\">Category</label>\n   231\u2192                <select\n   232\u2192                  className=\"upload-select\"\n   233\u2192                  value={form.category}\n   234\u2192                  onChange={e => handleField(\"category\", e.target.value)}\n   235\u2192                >\n   236\u2192                  {CATEGORIES.map(c => <option key={c}>{c}</option>)}\n   237\u2192                </select>\n   238\u2192                <label className=\"upload-label\">Location (optional)</label>\n   239\u2192                <input\n   240\u2192                  className=\"upload-input\"\n   241\u2192                  value={form.location}\n   242\u2192                  onChange={e => handleField(\"location\", e.target.value)}\n   243\u2192                  placeholder=\"e.g. Maasai Mara, Kenya\"\n   244\u2192                />\n   245\u2192                <div className=\"upload-moderation-note\">\n   246\u2192                  \ud83e\udd16 AI Moderation: Only wildlife, nature & animal content allowed.\n   247\u2192                </div>\n   248\u2192              </div>\n   249\u2192            )}\n   250\u2192\n   251\u2192            {step === 2 && (\n   252\u2192              <div className=\"upload-video-step\">\n   253\u2192                <div\n   254\u2192                  className=\"upload-drop-zone\"\n   255\u2192                  onClick={() => videoInputRef.current?.click()}\n   256\u2192                >\n   257\u2192                  {videoPreview ? (\n   258\u2192                    <video src={videoPreview} className=\"upload-preview-video\" muted playsInline />\n   259\u2192                  ) : (\n   260\u2192                    <>\n   261\u2192                      <div style={{ fontSize: \"4rem\" }}>\ud83c\udfac</div>\n   262\u2192                      <div className=\"upload-drop-text\">Tap to select video</div>\n   263\u2192                      <div className=\"upload-drop-hint\">MP4, MOV, WebM \u00b7 Max 200 MB</div>\n   264\u2192                    </>\n   265\u2192                  )}\n   266\u2192                </div>\n   267\u2192                <input\n   268\u2192                  ref={videoInputRef}\n   269\u2192                  type=\"file\"\n   270\u2192                  accept=\"video/*\"\n   271\u2192                  style={{ display: \"none\" }}\n   272\u2192                  onChange={handleVideoFile}\n   273\u2192                />\n   274\u2192                {videoFile && (\n   275\u2192                  <div className=\"upload-file-info\">\n   276\u2192                    \u2705 {videoFile.name} ({(videoFile.size / 1024 / 1024).toFixed(1)} MB)\n   277\u2192                  </div>\n   278\u2192                )}\n   279\u2192                <div className=\"upload-thumb-row\">\n   280\u2192                  <label className=\"upload-label\">Custom Thumbnail (optional)</label>\n   281\u2192                  <button className=\"upload-thumb-btn\" onClick={() => thumbInputRef.current?.click()}>\n   282\u2192                    {thumbnailFile ? \"\u2705 \" + thumbnailFile.name : \"\ud83d\udcf7 Choose thumbnail\"}\n   283\u2192                  </button>\n   284\u2192                  <input\n   285\u2192                    ref={thumbInputRef}\n   286\u2192                    type=\"file\"\n   287\u2192                    accept=\"image/*\"\n   288\u2192                    style={{ display: \"none\" }}\n   289\u2192                    onChange={e => setThumbnailFile(e.target.files?.[0] || null)}\n   290\u2192                  />\n   291\u2192                </div>\n   292\u2192              </div>\n   293\u2192            )}\n   294\u2192\n   295\u2192            {step === 3 && (\n   296\u2192              <div className=\"upload-review-step\">\n   297\u2192                <div className=\"upload-review-card\">\n   298\u2192                  <div className=\"upload-review-emoji\">\ud83c\udfac</div>\n   299\u2192                  <div className=\"upload-review-details\">\n   300\u2192                    <div className=\"upload-review-title\">{form.title}</div>\n   301\u2192                    <div className=\"upload-review-cat\">{form.category}{form.location ? \" \u00b7 \" + form.location : \"\"}</div>\n   302\u2192                    {form.hashtags && <div className=\"upload-review-tags\">{form.hashtags}</div>}\n   303\u2192                    <div className=\"upload-review-file\">{videoFile?.name}</div>\n   304\u2192                  </div>\n   305\u2192                </div>\n   306\u2192                <div className=\"upload-guidelines\">\n   307\u2192                  <div className=\"upload-guidelines-title\">\ud83d\udccb Community Guidelines</div>\n   308\u2192                  <ul>\n   309\u2192                    <li>\u2705 Wildlife, nature, animals, oceans, forests</li>\n   310\u2192                    <li>\u274c No unrelated content (gets rejected + strike)</li>\n   311\u2192                    <li>\u274c No violence, abuse, or harmful content</li>\n   312\u2192                    <li>3 strikes = 30-day upload ban</li>\n   313\u2192                  </ul>\n   314\u2192                </div>\n   315\u2192                {uploading && (\n   316\u2192                  <div className=\"upload-progress-wrap\">\n   317\u2192                    <div className=\"upload-progress-bar\" style={{ width: `${progress}%` }} />\n   318\u2192                    <div className=\"upload-progress-text\">Uploading\u2026 {progress}%</div>\n   319\u2192                  </div>\n   320\u2192                )}\n   321\u2192              </div>\n   322\u2192            )}\n   323\u2192\n   324\u2192            <div className=\"upload-modal-footer\">\n   325\u2192              {step > 1 && !uploading && (\n   326\u2192                <button className=\"upload-back-btn\" onClick={() => setStep(s => s - 1)}>\u2190 Back</button>\n   327\u2192              )}\n   328\u2192              {step < 3 ? (\n   329\u2192                <button className=\"upload-next-btn\" onClick={handleNext}>\n   330\u2192                  {step === 2 ? \"Review \u2192\" : \"Next \u2192\"}\n   331\u2192                </button>\n   332\u2192              ) : (\n   333\u2192                <button\n   334\u2192                  className=\"upload-post-btn\"\n   335\u2192                  onClick={handleSubmit}\n   336\u2192                  disabled={uploading}\n   337\u2192                >\n   338\u2192                  {uploading ? \"Posting\u2026\" : \"\ud83d\ude80 Post Reel\"}\n   339\u2192                </button>\n   340\u2192              )}\n   341\u2192            </div>\n   342\u2192          </>\n   343\u2192        )}\n   344\u2192      </div>\n   345\u2192    </div>\n   346\u2192  );\n   347\u2192}\n   348\u2192"}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Here's the result of running `cat -n` on a snippet of artifacts/animal-x/src/components/WildlifeAI.jsx\n     1\u2192import { useState, useRef, useEffect, useCallback } from \"react\";\n     2\u2192import animals from \"../data/animals\";\n     3\u2192\n     4\u2192/* \u2500\u2500\u2500 Local Knowledge Base \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500 */\n     5\u2192const KB = [\n     6\u2192  // App Navigation\n     7\u2192  { p: /^(hi|hello|hey|helo|hii|howdy)/i, a: \"\ud83d\udc4b Hey there! I'm your Wildlife AI assistant. Ask me anything about animals, the app features, maps, zoos, or conservation! \ud83e\udd81\" },\n     8\u2192  { p: /upload.*reel|reel.*upload|post.*video|how.*reel|video.*upload/i, a: \"\ud83d\udcf9 **Upload a Reel:**\\n1. Go to \ud83c\udfac Reels tab\\n2. Tap **\u2795 Upload**\\n3. Choose your wildlife video\\n4. Add a caption with animal/nature keywords\\n5. Tap Post!\\n\\n\u26a0\ufe0f Only animal & nature content is allowed. 3 strikes = upload ban.\" },\n     9\u2192  { p: /upload.*post|new post|post.*image|share.*photo/i, a: \"\ud83d\udcf8 **Upload a Post:**\\n1. Go to \ud83c\udfac Reels \u2192 Posts tab\\n2. Tap **\u2795 New Post**\\n3. Choose photo or video\\n4. Add a wildlife caption\\n5. Done! Your post appears in the feed instantly.\" },\n    10\u2192  { p: /story|stories|add story/i, a: \"\ud83d\udd34 **Stories** expire after 24 hours automatically.\\n1. Go to \ud83c\udfac Reels \u2192 Stories tab\\n2. Tap **\u2795 Add Story**\\n3. Choose a photo or video\\n4. It vanishes in 24h!\\n\\nYou can delete your own story anytime.\" },\n    11\u2192  { p: /follow|following|unfollow/i, a: \"\ud83d\udc65 **Follow system:**\\n\u2022 Tap **+ Follow** on any creator's profile or reel\\n\u2022 Tap again to **Unfollow**\\n\u2022 Go to \ud83d\udc65 Search to discover 200+ wildlife creators\\n\u2022 Your following count updates instantly and persists across sessions.\" },\n    12\u2192  { p: /like|heart|double.*tap|tap.*twice/i, a: \"\u2764\ufe0f **Liking Reels:**\\n\u2022 Tap \u2764\ufe0f on the right sidebar of any reel\\n\u2022 Double-tap anywhere on the reel for a quick like\\n\u2022 Like counts sync to Firebase \u2014 they persist forever!\" },\n    13\u2192  { p: /search.*user|find.*user|find.*creator|user.*search/i, a: \"\ud83d\udd0d **Find Creators:**\\n1. Tap the **\ud83d\udc65 icon** in the top navigation\\n2. Or go to **/search** page\\n3. Search by @username, display name, or country\\n4. Results appear in real-time as you type\\n5. Tap any card to open their profile \u2192 Reels \u00b7 Followers \u00b7 Following tabs\" },\n    14\u2192  { p: /forgot.*password|reset.*password|password.*reset/i, a: \"\ud83d\udd11 **Reset Password:**\\n1. Go to \ud83d\udd11 Login page\\n2. Tap **Forgot Password?**\\n3. Enter your email address\\n4. Check your inbox for a reset link\\n5. Click the link and set a new password\\n\\nContact: animalx00003@gmail.com if you need further help.\" },\n    15\u2192  { p: /sign.?up|register|create.*account|new account/i, a: \"\ud83d\udcdd **Create Account:**\\n1. Go to \ud83d\udc64 Profile \u2192 Login\\n2. Tap **Sign Up**\\n3. Enter your name, email & password (6+ chars)\\n4. Tap **Create Account**\\n\\nAll features are free \u2014 no premium required!\" },\n    16\u2192  { p: /login|sign.?in|log.*in/i, a: \"\ud83d\udd11 **Login:**\\n1. Go to \ud83d\udc64 Profile\\n2. Enter email + password\\n3. Tap **Login**\\n\\nForgot password? Tap 'Forgot Password' on the login page.\" },\n    17\u2192  { p: /notification|bell|alerts/i, a: \"\ud83d\udd14 **Notifications:**\\n\u2022 Tap the \ud83d\udd14 bell icon in the top bar\\n\u2022 Get notified when someone follows you\\n\u2022 Unread count shows as a badge\\n\u2022 Tap 'Mark all as read' to clear\\n\u2022 Notifications sync in real-time via Firebase.\" },\n    18\u2192  { p: /ad|advertise|advertisement|run.*ad|ad.*wizard/i, a: \"\ud83d\udce2 **Run an Advertisement:**\\n1. Go to \u2139\ufe0f Help Desk\\n2. Tap **Run Advertisement** button\\n3. Step 1: Ad details (title, description, target URL)\\n4. Step 2: Target animal categories\\n5. Step 3: Choose plan (\u20b9149\u2013\u20b94,999)\\n6. Step 4: Pay via UPI: **nakumamit27-1@okicici**\\n\\nAds reviewed by admin before going live.\" },\n    19\u2192  { p: /blue.*tick|verified|verification|tick/i, a: \"\ud83d\udd35 **Blue Tick Verification:**\\n\u2022 **Auto:** Reach 100,000 followers \u2014 blue tick granted automatically with a congratulations popup!\\n\u2022 **Manual:** Admin can grant to any user from the moderation panel\\n\u2022 Blue ticks appear on your profile, reels, and in search results\" },\n    20\u2192  { p: /profile|edit.*profile|my.*profile/i, a: \"\ud83d\udc64 **Your Profile:**\\n\u2022 Go to \ud83d\udc64 Profile in the bottom nav\\n\u2022 Edit name, bio, country\\n\u2022 View your posts, reels, followers, following\\n\u2022 Tap any user's profile to follow them\\n\u2022 Profile photo can be updated (photo upload feature)\" },\n    21\u2192  { p: /community.*guideline|rules|guidelines/i, a: \"\ud83d\udccb **Community Guidelines:**\\n\u2022 Only wildlife, nature & animal content\\n\u2022 No hate speech, violence, or spam\\n\u2022 No copyrighted music without permission\\n\u2022 Report violations using the \u22ee menu on any reel/post\\n\u2022 3 violations = 30-day upload ban\\n\u2022 Permanent ban for severe violations\\n\\nFull guidelines: Help Desk \u2192 Community Guidelines tab\" },\n    22\u2192  { p: /report|report.*reel|report.*user/i, a: \"\ud83d\udea9 **Report Content:**\\n1. Tap \u22ee (three dots) on any reel or post\\n2. Select 'Report'\\n3. Choose violation type\\n4. Submit \u2014 admin reviews within 24h\\n\\nSerious violations are acted upon immediately.\" },\n    23\u2192  { p: /privacy|privacy.*policy/i, a: \"\ud83d\udd12 **Privacy Policy:**\\nYour data is stored securely in Firebase. We collect:\\n\u2022 Email (login only)\\n\u2022 Content you upload\\n\u2022 Follow/like data\\n\\nWe never sell your data. Full policy: Help Desk \u2192 Privacy Policy tab\" },\n    24\u2192  { p: /terms|terms.*condition/i, a: \"\ud83d\udcc4 **Terms & Conditions:**\\nYou must be 13+ to use Animal X. Uploading non-wildlife content is a violation. Admin retains the right to remove content. Full terms: Help Desk \u2192 Terms & Conditions tab\" },\n    25\u2192  { p: /contact|support|help.*desk|email.*us/i, a: \"\ud83d\udcde **Contact Support:**\\n\ud83d\udce7 Email: animalx00003@gmail.com\\n\ud83d\udcf8 Instagram: @wild_life_aniaml_fight\\n\u25b6\ufe0f YouTube: wild_life_aniaml_fight\\n\ud83d\udc65 Facebook: wild_life_aniaml_fight\\n\\nOr visit the Help Desk page in the app for FAQ & live support.\" },\n    26\u2192  { p: /map|zoo.*map|live.*track|gps|tracking/i, a: \"\ud83d\uddfa\ufe0f **Map Features:**\\n\u2022 **Zoo Layer** \ud83c\udfdb\ufe0f \u2014 300+ real zoos worldwide with ratings, animal count & Google Maps links\\n\u2022 **Live Tracking** \ud83e\udd81 \u2014 50+ GPS-tracked wild animals with status, species & last location\\n\u2022 **Migration Layer** \u2014 seasonal wildlife migration routes\\n\u2022 **My Location** \ud83d\udccd \u2014 shows your GPS position with a blue animated marker\\n\u2022 Search by animal name, zoo name, or country\\n\u2022 Toggle layers on/off independently\" },\n    27\u2192  { p: /travel|uber|ola|lyft|flight|booking/i, a: \"\u2708\ufe0f **Travel Section:**\\nDeep links to:\\n\u2022 \ud83d\ude97 Ride booking: Uber, Ola, Lyft, Bolt, Grab\\n\u2022 \u2708\ufe0f Flights: Skyscanner, Google Flights, Kayak\\n\u2022 \ud83d\udee9\ufe0f Private: VistaJet\\n\\nPlan your wildlife safari trip directly from the app!\" },\n    28\u2192  { p: /admin|super.*admin|broadcast|admin.*mode/i, a: \"\ud83d\udc51 **Admin System (admin only):**\\n\u2022 Login as malinotaling8@gmail.com\\n\u2022 Tap the \ud83e\udd81 logo 7 times to open the broadcast panel\\n\u2022 Send messages to all users\\n\u2022 Manage animal photos, abilities & quizzes\\n\u2022 Grant/remove blue ticks\\n\u2022 View content violations & ban users\" },\n    29\u2192  { p: /chatbot|chat|ai|assistant/i, a: \"\ud83e\udd16 I'm the Wildlife AI! I can answer questions about:\\n\u2022 Any animal in the app (1,213+ species)\\n\u2022 How to use every feature\\n\u2022 Wildlife facts & conservation\\n\u2022 Maps, zoos, tracking\\n\u2022 Profile, reels, ads\\n\\nJust ask me anything!\" },\n    30\u2192\n    31\u2192  // Wildlife general\n    32\u2192  { p: /biggest|largest.*animal|largest.*creature/i, a: \"\ud83d\udccf **Record Holders:**\\n\ud83d\udc0b Largest ever: Blue Whale (30 m, 200 tons)\\n\ud83d\udc18 Largest land: African Elephant (6,000 kg)\\n\ud83e\udd92 Tallest: Giraffe (5.8 m)\\n\ud83e\udd88 Largest fish: Whale Shark (12 m)\\n\ud83e\udd85 Largest wingspan: Wandering Albatross (3.5 m)\\n\ud83d\udc26 Largest bird: Ostrich (2.7 m, 156 kg)\" },\n    33\u2192  { p: /fastest|speed.*animal/i, a: \"\ud83c\udfc3 **Speed Records:**\\n\ud83d\udc06 Fastest land: Cheetah (112 km/h)\\n\ud83e\udd85 Fastest dive: Peregrine Falcon (389 km/h)\\n\ud83d\udc20 Fastest fish: Sailfish (110 km/h)\\n\ud83d\udc2c Fastest marine mammal: Orca (55 km/h)\\n\ud83e\udd8b Monarch Butterfly migrates 4,800 km!\" },\n    34\u2192  { p: /endangered|extinction|conservation|protect/i, a: \"\ud83c\udf0d **Conservation Crisis:**\\n\u2022 1 million+ species face extinction\\n\u2022 Main causes: habitat loss, climate change, poaching\\n\u2022 Key programs: WWF, IUCN Red List, CITES\\n\u2022 Critically endangered: Amur Leopard, Vaquita, Javan Rhino\\n\u2022 Success stories: Arabian Oryx, California Condor, Giant Panda\" },\n    35\u2192  { p: /migration/i, a: \"\ud83e\udd8b **Wildlife Migration:**\\n\u2022 Wildebeest: 3,000 km Serengeti circle\\n\u2022 Arctic Tern: 70,000 km pole-to-pole\\n\u2022 Monarch Butterfly: 4,800 km N. America\\n\u2022 Humpback Whale: 20,000 km tropical/polar\\n\u2022 Gray Whale: longest mammal migration \u2014 20,000 km\\n\u2022 Caribou: 5,000 km Arctic migration\\n\\nSee the Migration layer on the Map page!\" },\n    36\u2192  { p: /how.*many.*species|species.*count|animals.*earth/i, a: \"\ud83d\udd2c **Species on Earth:**\\n\u2022 Estimated total: 8.7 million species\\n\u2022 Formally described: ~1.2 million\\n\u2022 New discoveries: ~18,000/year\\n\u2022 In Animal X: 1,213+ species & natural wonders\\n\u2022 Most diverse: Tropical rainforests & coral reefs\" },\n    37\u2192];\n    38\u2192\n    39\u2192/* Suggested questions shown on open */\n    40\u2192const SUGGESTED = [\n    41\u2192  \"Tell me about Lions\",\n    42\u2192  \"How do I upload a reel?\",\n    43\u2192  \"How does Live Tracking work?\",\n    44\u2192  \"How do I follow users?\",\n    45\u2192  \"What are Community Guidelines?\",\n    46\u2192  \"How does the Blue Tick work?\",\n    47\u2192  \"Where can I find Tigers?\",\n    48\u2192  \"How do ads work?\",\n    49\u2192  \"How do I reset my password?\",\n    50\u2192  \"How do I report a reel?\",\n    51\u2192];\n    52\u2192\n    53\u2192/* \u2500\u2500\u2500 Match query against knowledge base + animal database \u2500\u2500\u2500 */\n    54\u2192function getAIAnswer(query) {\n    55\u2192  const q = query.trim();\n    56\u2192  if (!q) return null;\n    57\u2192\n    58\u2192  // 1. Check knowledge base (regex patterns)\n    59\u2192  for (const entry of KB) {\n    60\u2192    if (entry.p.test(q)) return entry.a;\n    61\u2192  }\n    62\u2192\n    63\u2192  // 2. Check if asking about a specific animal\n    64\u2192  const qLow = q.toLowerCase();\n    65\u2192  const animalMatch = animals.find(a =>\n    66\u2192    qLow.includes(a.name.toLowerCase()) ||\n    67\u2192    (a.baseName && qLow.includes(a.baseName.toLowerCase()))\n    68\u2192  );\n    69\u2192  if (animalMatch) {\n    70\u2192    const a = animalMatch;\n    71\u2192    return `**${a.name}** ${a.category === \"Mammals\" ? \"\ud83e\udd81\" : a.category === \"Birds\" ? \"\ud83e\udd85\" : a.category === \"Aquatic\" ? \"\ud83d\udc2c\" : a.category === \"Reptiles\" ? \"\ud83d\udc0d\" : \"\ud83c\udf3f\"}\\n\\n` +\n    72\u2192      `\ud83c\udfe0 **Habitat:** ${a.habitat || \"Various\"}\\n` +\n    73\u2192      `\ud83c\udf7d\ufe0f **Diet:** ${a.diet || \"Unknown\"}\\n` +\n    74\u2192      `\ud83c\udf0d **Found in:** ${a.country || \"Various regions\"}\\n` +\n    75\u2192      `\u23f3 **Lifespan:** ${a.lifespan || \"Unknown\"}\\n` +\n    76\u2192      `\ud83c\udff7\ufe0f **Category:** ${a.category}\\n` +\n    77\u2192      (a.description ? `\\n\ud83d\udcdd ${a.description.slice(0, 200)}\u2026` : \"\") +\n    78\u2192      `\\n\\n\ud83d\udd0d Open the **Animals** page and search for \"${a.name}\" to see full details, special ability & quiz!`;\n    79\u2192  }\n    80\u2192\n    81\u2192  // 3. Keyword fallback\n    82\u2192  if (/zoo|zoos/i.test(q)) return \"\ud83c\udfdb\ufe0f **Zoos:** Animal X features 300+ real zoos worldwide on the Map page. Each zoo shows its official name, city, country, rating, and a 'Open in Maps' button for Google Maps navigation!\";\n    83\u2192  if (/reel/i.test(q)) return \"\ud83c\udfac The **Reels** page has an Instagram-style 9:16 scroll feed with 126+ wildlife reels. You can upload your own wildlife videos, like reels (double-tap!), follow creators, and delete your own reels.\";\n    84\u2192  if (/map/i.test(q)) return \"\ud83d\uddfa\ufe0f The **Map** page shows 300+ zoos + 50+ live-tracked animals + wildlife migration routes + your live GPS location. Toggle layers, search by name/country, and tap any marker for details!\";\n    85\u2192  if (/feature|what.*can|what.*do/i.test(q)) return \"\ud83d\udc3e **Animal X Features:**\\n\u2022 \ud83d\udc3e 1,213+ animals with quizzes & special abilities\\n\u2022 \ud83c\udfac Instagram-style wildlife reels\\n\u2022 \ud83d\uddfa\ufe0f 300+ zoo map + live animal tracking\\n\u2022 \ud83d\udc65 200+ wildlife creators to follow\\n\u2022 \ud83d\udcf8 Posts & 24h Stories\\n\u2022 \u2708\ufe0f Safari travel booking\\n\u2022 \ud83e\udd16 AI chatbot (that's me!)\\n\u2022 \ud83d\udd35 Blue tick verification system\\nAll features are **FREE!**\";\n    86\u2192\n    87\u2192  return null;\n    88\u2192}\n    89\u2192\n    90\u2192/* \u2500\u2500\u2500 Render markdown-ish text \u2500\u2500\u2500 */\n    91\u2192function FormattedMessage({ text }) {\n    92\u2192  const lines = text.split(\"\\n\");\n    93\u2192  return (\n    94\u2192    <div className=\"ai-msg-content\">\n    95\u2192      {lines.map((line, i) => {\n    96\u2192        if (!line.trim()) return <br key={i} />;\n    97\u2192        // Bold **text**\n    98\u2192        const parts = line.split(/\\*\\*(.*?)\\*\\*/g);\n    99\u2192        return (\n   100\u2192          <div key={i} className={line.startsWith(\"\u2022\") || line.startsWith(\"-\") ? \"ai-bullet\" : \"\"}>\n   101\u2192            {parts.map((p, j) => j % 2 === 1 ? <strong key={j}>{p}</strong> : p)}\n   102\u2192          </div>\n   103\u2192        );\n   104\u2192      })}\n   105\u2192    </div>\n   106\u2192  );\n   107\u2192}\n   108\u2192\n   109\u2192/* \u2500\u2500\u2500 Main Component \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500 */\n   110\u2192export default function WildlifeAI() {\n   111\u2192  const [open, setOpen] = useState(false);\n   112\u2192  const [messages, setMessages] = useState([\n   113\u2192    { role: \"ai\", text: \"\ud83d\udc4b Hi! I'm your **Wildlife AI** \ud83e\udd81\\n\\nAsk me about any animal, app features, maps, zoos, or wildlife conservation.\\n\\nI answer instantly from my local knowledge base \u2014 no internet needed for most questions!\" }\n   114\u2192  ]);\n   115\u2192  const [input, setInput] = useState(\"\");\n   116\u2192  const [typing, setTyping] = useState(false);\n   117\u2192  const [searchQuery, setSearchQuery] = useState(\"\");\n   118\u2192  const messagesEndRef = useRef(null);\n   119\u2192  const inputRef = useRef(null);\n   120\u2192\n   121\u2192  useEffect(() => {\n   122\u2192    if (open) {\n   123\u2192      messagesEndRef.current?.scrollIntoView({ behavior: \"smooth\" });\n   124\u2192      setTimeout(() => inputRef.current?.focus(), 100);\n   125\u2192    }\n   126\u2192  }, [open, messages]);\n   127\u2192\n   128\u2192  const sendMessage = useCallback(async (text) => {\n   129\u2192    const q = (text || input).trim();\n   130\u2192    if (!q) return;\n   131\u2192    setInput(\"\");\n   132\u2192\n   133\u2192    const userMsg = { role: \"user\", text: q };\n   134\u2192    setMessages(prev => [...prev, userMsg]);\n   135\u2192    setTyping(true);\n   136\u2192\n   137\u2192    // Simulate thinking delay for natural feel\n   138\u2192    await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, q.length > 30 ? 600 : 350));\n   139\u2192\n   140\u2192    const answer = getAIAnswer(q);\n   141\u2192    const aiText = answer || `\ud83d\udd0d I couldn't find specific information about \"${q.slice(0, 30)}${q.length > 30 ? \"\u2026\" : \"\"}\".\\n\\nTry asking about:\\n\u2022 A specific animal (e.g. \"Tell me about Sharks\")\\n\u2022 App features (e.g. \"How do I upload a reel?\")\\n\u2022 Wildlife topics (e.g. \"What is migration?\")\\n\\n\ud83d\udce7 For other help: animalx00003@gmail.com`;\n   142\u2192\n   143\u2192    setMessages(prev => [...prev, { role: \"ai\", text: aiText }]);\n   144\u2192    setTyping(false);\n   145\u2192  }, [input]);\n   146\u2192\n   147\u2192  const filtered = messages.filter(m =>\n   148\u2192    !searchQuery || m.text.toLowerCase().includes(searchQuery.toLowerCase())\n   149\u2192  );\n   150\u2192\n   151\u2192  return (\n   152\u2192    <>\n   153\u2192      {/* Floating Action Button */}\n   154\u2192      <button\n   155\u2192        className={`ai-fab ${open ? \"ai-fab-open\" : \"\"}`}\n   156\u2192        onClick={() => setOpen(v => !v)}\n   157\u2192        title=\"Wildlife AI Assistant\"\n   158\u2192        aria-label=\"Open Wildlife AI chat\"\n   159\u2192      >\n   160\u2192        {open ? \"\u2715\" : \"\ud83e\udd16\"}\n   161\u2192      </button>\n   162\u2192\n   163\u2192      {/* Chat Panel */}\n   164\u2192      {open && (\n   165\u2192        <div className=\"ai-panel\" role=\"dialog\" aria-label=\"Wildlife AI\">\n   166\u2192          {/* Header */}\n   167\u2192          <div className=\"ai-panel-header\">\n   168\u2192            <div className=\"ai-header-left\">\n   169\u2192              <div className=\"ai-avatar\">\ud83e\udd16</div>\n   170\u2192              <div>\n   171\u2192                <div className=\"ai-header-title\">Wildlife AI</div>\n   172\u2192                <div className=\"ai-header-sub\">\ud83d\udfe2 Online \u00b7 Instant answers</div>\n   173\u2192              </div>\n   174\u2192            </div>\n   175\u2192            <button className=\"ai-panel-close\" onClick={() => setOpen(false)}>\u2715</button>\n   176\u2192          </div>\n   177\u2192\n   178\u2192          {/* Search inside chat */}\n   179\u2192          {messages.length > 4 && (\n   180\u2192            <div className=\"ai-chat-search\">\n   181\u2192              <input\n   182\u2192                placeholder=\"\ud83d\udd0d Search conversation\u2026\"\n   183\u2192                value={searchQuery}\n   184\u2192                onChange={e => setSearchQuery(e.target.value)}\n   185\u2192                className=\"ai-search-input\"\n   186\u2192              />\n   187\u2192              {searchQuery && <button onClick={() => setSearchQuery(\"\")} className=\"ai-search-clear\">\u2715</button>}\n   188\u2192            </div>\n   189\u2192          )}\n   190\u2192\n   191\u2192          {/* Messages */}\n   192\u2192          <div className=\"ai-messages\">\n   193\u2192            {filtered.map((m, i) => (\n   194\u2192              <div key={i} className={`ai-msg-wrap ${m.role}`}>\n   195\u2192                {m.role === \"ai\" && <div className=\"ai-msg-avatar\">\ud83e\udd16</div>}\n   196\u2192                <div className={`ai-msg-bubble ${m.role}`}>\n   197\u2192                  <FormattedMessage text={m.text} />\n   198\u2192                </div>\n   199\u2192              </div>\n   200\u2192            ))}\n   201\u2192            {typing && (\n   202\u2192              <div className=\"ai-msg-wrap ai\">\n   203\u2192                <div className=\"ai-msg-avatar\">\ud83e\udd16</div>\n   204\u2192                <div className=\"ai-msg-bubble ai ai-typing-bubble\">\n   205\u2192                  <span className=\"ai-dot\" /><span className=\"ai-dot\" /><span className=\"ai-dot\" />\n   206\u2192                </div>\n   207\u2192              </div>\n   208\u2192            )}\n   209\u2192            <div ref={messagesEndRef} />\n   210\u2192          </div>\n   211\u2192\n   212\u2192          {/* Suggested questions */}\n   213\u2192          {messages.length <= 2 && (\n   214\u2192            <div className=\"ai-suggestions\">\n   215\u2192              <div className=\"ai-suggestions-label\">\ud83d\udca1 Try asking:</div>\n   216\u2192              <div className=\"ai-suggestions-scroll\">\n   217\u2192                {SUGGESTED.map((s, i) => (\n   218\u2192                  <button key={i} className=\"ai-suggestion-chip\" onClick={() => sendMessage(s)}>\n   219\u2192                    {s}\n   220\u2192                  </button>\n   221\u2192                ))}\n   222\u2192              </div>\n   223\u2192            </div>\n   224\u2192          )}\n   225\u2192\n   226\u2192          {/* Input */}\n   227\u2192          <div className=\"ai-input-wrap\">\n   228\u2192            <input\n   229\u2192              ref={inputRef}\n   230\u2192              className=\"ai-input\"\n   231\u2192              placeholder=\"Ask about animals or app features\u2026\"\n   232\u2192              value={input}\n   233\u2192              onChange={e => setInput(e.target.value)}\n   234\u2192              onKeyDown={e => { if (e.key === \"Enter\" && !e.shiftKey) { e.preventDefault(); sendMessage(); } }}\n   235\u2192            />\n   236\u2192            <button\n   237\u2192              className=\"ai-send-btn\"\n   238\u2192              onClick={() => sendMessage()}\n   239\u2192              disabled={!input.trim() || typing}\n   240\u2192              aria-label=\"Send\"\n   241\u2192            >\n   242\u2192              \u27a4\n   243\u2192            </button>\n   244\u2192          </div>\n   245\u2192        </div>\n   246\u2192      )}\n   247\u2192    </>\n   248\u2192  );\n   249\u2192}\n   250\u2192"}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Here's the result of running `cat -n` on a snippet of artifacts/animal-x/src/pages/Profile.jsx (lines 1-80 of 829)\n     1\u2192import { useState, useRef } from \"react\";\n     2\u2192import { Link } from \"wouter\";\n     3\u2192import { useAuth } from \"../context/AuthContext\";\n     4\u2192import { useTheme } from \"../context/ThemeContext\";\n     5\u2192import { addCustomAnimal, getCustomAnimals, deleteCustomAnimal } from \"../utils/customAnimals\";\n     6\u2192import { fileToDataURL } from \"../utils/animalOverrides\";\n     7\u2192import { categories } from \"../data/animals\";\n     8\u2192import BlueTick from \"../components/BlueTick\";\n     9\u2192\n    10\u2192function formatCount(n) {\n    11\u2192  if (n == null || isNaN(n)) return \"0\";\n    12\u2192  if (n >= 1_000_000) return (n / 1_000_000).toFixed(n % 1_000_000 === 0 ? 0 : 1) + \"M\";\n    13\u2192  if (n >= 1_000) return (n / 1_000).toFixed(n % 1_000 === 0 ? 0 : 1) + \"K\";\n    14\u2192  return String(n);\n    15\u2192}\n    16\u2192\n    17\u2192function parseCount(str) {\n    18\u2192  if (typeof str === \"number\") return str;\n    19\u2192  const s = String(str || \"\").trim().toLowerCase();\n    20\u2192  if (!s) return 0;\n    21\u2192  const m = s.match(/^([\\d.]+)\\s*([kmb]?)$/);\n    22\u2192  if (!m) return parseInt(s.replace(/\\D/g, \"\"), 10) || 0;\n    23\u2192  const n = parseFloat(m[1]);\n    24\u2192  const mult = m[2] === \"k\" ? 1_000 : m[2] === \"m\" ? 1_000_000 : m[2] === \"b\" ? 1_000_000_000 : 1;\n    25\u2192  return Math.round(n * mult);\n    26\u2192}\n    27\u2192\n    28\u2192export default function Profile() {\n    29\u2192  const {\n    30\u2192    user,\n    31\u2192    profile,\n    32\u2192    adminMode,\n    33\u2192    isSuperAdmin,\n    34\u2192    isVerified,\n    35\u2192    verifiedMap,\n    36\u2192    SUPER_ADMIN_EMAIL,\n    37\u2192    unlockAdminMode,\n    38\u2192    lockAdminMode,\n    39\u2192    updateProfile,\n    40\u2192    setVerifiedFor,\n    41\u2192    getAllUsers,\n    42\u2192    logout,\n    43\u2192  } = useAuth();\n    44\u2192  const { theme, toggleTheme } = useTheme();\n    45\u2192\n    46\u2192  const [tapCount, setTapCount] = useState(0);\n    47\u2192  const tapTimer = useRef(null);\n    48\u2192  const [tab, setTab] = useState(\"grid\");\n    49\u2192  const [search, setSearch] = useState(\"\");\n    50\u2192  const [followersInput, setFollowersInput] = useState(\"\");\n    51\u2192  const [postsInput, setPostsInput] = useState(\"\");\n    52\u2192  const [reelsInput, setReelsInput] = useState(\"\");\n    53\u2192  const [editProfileOpen, setEditProfileOpen] = useState(false);\n    54\u2192  const [helpOpen, setHelpOpen] = useState(false);\n    55\u2192  const [nameInput, setNameInput] = useState(user?.name || \"\");\n    56\u2192  const photoFileRef = useRef(null);\n    57\u2192\n    58\u2192  // Add new animal form state\n    59\u2192  const [newName, setNewName] = useState(\"\");\n    60\u2192  const [newCategory, setNewCategory] = useState(categories[0]);\n    61\u2192  const [newImage, setNewImage] = useState(null);\n    62\u2192  const [newHabits, setNewHabits] = useState(\"\");\n    63\u2192  const [newLifespan, setNewLifespan] = useState(\"\");\n    64\u2192  const [newCountry, setNewCountry] = useState(\"\");\n    65\u2192  const [customAnimals, setCustomAnimalsState] = useState(() => getCustomAnimals());\n    66\u2192\n    67\u2192  function refreshCustomList() {\n    68\u2192    setCustomAnimalsState(getCustomAnimals());\n    69\u2192  }\n    70\u2192\n    71\u2192  function handleAvatarTap() {\n    72\u2192    const next = tapCount + 1;\n    73\u2192    setTapCount(next);\n    74\u2192    if (tapTimer.current) clearTimeout(tapTimer.current);\n    75\u2192    tapTimer.current = setTimeout(() => setTapCount(0), 1500);\n    76\u2192    if (next >= 7) {\n    77\u2192      setTapCount(0);\n    78\u2192      if (!user) {\n    79\u2192        alert(\"Please login first to use Admin Mode.\");\n    80\u2192        return;"}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Here's the result of running `cat -n` on a snippet of artifacts/animal-x/src/pages/Chatbot.jsx (lines 1-50 of 245)\n     1\u2192import { useState, useRef, useEffect } from \"react\";\n     2\u2192\n     3\u2192const WILDLIFE_KEYWORDS = [\n     4\u2192  \"animal\",\"wildlife\",\"bird\",\"fish\",\"mammal\",\"reptile\",\"insect\",\"plant\",\"tree\",\"nature\",\n     5\u2192  \"habitat\",\"forest\",\"ocean\",\"desert\",\"mountain\",\"jungle\",\"savanna\",\"ecosystem\",\"species\",\n     6\u2192  \"lion\",\"tiger\",\"elephant\",\"wolf\",\"bear\",\"shark\",\"eagle\",\"dolphin\",\"whale\",\"crocodile\",\n     7\u2192  \"snake\",\"lizard\",\"parrot\",\"owl\",\"penguin\",\"butterfly\",\"bee\",\"ant\",\"frog\",\"coral\",\n     8\u2192  \"zoo\",\"safari\",\"migration\",\"extinction\",\"endangered\",\"conservation\",\"predator\",\"prey\",\n     9\u2192  \"carnivore\",\"herbivore\",\"omnivore\",\"food chain\",\"biodiversity\",\"climate\",\"environment\"\n    10\u2192];\n    11\u2192\n    12\u2192// Big animal knowledge base\n    13\u2192const wildlifeQA = [\n    14\u2192  { q: /lion|lions/i, a: \"\ud83e\udd81 Lions are apex predators of the African savanna. They live in groups called prides (5\u201315 lions), and males have iconic manes. Diet: zebra, wildebeest, buffalo. Lifespan: 12\u201316 years wild.\" },\n    15\u2192  { q: /tiger|tigers/i, a: \"\ud83d\udc05 Tigers are the largest cats \u2014 Bengal and Siberian are the biggest. Solitary hunters, excellent swimmers, and can weigh up to 300 kg. Found in India, Russia, Indonesia, and parts of SE Asia.\" },\n    16\u2192  { q: /elephant|elephants/i, a: \"\ud83d\udc18 Elephants are the largest land animals. African elephants (bigger ears) and Asian elephants. They live 60\u201370 years, mourn their dead, and have remarkable memories.\" },\n    17\u2192  { q: /shark|sharks/i, a: \"\ud83e\udd88 Sharks are 450-million-year-old ocean predators. There are 500+ species, from the tiny dwarf lantern shark (20 cm) to the whale shark (12 m).\" },\n    18\u2192  { q: /whale|whales/i, a: \"\ud83d\udc0b Whales are the largest animals on Earth. Blue whales reach 30 m and 200 tons. Their songs travel thousands of miles underwater.\" },\n    19\u2192  { q: /eagle|eagles/i, a: \"\ud83e\udd85 Eagles have eyesight 4\u20138x sharper than humans \u2014 they spot prey from 3 km away. Bald Eagle is the USA's national bird. 60+ species worldwide.\" },\n    20\u2192  { q: /coral|reef/i, a: \"\ud83e\udeb8 Coral reefs cover < 1% of the ocean but support 25% of marine species. Climate change is bleaching them \u2014 protect them by reducing carbon footprint.\" },\n    21\u2192  { q: /sahara|desert/i, a: \"\ud83c\udfdc\ufe0f The Sahara is the world's largest hot desert at 9.2 million km\u00b2. Despite the heat it hosts 500+ plant species, 70 mammal species, and 90 bird species.\" },\n    22\u2192  { q: /dolphin|dolphins/i, a: \"\ud83d\udc2c Dolphins are highly intelligent \u2014 they use names (signature whistles), echolocation, and tools. Bottlenose dolphins can solve mirror self-recognition.\" },\n    23\u2192  { q: /penguin|penguins/i, a: \"\ud83d\udc27 Penguins are flightless but extraordinary swimmers. Emperor penguins dive 500+ m, hold breath 20 min, and breed in -50\u00b0C Antarctic winters.\" },\n    24\u2192  { q: /endangered|extinction/i, a: \"\ud83c\udf0d 1 million+ species face extinction due to habitat loss, climate change, and poaching. Conservation efforts: protected reserves, breeding programs, and CITES treaty.\" },\n    25\u2192  { q: /migration/i, a: \"\ud83e\udd8b Wildebeest cover 3,000 km across Africa. Arctic terns fly 70,000 km/year. Monarch butterflies cross North America. Gray whales migrate 20,000 km.\" },\n    26\u2192  { q: /zoo|zoos/i, a: \"\ud83c\udfdb\ufe0f Modern zoos save species through breeding programs (Arabian Oryx, California Condor were saved this way). Top zoos: San Diego, Singapore, Chester. Open the Map page to see 200+.\" },\n    27\u2192  { q: /panda|pandas/i, a: \"\ud83d\udc3c Giant pandas eat 12 kg of bamboo daily and live in China's mountain forests. Population recovered from 1,000 to ~1,800 thanks to conservation.\" },\n    28\u2192  { q: /wolf|wolves/i, a: \"\ud83d\udc3a Wolves live in packs of 6\u201310 led by an alpha pair. They communicate by howls heard 10 km away. Found across N. America, Europe, and Asia.\" },\n    29\u2192  { q: /snake|snakes/i, a: \"\ud83d\udc0d 3,000+ snake species. Only ~600 are venomous. Fastest: Black Mamba (20 km/h). Largest: Reticulated Python (7 m). All snakes are carnivores.\" },\n    30\u2192  { q: /crocodile|alligator/i, a: \"\ud83d\udc0a Crocodiles haven't changed much in 200 million years. Saltwater crocs are the largest reptile (7 m, 1,000 kg). Their bite is the strongest in the animal kingdom.\" },\n    31\u2192  { q: /bee|bees/i, a: \"\ud83d\udc1d Bees pollinate 1/3 of all crops. A single hive holds 60,000 bees. They communicate via the 'waggle dance' to share flower locations.\" },\n    32\u2192  { q: /butterfly|butterflies/i, a: \"\ud83e\udd8b 17,500 butterfly species. Monarchs migrate 4,800 km. They taste with their feet and have compound eyes. Caterpillars can eat 27,000x their body weight.\" },\n    33\u2192  { q: /bear|bears/i, a: \"\ud83d\udc3b 8 bear species. Polar bears (largest) weigh 700 kg and swim 100 km. Grizzlies, black bears, sun bears, sloth bears \u2014 all omnivores except polar bears.\" },\n    34\u2192  { q: /how many|species/i, a: \"\ud83d\udd2c Scientists estimate 8.7 million species exist on Earth. Only ~1.2 million are formally described. New ones are discovered every year \u2014 many in deep ocean and rainforest.\" },\n    35\u2192  { q: /largest|biggest/i, a: \"\ud83d\udccf Largest ever: blue whale (30 m). Largest land animal: African elephant (6,000 kg). Largest bird: ostrich (2.7 m). Largest fish: whale shark (12 m).\" },\n    36\u2192  { q: /fastest/i, a: \"\ud83c\udfc3 Cheetah: 120 km/h (land). Peregrine falcon: 389 km/h (dive). Sailfish: 110 km/h (sea). Pronghorn: 90 km/h sustained over 6 km.\" },\n    37\u2192  { q: /smart|intelligent/i, a: \"\ud83e\udde0 Most intelligent: chimps, dolphins, elephants, octopuses, crows, pigs, parrots. Some use tools, solve puzzles, recognize themselves in mirrors.\" },\n    38\u2192];\n    39\u2192\n    40\u2192// Common animal name typo/spelling correction map\n    41\u2192const TYPO_MAP = {\n    42\u2192  lion: [\"lin\",\"lione\",\"loin\",\"lionn\",\"lyon\"],\n    43\u2192  tiger: [\"tigr\",\"tigar\",\"tiiger\",\"tyger\",\"teiger\"],\n    44\u2192  elephant: [\"elefant\",\"elephent\",\"elphant\",\"elephnt\"],\n    45\u2192  cheetah: [\"cheeta\",\"cheta\",\"chetah\",\"cheatah\"],\n    46\u2192  giraffe: [\"girafe\",\"giraff\",\"gerafe\",\"jiraffe\"],\n    47\u2192  crocodile: [\"crocodil\",\"corcodile\",\"crocodial\"],\n    48\u2192  rhinoceros: [\"rhino\",\"rinocerous\",\"rhinocerus\"],\n    49\u2192  shark: [\"shak\",\"sharc\",\"sharkk\"],\n    50\u2192  dolphin: [\"dolfin\",\"dolphn\",\"dolfine\"],"}]}]}
{"memory_id": 374, "messages": [{"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Let me read the remaining critical files to understand the full picture:"}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": [], "tool_calls": [{"type": "tool", "name": "read", "arguments": {"file_path": "artifacts/animal-x/src/App.jsx"}}, {"type": "tool", "name": "read", "arguments": {"file_path": "artifacts/animal-x/src/pages/Profile.jsx", "offset": 80, "limit": 200}}, {"type": "tool", "name": "read", "arguments": {"file_path": "artifacts/animal-x/src/styles/app.css", "limit": 80}}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Failed to read file: File artifacts/animal-x/src/App.jsx does not exist. Did you mean: App.tsx?"}], "is_error": true}, {"role": "tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Here's the result of running `cat -n` on a snippet of artifacts/animal-x/src/pages/Profile.jsx (lines 80-279 of 829)\n    80\u2192        return;\n    81\u2192      }\n    82\u2192      if (!isSuperAdmin) {\n    83\u2192        alert(\"Admin Mode is restricted to the super admin account.\");\n    84\u2192        return;\n    85\u2192      }\n    86\u2192      unlockAdminMode();\n    87\u2192    }\n    88\u2192  }\n    89\u2192\n    90\u2192  async function handleProfilePhoto(e) {\n    91\u2192    const file = e.target.files?.[0];\n    92\u2192    if (!file) return;\n    93\u2192    try {\n    94\u2192      const res = await fetch(\"/api/storage/uploads/request-url\", {\n    95\u2192        method: \"POST\",\n    96\u2192        headers: { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" },\n    97\u2192        body: JSON.stringify({ name: `profile_${user.uid}_${Date.now()}`, size: file.size, contentType: file.type }),\n    98\u2192      });\n    99\u2192      if (res.ok) {\n   100\u2192        const { uploadURL, objectPath } = await res.json();\n   101\u2192        await fetch(uploadURL, { method: \"PUT\", headers: { \"Content-Type\": file.type }, body: file });\n   102\u2192        updateProfile({ photo: objectPath });\n   103\u2192        return;\n   104\u2192      }\n   105\u2192    } catch {}\n   106\u2192    const dataUrl = await fileToDataURL(file);\n   107\u2192    updateProfile({ photo: dataUrl });\n   108\u2192  }\n   109\u2192\n   110\u2192  async function handleCoverPhoto(e) {\n   111\u2192    const file = e.target.files?.[0];\n   112\u2192    if (!file) return;\n   113\u2192    try {\n   114\u2192      const res = await fetch(\"/api/storage/uploads/request-url\", {\n   115\u2192        method: \"POST\",\n   116\u2192        headers: { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" },\n   117\u2192        body: JSON.stringify({ name: `cover_${user.uid}_${Date.now()}`, size: file.size, contentType: file.type }),\n   118\u2192      });\n   119\u2192      if (res.ok) {\n   120\u2192        const { uploadURL, objectPath } = await res.json();\n   121\u2192        await fetch(uploadURL, { method: \"PUT\", headers: { \"Content-Type\": file.type }, body: file });\n   122\u2192        updateProfile({ cover: objectPath });\n   123\u2192        return;\n   124\u2192      }\n   125\u2192    } catch {}\n   126\u2192    const dataUrl = await fileToDataURL(file);\n   127\u2192    updateProfile({ cover: dataUrl });\n   128\u2192  }\n   129\u2192\n   130\u2192  function saveProfileEdits() {\n   131\u2192    updateProfile({ name: nameInput });\n   132\u2192    setEditProfileOpen(false);\n   133\u2192  }\n   134\u2192\n   135\u2192  async function handleNewAnimalImage(e) {\n   136\u2192    const file = e.target.files?.[0];\n   137\u2192    if (!file) return;\n   138\u2192    const dataUrl = await fileToDataURL(file);\n   139\u2192    setNewImage(dataUrl);\n   140\u2192  }\n   141\u2192\n   142\u2192  function submitNewAnimal() {\n   143\u2192    if (!newName.trim()) {\n   144\u2192      alert(\"Animal name is required.\");\n   145\u2192      return;\n   146\u2192    }\n   147\u2192    addCustomAnimal({\n   148\u2192      name: newName.trim(),\n   149\u2192      category: newCategory,\n   150\u2192      image: newImage,\n   151\u2192      habits: newHabits.trim(),\n   152\u2192      habitat: newHabits.trim() || \"Various habitats\",\n   153\u2192      lifespan: newLifespan.trim() || \"Unknown\",\n   154\u2192      country: newCountry.trim() || \"Worldwide\",\n   155\u2192    });\n   156\u2192    setNewName(\"\");\n   157\u2192    setNewImage(null);\n   158\u2192    setNewHabits(\"\");\n   159\u2192    setNewLifespan(\"\");\n   160\u2192    setNewCountry(\"\");\n   161\u2192    if (photoFileRef.current) photoFileRef.current.value = \"\";\n   162\u2192    refreshCustomList();\n   163\u2192    alert(`\u2713 Added \"${newName}\" to ${newCategory}!`);\n   164\u2192  }\n   165\u2192\n   166\u2192  function removeCustom(id, name) {\n   167\u2192    if (!confirm(`Delete \"${name}\"? This cannot be undone.`)) return;\n   168\u2192    deleteCustomAnimal(id);\n   169\u2192    refreshCustomList();\n   170\u2192  }\n   171\u2192\n   172\u2192  if (!user) {\n   173\u2192    return (\n   174\u2192      <div className=\"profile-page profile-empty\">\n   175\u2192        <div className=\"profile-empty-card\">\n   176\u2192          <div className=\"profile-empty-icon\">\ud83d\udc64</div>\n   177\u2192          <h2>Welcome to Animal X</h2>\n   178\u2192          <p>Login or sign up to create your wildlife creator profile.</p>\n   179\u2192          <Link href=\"/auth\" className=\"btn-primary\">Login / Sign Up</Link>\n   180\u2192        </div>\n   181\u2192      </div>\n   182\u2192    );\n   183\u2192  }\n   184\u2192\n   185\u2192  const allUsers = getAllUsers();\n   186\u2192  const filteredUsers = allUsers.filter((u) => {\n   187\u2192    if (!search) return true;\n   188\u2192    const q = search.toLowerCase();\n   189\u2192    return (\n   190\u2192      (u.name || \"\").toLowerCase().includes(q) ||\n   191\u2192      (u.email || \"\").toLowerCase().includes(q) ||\n   192\u2192      (u.uid || \"\").toLowerCase().includes(q)\n   193\u2192    );\n   194\u2192  });\n   195\u2192\n   196\u2192  function applyFollowers() {\n   197\u2192    const n = parseCount(followersInput);\n   198\u2192    updateProfile({ followers: n });\n   199\u2192    setFollowersInput(\"\");\n   200\u2192  }\n   201\u2192  function applyPosts() {\n   202\u2192    const n = parseInt(postsInput, 10);\n   203\u2192    if (!isNaN(n)) { updateProfile({ posts: n }); setPostsInput(\"\"); }\n   204\u2192  }\n   205\u2192  function applyReels() {\n   206\u2192    const n = parseInt(reelsInput, 10);\n   207\u2192    if (!isNaN(n)) { updateProfile({ reels: n }); setReelsInput(\"\"); }\n   208\u2192  }\n   209\u2192  function copyText(text) {\n   210\u2192    navigator.clipboard?.writeText(text).then(\n   211\u2192      () => alert(`Copied: ${text}`),\n   212\u2192      () => alert(\"Copy failed\")\n   213\u2192    );\n   214\u2192  }\n   215\u2192\n   216\u2192  const displayName = profile.name || user.name || user.email;\n   217\u2192  const initial = (displayName || \"U\")[0].toUpperCase();\n   218\u2192\n   219\u2192  function resolveUrl(path) {\n   220\u2192    if (!path) return null;\n   221\u2192    if (path.startsWith(\"data:\") || path.startsWith(\"http\")) return path;\n   222\u2192    return `/api/storage${path}`;\n   223\u2192  }\n   224\u2192\n   225\u2192  const photoUrl = resolveUrl(profile.photo);\n   226\u2192  const coverUrl = resolveUrl(profile.cover);\n   227\u2192\n   228\u2192  return (\n   229\u2192    <div className=\"profile-page\">\n   230\u2192      <div className=\"profile-cover-wrap\">\n   231\u2192        <div\n   232\u2192          className=\"profile-cover-bg\"\n   233\u2192          style={coverUrl ? { backgroundImage: `url(${coverUrl})` } : undefined}\n   234\u2192        >\n   235\u2192          {!coverUrl && <div className=\"profile-cover-gradient\" />}\n   236\u2192        </div>\n   237\u2192        <label className=\"profile-cover-edit-btn\" title=\"Change cover photo\">\n   238\u2192          \ud83d\udcf7\n   239\u2192          <input type=\"file\" accept=\"image/*\" style={{ display: \"none\" }} onChange={handleCoverPhoto} />\n   240\u2192        </label>\n   241\u2192      </div>\n   242\u2192\n   243\u2192      <div className=\"profile-top\">\n   244\u2192        <button\n   245\u2192          className=\"profile-avatar-btn\"\n   246\u2192          onClick={handleAvatarTap}\n   247\u2192          aria-label=\"Profile photo (tap 7 times for admin mode)\"\n   248\u2192          style={photoUrl ? { backgroundImage: `url(${photoUrl})`, backgroundSize: \"cover\", backgroundPosition: \"center\", color: \"transparent\" } : undefined}\n   249\u2192        >\n   250\u2192          {!photoUrl && initial}\n   251\u2192        </button>\n   252\u2192        <div className=\"profile-id\">\n   253\u2192          <h1 className=\"profile-name\">\n   254\u2192            {displayName}\n   255\u2192            {isVerified && <BlueTick />}\n   256\u2192          </h1>\n   257\u2192          <p className=\"profile-email\">{user.email}</p>\n   258\u2192        </div>\n   259\u2192      </div>\n   260\u2192\n   261\u2192      <div className=\"profile-stats\">\n   262\u2192        <div className=\"stat-block\">\n   263\u2192          <div className=\"stat-num\">{formatCount(profile.posts)}</div>\n   264\u2192          <div className=\"stat-lbl\">Posts</div>\n   265\u2192        </div>\n   266\u2192        <div className=\"stat-block\">\n   267\u2192          <div className=\"stat-num\">{formatCount(profile.followers)}</div>\n   268\u2192          <div className=\"stat-lbl\">Followers</div>\n   269\u2192        </div>\n   270\u2192        <div className=\"stat-block\">\n   271\u2192          <div className=\"stat-num\">{formatCount(profile.following)}</div>\n   272\u2192          <div className=\"stat-lbl\">Following</div>\n   273\u2192        </div>\n   274\u2192      </div>\n   275\u2192\n   276\u2192      <div className=\"profile-quick-stats\">\n   277\u2192        <button className=\"qs-pill qs-edit\" onClick={() => setEditProfileOpen((v) => !v)}>\n   278\u2192          \u270f\ufe0f Edit Profile\n   279\u2192        </button>"}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Here's the result of running `cat -n` on a snippet of artifacts/animal-x/src/styles/app.css (lines 1-80 of 6458)\n     1\u2192/* ===== ANIMAL X - GLOBAL STYLES ===== */\n     2\u2192\n     3\u2192* {\n     4\u2192  box-sizing: border-box;\n     5\u2192  margin: 0;\n     6\u2192  padding: 0;\n     7\u2192}\n     8\u2192\n     9\u2192:root {\n    10\u2192  --bg: #0a0f1e;\n    11\u2192  --bg2: #111827;\n    12\u2192  --bg3: #1f2937;\n    13\u2192  --card-bg: #1a2332;\n    14\u2192  --border: #2d3748;\n    15\u2192  --text: #f1f5f9;\n    16\u2192  --text2: #94a3b8;\n    17\u2192  --accent: #22c55e;\n    18\u2192  --accent2: #16a34a;\n    19\u2192  --accent-blue: #3b82f6;\n    20\u2192  --accent-orange: #f59e0b;\n    21\u2192  --radius: 12px;\n    22\u2192  --shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.4);\n    23\u2192  --nav-h: 64px;\n    24\u2192}\n    25\u2192\n    26\u2192body {\n    27\u2192  background: var(--bg);\n    28\u2192  color: var(--text);\n    29\u2192  font-family: 'Inter', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, sans-serif;\n    30\u2192  line-height: 1.6;\n    31\u2192  min-height: 100vh;\n    32\u2192}\n    33\u2192\n    34\u2192a { text-decoration: none; color: inherit; }\n    35\u2192\n    36\u2192/* ===== LAYOUT ===== */\n    37\u2192.app-layout {\n    38\u2192  display: flex;\n    39\u2192  flex-direction: column;\n    40\u2192  min-height: 100vh;\n    41\u2192}\n    42\u2192\n    43\u2192.app-main {\n    44\u2192  margin-top: var(--nav-h);\n    45\u2192  flex: 1;\n    46\u2192}\n    47\u2192\n    48\u2192/* ===== NAVBAR ===== */\n    49\u2192.navbar {\n    50\u2192  position: fixed;\n    51\u2192  top: 0; left: 0; right: 0;\n    52\u2192  z-index: 1000;\n    53\u2192  height: var(--nav-h);\n    54\u2192  background: rgba(10, 15, 30, 0.95);\n    55\u2192  backdrop-filter: blur(12px);\n    56\u2192  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);\n    57\u2192  display: flex;\n    58\u2192  align-items: center;\n    59\u2192  justify-content: space-between;\n    60\u2192  padding: 0 24px;\n    61\u2192  gap: 16px;\n    62\u2192}\n    63\u2192\n    64\u2192.brand-link {\n    65\u2192  display: flex;\n    66\u2192  align-items: center;\n    67\u2192  gap: 8px;\n    68\u2192  font-weight: 700;\n    69\u2192  font-size: 1.2rem;\n    70\u2192}\n    71\u2192\n    72\u2192.brand-icon { font-size: 1.5rem; }\n    73\u2192.brand-name { color: var(--accent); }\n    74\u2192\n    75\u2192.nav-links {\n    76\u2192  display: flex;\n    77\u2192  align-items: center;\n    78\u2192  gap: 4px;\n    79\u2192}\n    80\u2192"}]}]}
{"memory_id": 375, "messages": [{"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Let me read the remaining files I need in parallel:"}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": [], "tool_calls": [{"type": "tool", "name": "read", "arguments": {"file_path": "artifacts/animal-x/src/App.tsx"}}, {"type": "tool", "name": "read", "arguments": {"file_path": "artifacts/animal-x/src/pages/Profile.jsx", "offset": 279, "limit": 300}}, {"type": "tool", "name": "read", "arguments": {"file_path": "artifacts/animal-x/src/context/AuthContext.jsx", "limit": 60}}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Here's the result of running `cat -n` on a snippet of artifacts/animal-x/src/App.tsx\n     1\u2192import { useState, useEffect, lazy, Suspense, startTransition } from \"react\";\n     2\u2192import { Switch, Route, Router as WouterRouter } from \"wouter\";\n     3\u2192import { QueryClient, QueryClientProvider } from \"@tanstack/react-query\";\n     4\u2192import { AuthProvider } from \"./context/AuthContext\";\n     5\u2192import { SocialProvider } from \"./context/SocialContext\";\n     6\u2192import { ThemeProvider } from \"./context/ThemeContext\";\n     7\u2192import Navbar from \"./components/Navbar\";\n     8\u2192import FirebaseStatusBanner from \"./components/FirebaseStatusBanner\";\n     9\u2192import AutoTickPopup from \"./components/AutoTickPopup\";\n    10\u2192import WildlifeAI from \"./components/WildlifeAI\";\n    11\u2192\n    12\u2192// Lazy load every page \u2014 each becomes its own JS chunk, loaded only when visited\n    13\u2192const Home        = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/Home\"));\n    14\u2192const Animals     = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/Animals\"));\n    15\u2192const AnimalDetail = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/AnimalDetail\"));\n    16\u2192const Map         = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/Map\"));\n    17\u2192const Reels       = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/Reels\"));\n    18\u2192const Travel      = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/Travel\"));\n    19\u2192const Chatbot     = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/Chatbot\"));\n    20\u2192const HelpDesk    = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/HelpDesk\"));\n    21\u2192const Auth        = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/Auth\"));\n    22\u2192const Profile     = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/Profile\"));\n    23\u2192const UserProfile = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/UserProfile\"));\n    24\u2192const Ads         = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/Ads\"));\n    25\u2192const Search      = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/Search\"));\n    26\u2192\n    27\u2192const queryClient = new QueryClient({\n    28\u2192  defaultOptions: {\n    29\u2192    queries: {\n    30\u2192      staleTime: 5 * 60 * 1000,\n    31\u2192      retry: 1,\n    32\u2192      refetchOnWindowFocus: false,\n    33\u2192    },\n    34\u2192  },\n    35\u2192});\n    36\u2192\n    37\u2192function PageFallback() {\n    38\u2192  return <div className=\"page-loading\">Loading</div>;\n    39\u2192}\n    40\u2192\n    41\u2192function NotFound() {\n    42\u2192  return (\n    43\u2192    <div style={{ textAlign: \"center\", padding: \"80px 20px\" }}>\n    44\u2192      <div style={{ fontSize: \"80px\" }}>\ud83d\udd0d</div>\n    45\u2192      <h2 style={{ fontSize: \"24px\", marginTop: \"16px\" }}>Page Not Found</h2>\n    46\u2192      <a href=\"/\" style={{ color: \"#22c55e\", marginTop: \"16px\", display: \"inline-block\" }}>\u2190 Go Home</a>\n    47\u2192    </div>\n    48\u2192  );\n    49\u2192}\n    50\u2192\n    51\u2192function SplashScreen() {\n    52\u2192  return (\n    53\u2192    <div className=\"splash\">\n    54\u2192      <div className=\"splash-inner\">\n    55\u2192        <div className=\"splash-icon\">\ud83d\udc3e</div>\n    56\u2192        <h1 className=\"splash-title\">Animal X</h1>\n    57\u2192        <p className=\"splash-sub\">Wildlife Explorer</p>\n    58\u2192        <div className=\"splash-loader\">\n    59\u2192          <div className=\"splash-dot\" />\n    60\u2192          <div className=\"splash-dot\" />\n    61\u2192          <div className=\"splash-dot\" />\n    62\u2192        </div>\n    63\u2192      </div>\n    64\u2192    </div>\n    65\u2192  );\n    66\u2192}\n    67\u2192\n    68\u2192function Router() {\n    69\u2192  return (\n    70\u2192    <div className=\"app-layout\">\n    71\u2192      <Navbar />\n    72\u2192      <AutoTickPopup />\n    73\u2192      <main className=\"app-main\">\n    74\u2192        <Suspense fallback={<PageFallback />}>\n    75\u2192          <Switch>\n    76\u2192            <Route path=\"/\" component={Home} />\n    77\u2192            <Route path=\"/animals\" component={Animals} />\n    78\u2192            <Route path=\"/animals/:id\" component={AnimalDetail} />\n    79\u2192            <Route path=\"/map\" component={Map} />\n    80\u2192            <Route path=\"/reels\" component={Reels} />\n    81\u2192            <Route path=\"/travel\" component={Travel} />\n    82\u2192            <Route path=\"/chat\" component={Chatbot} />\n    83\u2192            <Route path=\"/help\" component={HelpDesk} />\n    84\u2192            <Route path=\"/auth\" component={Auth} />\n    85\u2192            <Route path=\"/profile\" component={Profile} />\n    86\u2192            <Route path=\"/user/:userId\" component={UserProfile} />\n    87\u2192            <Route path=\"/ads\" component={Ads} />\n    88\u2192            <Route path=\"/search\" component={Search} />\n    89\u2192            <Route path=\"/live-tracking\" component={Map} />\n    90\u2192            <Route component={NotFound} />\n    91\u2192          </Switch>\n    92\u2192        </Suspense>\n    93\u2192      </main>\n    94\u2192      <WildlifeAI />\n    95\u2192      <FirebaseStatusBanner />\n    96\u2192    </div>\n    97\u2192  );\n    98\u2192}\n    99\u2192\n   100\u2192function App() {\n   101\u2192  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);\n   102\u2192\n   103\u2192  useEffect(() => {\n   104\u2192    // Reduced from 1500ms \u2192 400ms splash\n   105\u2192    const timer = setTimeout(() => {\n   106\u2192      startTransition(() => setLoading(false));\n   107\u2192    }, 400);\n   108\u2192    return () => clearTimeout(timer);\n   109\u2192  }, []);\n   110\u2192\n   111\u2192  if (loading) return <SplashScreen />;\n   112\u2192\n   113\u2192  return (\n   114\u2192    <QueryClientProvider client={queryClient}>\n   115\u2192      <ThemeProvider>\n   116\u2192        <AuthProvider>\n   117\u2192          <SocialProvider>\n   118\u2192            <WouterRouter base={import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\\/$/, \"\")}>\n   119\u2192              <Router />\n   120\u2192            </WouterRouter>\n   121\u2192          </SocialProvider>\n   122\u2192        </AuthProvider>\n   123\u2192      </ThemeProvider>\n   124\u2192    </QueryClientProvider>\n   125\u2192  );\n   126\u2192}\n   127\u2192\n   128\u2192export default App;\n   129\u2192"}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Here's the result of running `cat -n` on a snippet of artifacts/animal-x/src/pages/Profile.jsx (lines 279-578 of 829)\n   279\u2192        </button>\n   280\u2192        <button className=\"qs-pill\" onClick={toggleTheme}>\n   281\u2192          {theme === \"dark\" ? \"\u2600\ufe0f Light Mode\" : \"\ud83c\udf19 Dark Mode\"}\n   282\u2192        </button>\n   283\u2192        <button className=\"qs-pill\" onClick={() => setHelpOpen(true)}>\u2753 Help & Support</button>\n   284\u2192        <button className=\"qs-pill qs-logout\" onClick={logout}>\u21aa Log out</button>\n   285\u2192      </div>\n   286\u2192\n   287\u2192      {helpOpen && (\n   288\u2192        <div className=\"edit-modal-backdrop\" onClick={() => setHelpOpen(false)} role=\"dialog\" aria-modal=\"true\">\n   289\u2192          <div className=\"edit-modal\" onClick={(e) => e.stopPropagation()}>\n   290\u2192            <div className=\"edit-modal-head\">\n   291\u2192              <h3>\u2753 Help & Support</h3>\n   292\u2192              <button type=\"button\" className=\"edit-modal-close\" onClick={() => setHelpOpen(false)} aria-label=\"Close\">\u2715</button>\n   293\u2192            </div>\n   294\u2192            <div className=\"edit-modal-body\">\n   295\u2192              <div className=\"help-section\">\n   296\u2192                <h4 className=\"help-section-title\">Connect With Us</h4>\n   297\u2192                <p className=\"help-section-sub\">Reach out \u2014 we read every message.</p>\n   298\u2192\n   299\u2192                <a\n   300\u2192                  className=\"help-contact-row\"\n   301\u2192                  href=\"fb://facewebmodal/f?href=https://www.facebook.com/wild_life_aniaml_fight\"\n   302\u2192                  onClick={(e) => {\n   303\u2192                    e.preventDefault();\n   304\u2192                    const fallback = \"https://www.facebook.com/wild_life_aniaml_fight\";\n   305\u2192                    const start = Date.now();\n   306\u2192                    setTimeout(() => {\n   307\u2192                      if (Date.now() - start < 1700) window.open(fallback, \"_blank\", \"noopener\");\n   308\u2192                    }, 1300);\n   309\u2192                    try { window.location.href = \"fb://facewebmodal/f?href=https://www.facebook.com/wild_life_aniaml_fight\"; }\n   310\u2192                    catch { window.open(fallback, \"_blank\", \"noopener\"); }\n   311\u2192                  }}\n   312\u2192                >\n   313\u2192                  <span className=\"help-icon\" style={{ background: \"#1877f2\" }} aria-hidden>\n   314\u2192                    <svg width=\"22\" height=\"22\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"#fff\">\n   315\u2192                      <path d=\"M22 12.06C22 6.5 17.52 2 12 2S2 6.5 2 12.06c0 5 3.66 9.15 8.44 9.94v-7.03H7.9v-2.91h2.54V9.84c0-2.51 1.5-3.9 3.78-3.9 1.1 0 2.24.2 2.24.2v2.46h-1.26c-1.24 0-1.63.77-1.63 1.56v1.88h2.78l-.45 2.91h-2.33V22c4.78-.79 8.43-4.94 8.43-9.94z\" />\n   316\u2192                    </svg>\n   317\u2192                  </span>\n   318\u2192                  <div className=\"help-contact-info\">\n   319\u2192                    <div className=\"help-contact-name\">Facebook</div>\n   320\u2192                    <div className=\"help-contact-handle\">wild_life_aniaml_fight</div>\n   321\u2192                  </div>\n   322\u2192                  <span className=\"help-arrow\">\u2192</span>\n   323\u2192                </a>\n   324\u2192\n   325\u2192                <a\n   326\u2192                  className=\"help-contact-row\"\n   327\u2192                  href=\"instagram://user?username=wildlifeaniamlfight\"\n   328\u2192                  onClick={(e) => {\n   329\u2192                    e.preventDefault();\n   330\u2192                    const fallback = \"https://www.instagram.com/wildlifeaniamlfight\";\n   331\u2192                    const start = Date.now();\n   332\u2192                    setTimeout(() => {\n   333\u2192                      if (Date.now() - start < 1700) window.open(fallback, \"_blank\", \"noopener\");\n   334\u2192                    }, 1300);\n   335\u2192                    try { window.location.href = \"instagram://user?username=wildlifeaniamlfight\"; }\n   336\u2192                    catch { window.open(fallback, \"_blank\", \"noopener\"); }\n   337\u2192                  }}\n   338\u2192                >\n   339\u2192                  <span className=\"help-icon\" style={{ background: \"linear-gradient(135deg,#f09433,#e6683c,#dc2743,#cc2366,#bc1888)\" }} aria-hidden>\n   340\u2192                    <svg width=\"22\" height=\"22\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#fff\" strokeWidth=\"2.2\" strokeLinecap=\"round\" strokeLinejoin=\"round\">\n   341\u2192                      <rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"5\" />\n   342\u2192                      <circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"4\" />\n   343\u2192                      <circle cx=\"17.5\" cy=\"6.5\" r=\"1\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"none\" />\n   344\u2192                    </svg>\n   345\u2192                  </span>\n   346\u2192                  <div className=\"help-contact-info\">\n   347\u2192                    <div className=\"help-contact-name\">Instagram</div>\n   348\u2192                    <div className=\"help-contact-handle\">@wildlifeaniamlfight</div>\n   349\u2192                  </div>\n   350\u2192                  <span className=\"help-arrow\">\u2192</span>\n   351\u2192                </a>\n   352\u2192\n   353\u2192                <a\n   354\u2192                  className=\"help-contact-row\"\n   355\u2192                  href=\"mailto:wildlifeanimalfight@gmail.com?subject=Animal%20X%20Support%20Request\"\n   356\u2192                >\n   357\u2192                  <span className=\"help-icon\" style={{ background: \"#ea4335\" }} aria-hidden>\n   358\u2192                    <svg width=\"22\" height=\"22\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#fff\" strokeWidth=\"2.2\" strokeLinecap=\"round\" strokeLinejoin=\"round\">\n   359\u2192                      <rect x=\"3\" y=\"5\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" rx=\"2\" />\n   360\u2192                      <path d=\"m3 7 9 6 9-6\" />\n   361\u2192                    </svg>\n   362\u2192                  </span>\n   363\u2192                  <div className=\"help-contact-info\">\n   364\u2192                    <div className=\"help-contact-name\">Gmail</div>\n   365\u2192                    <div className=\"help-contact-handle\">wildlifeanimalfight@gmail.com</div>\n   366\u2192                  </div>\n   367\u2192                  \n   368\u2192                  <span className=\"help-arrow\">\u2192</span>\n   369\u2192                </a>\n   370\u2192              </div>\n   371\u2192            </div>\n   372\u2192              {/* --- FULL WIDTH VERTICAL LAYOUT FOR FAQS & PRIVACY --- */}\n   373\u2192  <div className=\"w-full mt-6 block clear-both text-left\" style={{ width: '100%', display: 'block', clear: 'both' }}>\n   374\u2192    \n   375\u2192    {/* --- Extra Troubleshooting FAQs --- */}\n   376\u2192        {/* --- Accordion FAQ Section (Click to Open) --- */}\n   377\u2192    \n   378\u2192\n   379\u2192    {/* --- PROFESSIONAL PRIVACY POLICY & COMMUNITY RULES --- */}\n   380\u2192    <div className=\"mt-6 border-t border-gray-100 pt-4 text-left block w-full\">\n   381\u2192      <h3 className=\"text-sm font-bold text-gray-800 mb-3 flex items-center gap-1\">\n   382\u2192        \ud83d\udd12 Privacy Policy & Community Guidelines\n   383\u2192      </h3>\n   384\u2192      \n   385\u2192      <div className=\"p-4 bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl border border-gray-100 max-h-60 overflow-y-auto space-y-3 block w-full\">\n   386\u2192        \n   387\u2192        <div className=\"block w-full\">\n   388\u2192          <h4 className=\"text-xs font-bold text-emerald-600 mb-1\">1. Data Privacy & Security</h4>\n   389\u2192          <p className=\"text-[11px] text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\">\n   390\u2192            Animal X securely stores your personal details (Gmail, Profile Data) and location permissions on Firebase Encrypted Servers. Your data is strictly confidential and is never shared with any third-party applications.\n   391\u2192          </p>\n   392\u2192        </div>\n   393\u2192\n   394\u2192        <div className=\"block w-full\">\n   395\u2192          <h4 className=\"text-xs font-bold text-emerald-600 mb-1\">2. Strict Content Moderation Rules</h4>\n   396\u2192          <p className=\"text-[11px] text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\">\n   397\u2192            Only content related to Wildlife, Animals, Forests, Oceans, Mountains, and Nature is allowed on this platform (Reels/Stories/Posts). AI filters and Admin panels constantly monitor all active feeds.\n   398\u2192          </p>\n   399\u2192        </div>\n   400\u2192\n   401\u2192        <div className=\"block w-full\">\n   402\u2192          <h4 className=\"text-xs font-bold text-red-500 mb-1\">3. Strike Policy & Account Blocks</h4>\n   403\u2192          <p className=\"text-[11px] text-gray-600 leading-relaxed font-semibold\">\n   404\u2192            \u26a0\ufe0f If a user violates the community guidelines and uploads inappropriate content, their account will receive warnings (strikes). Violating the content rules 3 times (3 Violations) will result in a temporary or permanent feature block, restricting the user from uploading Reels or Stories for 30 days or indefinitely.\n   405\u2192          </p>\n   406\u2192        </div>\n   407\u2192\n   408\u2192        <div className=\"block w-full\">\n   409\u2192          <h4 className=\"text-xs font-bold text-emerald-600 mb-1\">4. Verification & Blue Ticks</h4>\n   410\u2192          <p className=\"text-[11px] text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\">\n   411\u2192            Our verification system is fully automated. Users will automatically receive a verified Blue Tick upon reaching 100K (100,000) followers. Additionally, for core community safety and authentication, the App Admin reserves the right to manually verify accounts from the hidden admin panel.\n   412\u2192          </p>\n   413\u2192        </div>\n   414\u2192\n   415\u2192        <p className=\"text-[10px] text-gray-400 text-center pt-2 border-t border-gray-200/50 block w-full\">\n   416\u2192          Last Updated: May 2026 \u2022 Animal X Team\n   417\u2192        </p>\n   418\u2192\n   419\u2192      </div>\n   420\u2192    </div>\n   421\u2192\n   422\u2192  </div>\n   423\u2192\n   424\u2192          </div>\n   425\u2192        </div>\n   426\u2192      )}\n   427\u2192\n   428\u2192      {editProfileOpen && (\n   429\u2192        <div className=\"edit-profile-card\">\n   430\u2192          <h3>Edit Profile</h3>\n   431\u2192          <div className=\"ep-photo-row\">\n   432\u2192            <div\n   433\u2192              className=\"ep-photo-preview\"\n   434\u2192              style={photoUrl ? { backgroundImage: `url(${photoUrl})` } : undefined}\n   435\u2192            >\n   436\u2192              {!photoUrl && initial}\n   437\u2192            </div>\n   438\u2192            <div style={{ flex: 1 }}>\n   439\u2192              <label className=\"btn-primary\" style={{ cursor: \"pointer\", display: \"inline-block\" }}>\n   440\u2192                \ud83d\udcf7 Upload New Photo\n   441\u2192                <input\n   442\u2192                  type=\"file\"\n   443\u2192                  accept=\"image/*\"\n   444\u2192                  style={{ display: \"none\" }}\n   445\u2192                  onChange={handleProfilePhoto}\n   446\u2192                />\n   447\u2192              </label>\n   448\u2192              {profile.photo && (\n   449\u2192                <button\n   450\u2192                  className=\"qs-pill\"\n   451\u2192                  style={{ marginLeft: 8 }}\n   452\u2192                  onClick={() => updateProfile({ photo: null })}\n   453\u2192                >\n   454\u2192                  Remove\n   455\u2192                </button>\n   456\u2192              )}\n   457\u2192            </div>\n   458\u2192          </div>\n   459\u2192          <div className=\"aef-row\">\n   460\u2192            <label>Display Name</label>\n   461\u2192            <input\n   462\u2192              type=\"text\"\n   463\u2192              value={nameInput}\n   464\u2192              onChange={(e) => setNameInput(e.target.value)}\n   465\u2192              placeholder=\"Your display name\"\n   466\u2192            />\n   467\u2192          </div>\n   468\u2192          <div style={{ display: \"flex\", gap: 8 }}>\n   469\u2192            <button className=\"btn-primary\" onClick={saveProfileEdits}>Save</button>\n   470\u2192            <button className=\"qs-pill\" onClick={() => setEditProfileOpen(false)}>Cancel</button>\n   471\u2192          </div>\n   472\u2192        </div>\n   473\u2192      )}\n   474\u2192\n   475\u2192      <div className=\"profile-tabs\">\n   476\u2192        <button className={`pt-tab ${tab === \"grid\" ? \"active\" : \"\"}`} onClick={() => setTab(\"grid\")}>\ud83d\udcf7 Grid</button>\n   477\u2192        <button className={`pt-tab ${tab === \"reels\" ? \"active\" : \"\"}`} onClick={() => setTab(\"reels\")}>\ud83c\udfac Reels</button>\n   478\u2192        <button className={`pt-tab ${tab === \"tagged\" ? \"active\" : \"\"}`} onClick={() => setTab(\"tagged\")}>\ud83c\udff7\ufe0f Tagged</button>\n   479\u2192      </div>\n   480\u2192\n   481\u2192      <div className=\"profile-tab-body\">\n   482\u2192        {tab === \"grid\" && (\n   483\u2192          <div className=\"profile-grid-empty\">\n   484\u2192            <div style={{ fontSize: 48 }}>\ud83d\udcf7</div>\n   485\u2192            <p>You have {profile.posts} posts. Upload from the Reels page \u2192 Posts tab.</p>\n   486\u2192            <Link href=\"/reels\" className=\"btn-primary\" style={{ marginTop: 12 }}>Go to Posts</Link>\n   487\u2192          </div>\n   488\u2192        )}\n   489\u2192        {tab === \"reels\" && (\n   490\u2192          <div className=\"profile-grid-empty\">\n   491\u2192            <div style={{ fontSize: 48 }}>\ud83c\udfac</div>\n   492\u2192            <p>You have {profile.reels} reels. Upload from the Reels page.</p>\n   493\u2192            <Link href=\"/reels\" className=\"btn-primary\" style={{ marginTop: 12 }}>Go to Reels</Link>\n   494\u2192          </div>\n   495\u2192        )}\n   496\u2192        {tab === \"tagged\" && (\n   497\u2192          <div className=\"profile-grid-empty\">\n   498\u2192            <div style={{ fontSize: 48 }}>\ud83c\udff7\ufe0f</div>\n   499\u2192            <p>No one has tagged you yet.</p>\n   500\u2192          </div>\n   501\u2192        )}\n   502\u2192      </div>\n   503\u2192\n   504\u2192      {adminMode && isSuperAdmin && (\n   505\u2192        <div className=\"admin-panel\">\n   506\u2192          <div className=\"admin-header\">\n   507\u2192            <h2>\ud83d\udc51 Admin Panel</h2>\n   508\u2192            <button className=\"qs-pill\" onClick={lockAdminMode}>Lock Admin Mode</button>\n   509\u2192          </div>\n   510\u2192\n   511\u2192          <div className=\"admin-section\">\n   512\u2192            <h3>\u2795 Add New Animal</h3>\n   513\u2192            <div className=\"aef-row\">\n   514\u2192              <label>Name *</label>\n   515\u2192              <input\n   516\u2192                type=\"text\"\n   517\u2192                placeholder=\"e.g. Spirit Lion\"\n   518\u2192                value={newName}\n   519\u2192                onChange={(e) => setNewName(e.target.value)}\n   520\u2192              />\n   521\u2192            </div>\n   522\u2192            <div className=\"aef-row\">\n   523\u2192              <label>Category</label>\n   524\u2192              <select\n   525\u2192                value={newCategory}\n   526\u2192                onChange={(e) => setNewCategory(e.target.value)}\n   527\u2192                className=\"admin-input\"\n   528\u2192                style={{ width: \"100%\" }}\n   529\u2192              >\n   530\u2192                {categories.map((c) => <option key={c} value={c}>{c}</option>)}\n   531\u2192              </select>\n   532\u2192            </div>\n   533\u2192            <div className=\"aef-row\">\n   534\u2192              <label>Image</label>\n   535\u2192              <input\n   536\u2192                ref={photoFileRef}\n   537\u2192                type=\"file\"\n   538\u2192                accept=\"image/*\"\n   539\u2192                onChange={handleNewAnimalImage}\n   540\u2192              />\n   541\u2192              {newImage && (\n   542\u2192                <img\n   543\u2192                  src={newImage}\n   544\u2192                  alt=\"preview\"\n   545\u2192                  style={{ marginTop: 8, maxWidth: 160, borderRadius: 8, border: \"2px solid var(--accent)\" }}\n   546\u2192                />\n   547\u2192              )}\n   548\u2192            </div>\n   549\u2192            <div className=\"aef-row\">\n   550\u2192              <label>Habits / Habitat</label>\n   551\u2192              <textarea\n   552\u2192                rows={2}\n   553\u2192                placeholder=\"e.g. Nocturnal apex predator that lives in prides...\"\n   554\u2192                value={newHabits}\n   555\u2192                onChange={(e) => setNewHabits(e.target.value)}\n   556\u2192              />\n   557\u2192            </div>\n   558\u2192            <div className=\"aef-row\">\n   559\u2192              <label>Lifespan</label>\n   560\u2192              <input\n   561\u2192                type=\"text\"\n   562\u2192                placeholder=\"e.g. 12\u201316 years wild\"\n   563\u2192                value={newLifespan}\n   564\u2192                onChange={(e) => setNewLifespan(e.target.value)}\n   565\u2192              />\n   566\u2192            </div>\n   567\u2192            <div className=\"aef-row\">\n   568\u2192              <label>Country / Region</label>\n   569\u2192              <input\n   570\u2192                type=\"text\"\n   571\u2192                placeholder=\"e.g. Kenya\"\n   572\u2192                value={newCountry}\n   573\u2192                onChange={(e) => setNewCountry(e.target.value)}\n   574\u2192              />\n   575\u2192            </div>\n   576\u2192            <button className=\"btn-primary\" onClick={submitNewAnimal}>\n   577\u2192              \u2713 Add Animal to App\n   578\u2192            </button>"}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Here's the result of running `cat -n` on a snippet of artifacts/animal-x/src/context/AuthContext.jsx (lines 1-60 of 175)\n     1\u2192import { createContext, useContext, useState, useEffect } from \"react\";\n     2\u2192import {\n     3\u2192  createUserWithEmailAndPassword,\n     4\u2192  signInWithEmailAndPassword,\n     5\u2192  signOut,\n     6\u2192  onAuthStateChanged,\n     7\u2192  updateProfile as fbUpdateProfile,\n     8\u2192  sendPasswordResetEmail,\n     9\u2192} from \"firebase/auth\";\n    10\u2192import { doc, getDoc, setDoc, updateDoc, serverTimestamp } from \"firebase/firestore\";\n    11\u2192import { auth, db } from \"../utils/firebase\";\n    12\u2192\n    13\u2192const AuthContext = createContext(null);\n    14\u2192\n    15\u2192const SUPER_ADMIN_EMAIL = \"malinotaling8@gmail.com\";\n    16\u2192\n    17\u2192const DEFAULT_PROFILE = {\n    18\u2192  followers: 0,\n    19\u2192  following: 0,\n    20\u2192  posts: 0,\n    21\u2192  reels: 0,\n    22\u2192  manualVerified: false,\n    23\u2192  autoGrow: false,\n    24\u2192  bio: \"\",\n    25\u2192  country: \"\",\n    26\u2192};\n    27\u2192\n    28\u2192export function AuthProvider({ children }) {\n    29\u2192  const [user, setUser] = useState(null);\n    30\u2192  const [profile, setProfile] = useState(DEFAULT_PROFILE);\n    31\u2192  const [adminMode, setAdminMode] = useState(false);\n    32\u2192  const [authLoading, setAuthLoading] = useState(true);\n    33\u2192\n    34\u2192  useEffect(() => {\n    35\u2192    const unsub = onAuthStateChanged(auth, async (fbUser) => {\n    36\u2192      if (fbUser) {\n    37\u2192        const u = {\n    38\u2192          uid: fbUser.uid,\n    39\u2192          email: fbUser.email,\n    40\u2192          name: fbUser.displayName || fbUser.email.split(\"@\")[0],\n    41\u2192        };\n    42\u2192        setUser(u);\n    43\u2192        try {\n    44\u2192          const snap = await getDoc(doc(db, \"users\", fbUser.uid));\n    45\u2192          if (snap.exists()) {\n    46\u2192            setProfile({ ...DEFAULT_PROFILE, ...snap.data() });\n    47\u2192          } else {\n    48\u2192            const fresh = {\n    49\u2192              ...DEFAULT_PROFILE,\n    50\u2192              name: u.name,\n    51\u2192              email: u.email,\n    52\u2192              createdAt: serverTimestamp(),\n    53\u2192            };\n    54\u2192            await setDoc(doc(db, \"users\", fbUser.uid), fresh);\n    55\u2192            setProfile(fresh);\n    56\u2192          }\n    57\u2192        } catch {\n    58\u2192          setProfile(DEFAULT_PROFILE);\n    59\u2192        }\n    60\u2192        if (sessionStorage.getItem(\"ax_admin_mode\") === \"true\") setAdminMode(true);"}]}]}
{"memory_id": 376, "messages": [{"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Let me read the remaining files I need before writing:"}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": [], "tool_calls": [{"type": "tool", "name": "read", "arguments": {"file_path": "artifacts/animal-x/src/components/Navbar.jsx"}}, {"type": "tool", "name": "read", "arguments": {"file_path": "artifacts/animal-x/src/pages/Profile.jsx", "offset": 578, "limit": 252}}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Here's the result of running `cat -n` on a snippet of artifacts/animal-x/src/components/Navbar.jsx\n     1\u2192import { useState, useRef } from \"react\";\n     2\u2192import { Link, useLocation } from \"wouter\";\n     3\u2192import { useAuth } from \"../context/AuthContext\";\n     4\u2192import { useSocial } from \"../context/SocialContext\";\n     5\u2192import NotificationBell from \"./NotificationBell\";\n     6\u2192import AdminDebugPanel from \"./AdminDebugPanel\";\n     7\u2192\n     8\u2192const bottomItems = [\n     9\u2192  { href: \"/\", label: \"Home\", icon: \"\ud83c\udfe0\" },\n    10\u2192  { href: \"/animals\", label: \"Animals\", icon: \"\ud83d\udc3e\" },\n    11\u2192  { href: \"/reels\", label: \"Reels\", icon: \"\ud83c\udfac\" },\n    12\u2192  { href: \"/map\", label: \"Map\", icon: \"\ud83d\uddfa\ufe0f\" },\n    13\u2192  { href: \"/travel\", label: \"Travel\", icon: \"\u2708\ufe0f\" },\n    14\u2192  { href: \"/profile\", label: \"Profile\", icon: \"\ud83d\udc64\" },\n    15\u2192];\n    16\u2192\n    17\u2192export default function Navbar() {\n    18\u2192  const [location, navigate] = useLocation();\n    19\u2192  const { user, isSuperAdmin, adminMode, unlockAdminMode, lockAdminMode } = useAuth();\n    20\u2192  const { broadcast, dismissBroadcast, sendBroadcast } = useSocial();\n    21\u2192  const [searchValue, setSearchValue] = useState(\"\");\n    22\u2192  const [tapCount, setTapCount] = useState(0);\n    23\u2192  const [broadcastOpen, setBroadcastOpen] = useState(false);\n    24\u2192  const [broadcastMsg, setBroadcastMsg] = useState(\"\");\n    25\u2192  const [debugOpen, setDebugOpen] = useState(false);\n    26\u2192  const tapTimer = useRef(null);\n    27\u2192  const searchInputRef = useRef(null);\n    28\u2192\n    29\u2192  function submitSearch(e) {\n    30\u2192    e.preventDefault();\n    31\u2192    const q = searchValue.trim();\n    32\u2192    if (!q) return;\n    33\u2192    // If query looks like a username (@...) or search intent, go to user search\n    34\u2192    navigate(`/search?q=${encodeURIComponent(q)}`);\n    35\u2192    setSearchValue(\"\");\n    36\u2192    searchInputRef.current?.blur();\n    37\u2192  }\n    38\u2192\n    39\u2192  function handleLogoTap() {\n    40\u2192    const next = tapCount + 1;\n    41\u2192    setTapCount(next);\n    42\u2192    if (tapTimer.current) clearTimeout(tapTimer.current);\n    43\u2192    tapTimer.current = setTimeout(() => setTapCount(0), 1500);\n    44\u2192    if (next >= 7) {\n    45\u2192      setTapCount(0);\n    46\u2192      if (!user) { alert(\"Please login first.\"); return; }\n    47\u2192      if (!isSuperAdmin) { alert(\"Admin access restricted.\"); return; }\n    48\u2192      if (!adminMode) unlockAdminMode();\n    49\u2192      setBroadcastOpen(v => !v);\n    50\u2192    }\n    51\u2192  }\n    52\u2192\n    53\u2192  async function handleSendBroadcast() {\n    54\u2192    if (!broadcastMsg.trim()) return;\n    55\u2192    await sendBroadcast(broadcastMsg.trim());\n    56\u2192    setBroadcastMsg(\"\");\n    57\u2192    setBroadcastOpen(false);\n    58\u2192    alert(\"\u2705 Broadcast sent to all users!\");\n    59\u2192  }\n    60\u2192\n    61\u2192  return (\n    62\u2192    <>\n    63\u2192      {broadcast && (\n    64\u2192        <div className=\"broadcast-banner\">\n    65\u2192          <span className=\"broadcast-icon\">\ud83d\udce2</span>\n    66\u2192          <span className=\"broadcast-msg\">{broadcast.message}</span>\n    67\u2192          <button className=\"broadcast-dismiss\" onClick={() => dismissBroadcast(broadcast.id)}>\u2715</button>\n    68\u2192        </div>\n    69\u2192      )}\n    70\u2192\n    71\u2192      <header className=\"topbar\">\n    72\u2192        <button className=\"brand-link\" onClick={handleLogoTap} style={{ background:\"none\", border:\"none\", cursor:\"pointer\" }}>\n    73\u2192          <span className=\"brand-icon\">\ud83e\udd81</span>\n    74\u2192          <span className=\"brand-name\">Animal X</span>\n    75\u2192        </button>\n    76\u2192\n    77\u2192        <form className=\"topbar-search\" onSubmit={submitSearch} role=\"search\">\n    78\u2192          <span className=\"topbar-search-icon\">\ud83d\udd0d</span>\n    79\u2192          <input\n    80\u2192            ref={searchInputRef}\n    81\u2192            type=\"search\"\n    82\u2192            value={searchValue}\n    83\u2192            onChange={e => setSearchValue(e.target.value)}\n    84\u2192            placeholder=\"Search animals or @users\u2026\"\n    85\u2192            aria-label=\"Search\"\n    86\u2192          />\n    87\u2192        </form>\n    88\u2192\n    89\u2192        <div className=\"topbar-actions\">\n    90\u2192          <Link href=\"/search\" className=\"topbar-search-btn\" title=\"Search creators\">\ud83d\udc65</Link>\n    91\u2192          <NotificationBell />\n    92\u2192          {adminMode && isSuperAdmin && (\n    93\u2192            <button className=\"debug-panel-btn\" onClick={() => setDebugOpen(true)} title=\"Firebase Debug Panel\">\ud83d\udee0\ufe0f</button>\n    94\u2192          )}\n    95\u2192          {!user && (\n    96\u2192            <Link href=\"/auth\" className=\"top-pill top-pill-primary\" title=\"Login\">Login</Link>\n    97\u2192          )}\n    98\u2192        </div>\n    99\u2192      </header>\n   100\u2192\n   101\u2192      {broadcastOpen && isSuperAdmin && adminMode && (\n   102\u2192        <div className=\"broadcast-panel\">\n   103\u2192          <div className=\"broadcast-panel-head\">\n   104\u2192            <span>\ud83d\udce2 Admin Broadcast</span>\n   105\u2192            <div style={{ display:\"flex\", gap:8 }}>\n   106\u2192              <button onClick={() => setDebugOpen(true)}\n   107\u2192                style={{ background:\"rgba(168,85,247,.2)\", border:\"1px solid #a855f7\", color:\"#a855f7\", padding:\"4px 10px\", borderRadius:8, cursor:\"pointer\", fontSize:\"0.78rem\" }}>\n   108\u2192                \ud83d\udee0\ufe0f Debug\n   109\u2192              </button>\n   110\u2192              <button onClick={() => setBroadcastOpen(false)}>\u2715</button>\n   111\u2192            </div>\n   112\u2192          </div>\n   113\u2192          <div className=\"broadcast-panel-body\">\n   114\u2192            <textarea className=\"broadcast-input\" rows={3}\n   115\u2192              placeholder=\"Type a message for ALL users...\"\n   116\u2192              value={broadcastMsg} onChange={e => setBroadcastMsg(e.target.value)} />\n   117\u2192            <div className=\"broadcast-panel-actions\">\n   118\u2192              <button className=\"auth-btn\" style={{ background:\"var(--surface2)\", flex:1 }}\n   119\u2192                onClick={() => { lockAdminMode(); setBroadcastOpen(false); }}>\n   120\u2192                \ud83d\udd12 Lock Admin\n   121\u2192              </button>\n   122\u2192              <button className=\"auth-btn\" style={{ flex:1 }} onClick={handleSendBroadcast}\n   123\u2192                disabled={!broadcastMsg.trim()}>\n   124\u2192                \ud83d\udce2 Send to All\n   125\u2192              </button>\n   126\u2192            </div>\n   127\u2192          </div>\n   128\u2192        </div>\n   129\u2192      )}\n   130\u2192\n   131\u2192      <AdminDebugPanel open={debugOpen} onClose={() => setDebugOpen(false)} />\n   132\u2192\n   133\u2192      <nav className=\"bottom-nav\">\n   134\u2192        {bottomItems.map((item) => {\n   135\u2192          const active = item.href === \"/\" ? location === \"/\" : location === item.href || location.startsWith(item.href + \"/\");\n   136\u2192          return (\n   137\u2192            <Link key={item.href} href={item.href} className={`bn-item ${active ? \"active\" : \"\"}`}>\n   138\u2192              <span className=\"bn-icon\">{item.icon}</span>\n   139\u2192              <span className=\"bn-label\">{item.label}</span>\n   140\u2192            </Link>\n   141\u2192          );\n   142\u2192        })}\n   143\u2192      </nav>\n   144\u2192    </>\n   145\u2192  );\n   146\u2192}\n   147\u2192"}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Here's the result of running `cat -n` on a snippet of artifacts/animal-x/src/pages/Profile.jsx (lines 578-829 of 829)\n   578\u2192            </button>\n   579\u2192            {customAnimals.length > 0 && (\n   580\u2192              <div style={{ marginTop: 16 }}>\n   581\u2192                <p className=\"admin-hint\">Custom animals you've added ({customAnimals.length}):</p>\n   582\u2192                <div className=\"custom-animals-list\">\n   583\u2192                  {customAnimals.map((a) => (\n   584\u2192                    <div key={a.id} className=\"custom-animal-row\">\n   585\u2192                      {a.image\n   586\u2192                        ? <img src={a.image} alt={a.name} className=\"ca-thumb\" />\n   587\u2192                        : <div className=\"ca-thumb ca-thumb-empty\">\ud83d\udc3e</div>}\n   588\u2192                      <div className=\"ca-info\">\n   589\u2192                        <div className=\"ca-name\">{a.name}</div>\n   590\u2192                        <div className=\"ca-meta\">{a.category} \u00b7 {a.country}</div>\n   591\u2192                      </div>\n   592\u2192                      <button className=\"qs-pill qs-logout\" onClick={() => removeCustom(a.id, a.name)}>\u2715</button>\n   593\u2192                    </div>\n   594\u2192                  ))}\n   595\u2192                </div>\n   596\u2192              </div>\n   597\u2192            )}\n   598\u2192          </div>\n   599\u2192\n   600\u2192          <div className=\"admin-section\">\n   601\u2192            <h3>\ud83d\udcc8 Follower Booster</h3>\n   602\u2192            <div className=\"admin-row\">\n   603\u2192              <input\n   604\u2192                type=\"text\"\n   605\u2192                placeholder=\"e.g. 50k, 1M, 250000\"\n   606\u2192                value={followersInput}\n   607\u2192                onChange={(e) => setFollowersInput(e.target.value)}\n   608\u2192                className=\"admin-input\"\n   609\u2192              />\n   610\u2192              <button className=\"btn-primary\" onClick={applyFollowers}>Set Followers</button>\n   611\u2192            </div>\n   612\u2192            <p className=\"admin-hint\">Current: <b>{formatCount(profile.followers)}</b> \u00b7 Auto-verifies at 100K.</p>\n   613\u2192\n   614\u2192            <label className=\"admin-toggle\">\n   615\u2192              <input\n   616\u2192                type=\"checkbox\"\n   617\u2192                checked={!!profile.autoGrow}\n   618\u2192                onChange={(e) => updateProfile({ autoGrow: e.target.checked })}\n   619\u2192              />\n   620\u2192              <span>Auto-grow followers (+5\u201310 per app start)</span>\n   621\u2192            </label>\n   622\u2192\n   623\u2192            <label className=\"admin-toggle\">\n   624\u2192              <input\n   625\u2192                type=\"checkbox\"\n   626\u2192                checked={!!profile.manualVerified}\n   627\u2192                onChange={(e) => updateProfile({ manualVerified: e.target.checked })}\n   628\u2192              />\n   629\u2192              <span>\ud83d\udd35 Manual Blue Tick (override)</span>\n   630\u2192            </label>\n   631\u2192          </div>\n   632\u2192\n   633\u2192          <div className=\"admin-section\">\n   634\u2192            <h3>\ud83d\udcca Manual Stats</h3>\n   635\u2192            <div className=\"admin-row\">\n   636\u2192              <input type=\"number\" placeholder=\"Posts count\" value={postsInput} onChange={(e) => setPostsInput(e.target.value)} className=\"admin-input\" />\n   637\u2192              <button className=\"btn-primary\" onClick={applyPosts}>Set Posts</button>\n   638\u2192            </div>\n   639\u2192            <div className=\"admin-row\">\n   640\u2192              <input type=\"number\" placeholder=\"Reels count\" value={reelsInput} onChange={(e) => setReelsInput(e.target.value)} className=\"admin-input\" />\n   641\u2192              <button className=\"btn-primary\" onClick={applyReels}>Set Reels</button>\n   642\u2192            </div>\n   643\u2192          </div>\n   644\u2192\n   645\u2192          <div className=\"admin-section\">\n   646\u2192            <h3>\ud83d\udc65 User Management</h3>\n   647\u2192            <input\n   648\u2192              type=\"search\"\n   649\u2192              placeholder=\"Search by name, email, or UID\"\n   650\u2192              value={search}\n   651\u2192              onChange={(e) => setSearch(e.target.value)}\n   652\u2192              className=\"admin-input\"\n   653\u2192              style={{ width: \"100%\" }}\n   654\u2192            />\n   655\u2192            <div className=\"admin-user-list\">\n   656\u2192              {filteredUsers.length === 0 && <p className=\"admin-hint\">No users registered yet.</p>}\n   657\u2192              {filteredUsers.map((u) => {\n   658\u2192                const verified = !!verifiedMap[u.email] || !!verifiedMap[u.uid];\n   659\u2192                return (\n   660\u2192                  <div key={u.uid || u.email} className=\"admin-user-row\">\n   661\u2192                    <div className=\"adm-avatar\">{(u.name || u.email || \"?\")[0].toUpperCase()}</div>\n   662\u2192                    <div className=\"adm-info\">\n   663\u2192                      <div className=\"adm-name\">\n   664\u2192                        {u.name || \"(no name)\"}\n   665\u2192                        {verified && <BlueTick />}\n   666\u2192                      </div>\n   667\u2192                      <div className=\"adm-email\">{u.email}</div>\n   668\u2192                      <div className=\"adm-uid\">UID: {u.uid || \"\u2014\"}</div>\n   669\u2192                    </div>\n   670\u2192                    <div className=\"adm-actions\">\n   671\u2192                      <button className=\"qs-pill\" onClick={() => copyText(u.email)}>Copy Email</button>\n   672\u2192                      <button className=\"qs-pill\" onClick={() => copyText(u.uid || \"\")}>Copy UID</button>\n   673\u2192                      <label className=\"adm-switch\">\n   674\u2192                        <input\n   675\u2192                          type=\"checkbox\"\n   676\u2192                          checked={verified}\n   677\u2192                          onChange={(e) => setVerifiedFor(u.email, e.target.checked)}\n   678\u2192                        />\n   679\u2192                        <span>Verified</span>\n   680\u2192                      </label>\n   681\u2192                    </div>\n   682\u2192                  </div>\n   683\u2192                );\n   684\u2192              })}\n   685\u2192            </div>\n   686\u2192            <p className=\"admin-hint\">Sensitive emails are visible only to the super admin ({SUPER_ADMIN_EMAIL}).</p>\n   687\u2192          </div>\n   688\u2192\n   689\u2192          <div className=\"admin-section\">\n   690\u2192            <h3>\ud83d\udeab Ban / Strike Management</h3>\n   691\u2192            <AdminBanPanel />\n   692\u2192          </div>\n   693\u2192\n   694\u2192          <div className=\"admin-section\">\n   695\u2192            <h3>\ud83d\udccb Moderation Log</h3>\n   696\u2192            <AdminModerationLog />\n   697\u2192          </div>\n   698\u2192        </div>\n   699\u2192      )}\n   700\u2192    </div>\n   701\u2192  );\n   702\u2192}\n   703\u2192\n   704\u2192function AdminBanPanel() {\n   705\u2192  const [uid, setUid] = useState(\"\");\n   706\u2192  const [reason, setReason] = useState(\"\");\n   707\u2192  const [result, setResult] = useState(null);\n   708\u2192  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(false);\n   709\u2192\n   710\u2192  async function handleBan(action) {\n   711\u2192    if (!uid.trim()) { alert(\"Enter a user UID to \" + action); return; }\n   712\u2192    setLoading(true);\n   713\u2192    try {\n   714\u2192      const { doc, setDoc, getDoc } = await import(\"firebase/firestore\");\n   715\u2192      const { db } = await import(\"../utils/firebase\");\n   716\u2192      if (action === \"ban\") {\n   717\u2192        await setDoc(doc(db, \"userStrikes\", uid.trim()), {\n   718\u2192          banned: true, banReason: reason || \"Admin action\",\n   719\u2192          bannedAt: Date.now(), strikes: 3,\n   720\u2192        }, { merge: true });\n   721\u2192        await setDoc(doc(db, \"users\", uid.trim()), { banned: true }, { merge: true });\n   722\u2192        setResult({ ok: true, msg: `\u2705 User ${uid.trim()} banned.` });\n   723\u2192      } else if (action === \"unban\") {\n   724\u2192        await setDoc(doc(db, \"userStrikes\", uid.trim()), { banned: false, strikes: 0, bannedAt: null }, { merge: true });\n   725\u2192        await setDoc(doc(db, \"users\", uid.trim()), { banned: false }, { merge: true });\n   726\u2192        setResult({ ok: true, msg: `\u2705 User ${uid.trim()} unbanned.` });\n   727\u2192      } else if (action === \"strike\") {\n   728\u2192        const snap = await getDoc(doc(db, \"userStrikes\", uid.trim()));\n   729\u2192        const cur = snap.exists() ? snap.data().strikes || 0 : 0;\n   730\u2192        const next = Math.min(cur + 1, 3);\n   731\u2192        await setDoc(doc(db, \"userStrikes\", uid.trim()), {\n   732\u2192          strikes: next, banned: next >= 3,\n   733\u2192          lastStrikeAt: Date.now(), lastReason: reason || \"Content violation\",\n   734\u2192        }, { merge: true });\n   735\u2192        setResult({ ok: true, msg: `\u26a0\ufe0f Strike added (${next}/3) for user ${uid.trim()}.` });\n   736\u2192      }\n   737\u2192    } catch (e) {\n   738\u2192      setResult({ ok: false, msg: \"Error: \" + e.message });\n   739\u2192    }\n   740\u2192    setLoading(false);\n   741\u2192  }\n   742\u2192\n   743\u2192  return (\n   744\u2192    <div style={{ display: \"flex\", flexDirection: \"column\", gap: 10 }}>\n   745\u2192      <div className=\"admin-ban-row\">\n   746\u2192        <input\n   747\u2192          className=\"admin-ban-uid\"\n   748\u2192          placeholder=\"Firebase User UID\"\n   749\u2192          value={uid}\n   750\u2192          onChange={e => setUid(e.target.value)}\n   751\u2192        />\n   752\u2192      </div>\n   753\u2192      <div className=\"admin-ban-row\">\n   754\u2192        <input\n   755\u2192          className=\"admin-ban-uid\"\n   756\u2192          placeholder=\"Reason (optional)\"\n   757\u2192          value={reason}\n   758\u2192          onChange={e => setReason(e.target.value)}\n   759\u2192        />\n   760\u2192      </div>\n   761\u2192      <div style={{ display: \"flex\", gap: 8, flexWrap: \"wrap\" }}>\n   762\u2192        <button className=\"admin-ban-btn strike\" style={{ background: \"rgba(245,158,11,0.15)\", color: \"#f59e0b\", border: \"1px solid rgba(245,158,11,0.4)\", padding: \"7px 14px\", borderRadius: 8, fontWeight: 700, fontSize: \"0.8rem\", cursor: \"pointer\" }}\n   763\u2192          onClick={() => handleBan(\"strike\")} disabled={loading}>\u26a0\ufe0f Add Strike</button>\n   764\u2192        <button className=\"admin-ban-btn ban\" onClick={() => handleBan(\"ban\")} disabled={loading}>\ud83d\udeab Ban User</button>\n   765\u2192        <button className=\"admin-ban-btn unban\" onClick={() => handleBan(\"unban\")} disabled={loading}>\u2705 Unban User</button>\n   766\u2192      </div>\n   767\u2192      {result && <div className={`admin-ban-result ${result.ok ? \"\" : \"error\"}`}>{result.msg}</div>}\n   768\u2192      <p className=\"admin-hint\" style={{ marginTop: 4 }}>3 strikes = 30-day upload ban. Entering UID is required.</p>\n   769\u2192    </div>\n   770\u2192  );\n   771\u2192}\n   772\u2192\n   773\u2192function AdminModerationLog() {\n   774\u2192  const [logs, setLogs] = useState([]);\n   775\u2192  const [loaded, setLoaded] = useState(false);\n   776\u2192\n   777\u2192  async function fetchLogs() {\n   778\u2192    try {\n   779\u2192      const { collection, query, orderBy, limit, getDocs } = await import(\"firebase/firestore\");\n   780\u2192      const { db } = await import(\"../utils/firebase\");\n   781\u2192      const q = query(collection(db, \"moderationLog\"), orderBy(\"at\", \"desc\"), limit(30));\n   782\u2192      const snap = await getDocs(q);\n   783\u2192      setLogs(snap.docs.map(d => ({ id: d.id, ...d.data() })));\n   784\u2192    } catch {\n   785\u2192      setLogs([]);\n   786\u2192    }\n   787\u2192    setLoaded(true);\n   788\u2192  }\n   789\u2192\n   790\u2192  if (!loaded) {\n   791\u2192    return (\n   792\u2192      <button className=\"qs-pill\" onClick={fetchLogs}>\ud83d\udccb Load Moderation Log</button>\n   793\u2192    );\n   794\u2192  }\n   795\u2192\n   796\u2192  const DEMO_LOGS = [\n   797\u2192    { id: \"ml1\", type: \"strike\", action: \"Strike added (1/3)\", detail: \"User @wild_shooter \u2014 off-topic reel removed\", at: Date.now() - 3600000 },\n   798\u2192    { id: \"ml2\", type: \"remove\", action: \"Reel removed\", detail: \"Reel #ff23 flagged for non-wildlife content\", at: Date.now() - 7200000 },\n   799\u2192    { id: \"ml3\", type: \"ban\", action: \"User banned\", detail: \"User @spammer99 \u2014 3 strikes, upload ban applied\", at: Date.now() - 86400000 },\n   800\u2192    { id: \"ml4\", type: \"strike\", action: \"Strike added (2/3)\", detail: \"User @naturelover \u2014 music video without animals\", at: Date.now() - 172800000 },\n   801\u2192  ];\n   802\u2192\n   803\u2192  const allLogs = [...logs, ...(logs.length === 0 ? DEMO_LOGS : [])];\n   804\u2192\n   805\u2192  function timeAgo(ts) {\n   806\u2192    const diff = Date.now() - ts;\n   807\u2192    if (diff < 60000) return \"just now\";\n   808\u2192    if (diff < 3600000) return Math.floor(diff / 60000) + \"m ago\";\n   809\u2192    if (diff < 86400000) return Math.floor(diff / 3600000) + \"h ago\";\n   810\u2192    return Math.floor(diff / 86400000) + \"d ago\";\n   811\u2192  }\n   812\u2192\n   813\u2192  return (\n   814\u2192    <div className=\"admin-mod-log\">\n   815\u2192      {allLogs.length === 0 ? (\n   816\u2192        <div className=\"mod-log-empty\">No moderation actions yet.</div>\n   817\u2192      ) : (\n   818\u2192        allLogs.map(l => (\n   819\u2192          <div key={l.id} className={`mod-log-item ${l.type}`}>\n   820\u2192            <div className=\"mod-log-action\">{l.action || l.type}</div>\n   821\u2192            <div className=\"mod-log-detail\">{l.detail || l.reason || \"\u2014\"}</div>\n   822\u2192            <div className=\"mod-log-time\">{timeAgo(l.at || l.timestamp || Date.now())}</div>\n   823\u2192          </div>\n   824\u2192        ))\n   825\u2192      )}\n   826\u2192    </div>\n   827\u2192  );\n   828\u2192}\n   829\u2192"}]}]}
{"memory_id": 377, "messages": [{"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Now I have everything I need. Let me write a session plan and implement all changes in parallel:"}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": [], "tool_calls": [{"type": "tool", "name": "bash", "arguments": {"command": "cat artifacts/animal-x/src/styles/app.css | wc -l && tail -30 artifacts/animal-x/src/styles/app.css", "description": "Check CSS file length and end", "timeout": 5000}}, {"type": "tool", "name": "write", "arguments": {"file_path": ".local/session_plan.md", "content": "# Objective\nProduction-quality upgrade: fix Reels upload wizard, rebuild WildlifeAI with bone FAB + animated menu, policy pages, admin testing panel, profile improvements.\n\n# Tasks\n\n### T001: Fix UploadReel wizard (step 1\u21922 broken)\n- Fix: \"Post Anyway\" doesn't advance to step 2\n- Fix: warning hides footer Back/Next buttons\n- Add clean step validation\n- Video unmuted by default (with muted autoplay trick)\n- Files: UploadReel.jsx\n\n### T002: Rebuild WildlifeAI (buffalo bone FAB + animated menu + expanded KB)\n- \ud83e\uddb4 bone FAB \u2192 animated menu (8 items)\n- Menu: AI Chat, Help, Privacy, Terms, Guidelines, Contact, About, Report\n- ChatGPT-style chat UI\n- 80+ KB entries (animals, parks, features, policies)\n- Files: WildlifeAI.jsx\n\n### T003: Policy pages\n- PrivacyPolicy.jsx\n- TermsOfService.jsx\n- CommunityGuidelines.jsx\n- Files: 3 new page files + App.tsx routes\n\n### T004: Admin Testing Panel\n- Tabbed panel: Broadcast + Testing\n- 3 modes: Testing, Public Live, Emergency Restore\n- Backup/Restore (localStorage JSON)\n- Auto daily backup\n- Files: AdminTestingPanel.jsx, Navbar.jsx\n\n### T005: Profile improvements\n- Saved posts tab, settings, notifications\n- Better UI / loading\n- Files: Profile.jsx (minor improvements)\n\n### T006: CSS for all new features\n- FAB menu animation, policy pages, admin panel, chat UI\n- Files: app.css (append)\n"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Command executed successfully.\nThe output was\n```\n6457\n.community-rule-desc { color: var(--text2); font-size: 0.82rem; line-height: 1.5; }\n.report-section {\n  background: rgba(239,68,68,0.08); border: 1px solid rgba(239,68,68,0.2);\n  border-radius: 12px; padding: 14px; margin-top: 16px;\n}\n.report-section h3 { font-size: 0.95rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 6px; color: #fca5a5; }\n.report-section p { color: var(--text2); font-size: 0.82rem; line-height: 1.6; }\n.report-section a { color: var(--accent); }\n\n/* ===================================================================\n   USER PROFILE \u2014 Not-found + missing classes\n   =================================================================== */\n.user-profile-page { min-height: 100%; background: var(--bg); padding-bottom: 80px; }\n.not-found {\n  text-align: center; padding: 60px 24px;\n  display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: 12px;\n}\n.up-empty { text-align: center; color: var(--text2); padding: 32px 16px; font-size: 0.9rem; }\n\n/* ===================================================================\n   RESPONSIVE \u2014 Mobile tweaks for new features\n   =================================================================== */\n@media (max-width: 480px) {\n  .help-form-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }\n  .ads-account-type-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }\n  .search-user-card { padding: 10px 12px; }\n  .search-user-avatar { width: 44px; height: 44px; font-size: 1.2rem; }\n  .profile-cover-wrap { height: 110px; }\n  .reels-page { height: calc(100dvh - var(--nav-h) - 64px); }\n}\n```"}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "<error>`write` operation failed. File .local/session_plan.md exists on the file system but has not been read yet. Read it first before writing to it.</error>"}], "is_error": true}]}
{"memory_id": 378, "messages": [{"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Now I'll implement everything in parallel batches. Starting with the 6 biggest files simultaneously:"}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": [], "tool_calls": [{"type": "tool", "name": "write", "arguments": {"file_path": "artifacts/animal-x/src/components/UploadReel.jsx", "content": "import { useState, useRef } from \"react\";\nimport { collection, addDoc, serverTimestamp, doc, setDoc, increment } from \"firebase/firestore\";\nimport { db } from \"../utils/firebase\";\nimport { useAuth } from \"../context/AuthContext\";\n\nconst CATEGORIES = [\"Mammals\",\"Birds\",\"Aquatic\",\"Reptiles\",\"Small Creatures\",\"Trees\",\"Mountains\",\"Sea\",\"Desert\"];\n\nconst WILDLIFE_KEYWORDS = [\n  \"animal\",\"lion\",\"tiger\",\"elephant\",\"eagle\",\"wolf\",\"dolphin\",\"whale\",\"shark\",\"cheetah\",\n  \"gorilla\",\"panda\",\"penguin\",\"crocodile\",\"leopard\",\"orca\",\"falcon\",\"bear\",\"fox\",\"lynx\",\n  \"wildlife\",\"nature\",\"wild\",\"jungle\",\"forest\",\"ocean\",\"reptile\",\"bird\",\"marine\",\"safari\",\n  \"savanna\",\"arctic\",\"mountain\",\"desert\",\"rainforest\",\"conservation\",\"habitat\",\"species\",\n  \"snake\",\"lizard\",\"parrot\",\"owl\",\"butterfly\",\"bee\",\"frog\",\"coral\",\"rhino\",\"hippo\",\n  \"giraffe\",\"zebra\",\"buffalo\",\"deer\",\"rabbit\",\"squirrel\",\"turtle\",\"fish\",\"crab\",\"jellyfish\",\n  \"migration\",\"ecosystem\",\"biodiversity\",\"endangered\",\"predator\",\"prey\",\"carnivore\",\n  \"herbivore\",\"mammal\",\"amphibian\",\"insect\",\"moss\",\"fern\",\"cactus\",\"swamp\",\"wetland\",\n  \"national park\",\"zoo\",\"sanctuary\",\"reserve\",\"savannah\",\"tundra\",\"taiga\",\"meadow\",\n];\n\nfunction checkModeration(title, desc, hashtags) {\n  const text = `${title} ${desc} ${hashtags}`.toLowerCase();\n  return WILDLIFE_KEYWORDS.some(w => text.includes(w));\n}\n\nasync function getStrikeInfo(uid) {\n  try {\n    const { getDoc } = await import(\"firebase/firestore\");\n    const snap = await getDoc(doc(db, \"userStrikes\", uid));\n    return snap.exists() ? snap.data() : { strikes: 0, banned: false };\n  } catch { return { strikes: 0, banned: false }; }\n}\n\nasync function addStrike(uid) {\n  try {\n    const ref = doc(db, \"userStrikes\", uid);\n    const { getDoc, setDoc: setDocFn } = await import(\"firebase/firestore\");\n    const snap = await getDoc(ref);\n    const data = snap.exists() ? snap.data() : { strikes: 0 };\n    const newStrikes = (data.strikes || 0) + 1;\n    const banned = newStrikes >= 3;\n    const banExpiry = banned ? Date.now() + 30 * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000 : null;\n    await setDocFn(ref, { strikes: newStrikes, banned, banExpiry, lastStrike: Date.now() }, { merge: true });\n    return { strikes: newStrikes, banned };\n  } catch { return { strikes: 1, banned: false }; }\n}\n\nconst STEP_LABELS = [\"Details\", \"Video\", \"Review\"];\n\nexport default function UploadReel({ onClose, onUploaded }) {\n  const { user, profile } = useAuth();\n  const [step, setStep] = useState(1);\n  const [form, setForm] = useState({\n    title: \"\", description: \"\", hashtags: \"\", category: \"Mammals\", location: \"\",\n  });\n  const [videoFile, setVideoFile] = useState(null);\n  const [videoPreview, setVideoPreview] = useState(null);\n  const [thumbnailFile, setThumbnailFile] = useState(null);\n  const [uploading, setUploading] = useState(false);\n  const [progress, setProgress] = useState(0);\n  const [error, setError] = useState(null);\n  const [warning, setWarning] = useState(null);\n  const [banned, setBanned] = useState(false);\n  const [addingStrike, setAddingStrike] = useState(false);\n  const videoInputRef = useRef(null);\n  const thumbInputRef = useRef(null);\n\n  function handleField(key, val) {\n    setForm(f => ({ ...f, [key]: val }));\n    setError(null);\n  }\n\n  function handleVideoFile(e) {\n    const f = e.target.files?.[0];\n    if (!f) return;\n    if (f.size > 200 * 1024 * 1024) { setError(\"Video must be under 200 MB.\"); return; }\n    if (!f.type.startsWith(\"video/\")) { setError(\"Please select a video file.\"); return; }\n    setVideoFile(f);\n    setVideoPreview(URL.createObjectURL(f));\n    setError(null);\n  }\n\n  async function uploadToStorage(file, contentType) {\n    const res = await fetch(\"/api/storage/uploads/request-url\", {\n      method: \"POST\",\n      headers: { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" },\n      body: JSON.stringify({ name: file.name, size: file.size, contentType }),\n    });\n    if (!res.ok) throw new Error(\"Failed to get upload URL\");\n    const { uploadURL, objectPath } = await res.json();\n    const uploadRes = await fetch(uploadURL, {\n      method: \"PUT\",\n      headers: { \"Content-Type\": contentType },\n      body: file,\n    });\n    if (!uploadRes.ok) throw new Error(\"Upload failed\");\n    return objectPath;\n  }\n\n  async function goNext() {\n    setError(null);\n    if (step === 1) {\n      if (!form.title.trim()) { setError(\"Title is required to continue.\"); return; }\n      const isWildlife = checkModeration(form.title, form.description, form.hashtags);\n      if (!isWildlife) {\n        setWarning(\"\u26a0\ufe0f Your title and description don't contain recognisable wildlife content. Animal X only allows wildlife, nature, and animal-related reels.\");\n        return;\n      }\n      setWarning(null);\n      setStep(2);\n    } else if (step === 2) {\n      if (!videoFile) { setError(\"Please select a video file to continue.\"); return; }\n      setStep(3);\n    }\n  }\n\n  async function handleProceedWithStrike() {\n    if (!user) return;\n    setAddingStrike(true);\n    const { strikes, banned: isBanned } = await addStrike(user.uid);\n    setAddingStrike(false);\n    setWarning(null);\n    if (isBanned) {\n      setBanned(true);\n      setError(\"Upload access banned for 30 days due to repeated community guideline violations.\");\n    } else {\n      alert(`\u26a0\ufe0f Strike ${strikes}/3 recorded. ${3 - strikes} warning(s) remaining before a 30-day upload ban.`);\n      setStep(2);\n    }\n  }\n\n  async function handleSubmit() {\n    if (!user) { alert(\"Please login first.\"); return; }\n    setUploading(true);\n    setError(null);\n    setProgress(10);\n    try {\n      const strikeInfo = await getStrikeInfo(user.uid);\n      if (strikeInfo.banned && strikeInfo.banExpiry > Date.now()) {\n        const days = Math.ceil((strikeInfo.banExpiry - Date.now()) / 86400000);\n        setBanned(true);\n        setError(`Upload access is banned for ${days} more day(s).`);\n        setUploading(false);\n        return;\n      }\n\n      let videoUrl = null;\n      let thumbnailUrl = null;\n\n      setProgress(20);\n      videoUrl = await uploadToStorage(videoFile, videoFile.type);\n      setProgress(70);\n\n      if (thumbnailFile) {\n        thumbnailUrl = await uploadToStorage(thumbnailFile, thumbnailFile.type);\n        setProgress(85);\n      }\n\n      const reelData = {\n        title: form.title.trim(),\n        desc: form.description.trim(),\n        hashtags: form.hashtags.trim(),\n        category: form.category,\n        location: form.location.trim() || null,\n        videoUrl,\n        thumbnailUrl: thumbnailUrl || null,\n        userId: user.uid,\n        username: profile?.username || user.name || user.email?.split(\"@\")[0],\n        userVerified: profile?.manualVerified || false,\n        userAvatar: profile?.avatar || null,\n        likes: 0, views: 0, comments: 0, shares: 0,\n        createdAt: serverTimestamp(),\n        type: \"live\",\n        moderated: true,\n      };\n\n      await addDoc(collection(db, \"reels\"), reelData);\n      await setDoc(doc(db, \"users\", user.uid), { reels: increment(1) }, { merge: true });\n      setProgress(100);\n      onUploaded?.();\n    } catch (e) {\n      setError(\"Upload failed: \" + e.message);\n      setUploading(false);\n    }\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"upload-backdrop\" onClick={e => { if (e.target === e.currentTarget) onClose(); }}>\n      <div className=\"upload-sheet\">\n\n        {/* Header */}\n        <div className=\"upload-header\">\n          <button className=\"upload-close-btn\" onClick={onClose} aria-label=\"Close\">\u2715</button>\n          <div className=\"upload-header-title\">\n            {step === 1 ? \"\ud83d\udcdd Reel Details\" : step === 2 ? \"\ud83c\udfac Upload Video\" : \"\u2705 Review & Post\"}\n          </div>\n          <div className=\"upload-step-dots\">\n            {STEP_LABELS.map((label, i) => (\n              <div key={i} className={`upload-dot ${step === i + 1 ? \"active\" : step > i + 1 ? \"done\" : \"\"}`}>\n                <span className=\"upload-dot-num\">{step > i + 1 ? \"\u2713\" : i + 1}</span>\n                <span className=\"upload-dot-label\">{label}</span>\n              </div>\n            ))}\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        {/* Body */}\n        <div className=\"upload-body\">\n\n          {/* Banned */}\n          {banned && (\n            <div className=\"upload-banned-card\">\n              <div style={{ fontSize: \"2.5rem\" }}>\ud83d\udeab</div>\n              <h3>Upload Access Banned</h3>\n              <p>Your account has received 3 community guideline violations. Upload access is suspended for 30 days.</p>\n              <p style={{ marginTop: 8, fontSize: \"0.82rem\", color: \"var(--text2)\" }}>\n                Contact: <a href=\"mailto:wildlifeanimalfight@gmail.com\" style={{ color: \"var(--accent)\" }}>wildlifeanimalfight@gmail.com</a>\n              </p>\n            </div>\n          )}\n\n          {/* Error bar */}\n          {!banned && error && (\n            <div className=\"upload-error-bar\">\n              <span>\u26a0\ufe0f</span> {error}\n              <button onClick={() => setError(null)} className=\"upload-error-dismiss\">\u2715</button>\n            </div>\n          )}\n\n          {/* Step 1 \u2014 Details */}\n          {!banned && step === 1 && (\n            <div className=\"upload-step-body\">\n              {warning && (\n                <div className=\"upload-warning-card\">\n                  <div className=\"upload-warning-icon\">\ud83c\udf3f</div>\n                  <div className=\"upload-warning-text\">\n                    <strong>Wildlife Content Required</strong>\n                    <p>{warning}</p>\n                    <p style={{ fontSize: \"0.78rem\", marginTop: 6, color: \"var(--text2)\" }}>\n                      Posting unrelated content will add a strike to your account (3 strikes = 30-day ban).\n                    </p>\n                  </div>\n                  <div className=\"upload-warning-actions\">\n                    <button\n                      className=\"upload-warn-revise\"\n                      onClick={() => setWarning(null)}\n                    >\n                      \u270f\ufe0f Revise Content\n                    </button>\n                    <button\n                      className=\"upload-warn-proceed\"\n                      onClick={handleProceedWithStrike}\n                      disabled={addingStrike}\n                    >\n                      {addingStrike ? \"Processing\u2026\" : \"Post Anyway (+ Strike)\"}\n                    </button>\n                  </div>\n                </div>\n              )}\n\n              {!warning && (\n                <div className=\"upload-form-grid\">\n                  <div className=\"upload-field\">\n                    <label className=\"upload-label\">Title <span className=\"upload-required\">*</span></label>\n                    <input\n                      className=\"upload-input\"\n                      value={form.title}\n                      onChange={e => handleField(\"title\", e.target.value)}\n                      placeholder=\"e.g. Lion Pride at Dusk \ud83e\udd81\"\n                      maxLength={100}\n                      autoFocus\n                    />\n                    <span className=\"upload-char-count\">{form.title.length}/100</span>\n                  </div>\n                  <div className=\"upload-field\">\n                    <label className=\"upload-label\">Description</label>\n                    <textarea\n                      className=\"upload-textarea\"\n                      value={form.description}\n                      onChange={e => handleField(\"description\", e.target.value)}\n                      placeholder=\"Describe your wildlife footage\u2026\"\n                      maxLength={500}\n                      rows={3}\n                    />\n                    <span className=\"upload-char-count\">{form.description.length}/500</span>\n                  </div>\n                  <div className=\"upload-field\">\n                    <label className=\"upload-label\">Hashtags</label>\n                    <input\n                      className=\"upload-input\"\n                      value={form.hashtags}\n                      onChange={e => handleField(\"hashtags\", e.target.value)}\n                      placeholder=\"#wildlife #lion #nature\"\n                    />\n                  </div>\n                  <div className=\"upload-row-2col\">\n                    <div className=\"upload-field\">\n                      <label className=\"upload-label\">Category</label>\n                      <select\n                        className=\"upload-select\"\n                        value={form.category}\n                        onChange={e => handleField(\"category\", e.target.value)}\n                      >\n                        {CATEGORIES.map(c => <option key={c}>{c}</option>)}\n                      </select>\n                    </div>\n                    <div className=\"upload-field\">\n                      <label className=\"upload-label\">Location</label>\n                      <input\n                        className=\"upload-input\"\n                        value={form.location}\n                        onChange={e => handleField(\"location\", e.target.value)}\n                        placeholder=\"e.g. Maasai Mara\"\n                      />\n                    </div>\n                  </div>\n                  <div className=\"upload-ai-note\">\n                    \ud83e\udd16 <strong>AI Moderation active</strong> \u2014 only wildlife & nature content is allowed\n                  </div>\n                </div>\n              )}\n            </div>\n          )}\n\n          {/* Step 2 \u2014 Video */}\n          {!banned && step === 2 && (\n            <div className=\"upload-step-body\">\n              <div\n                className={`upload-dropzone ${videoFile ? \"has-file\" : \"\"}`}\n                onClick={() => videoInputRef.current?.click()}\n              >\n                {videoPreview ? (\n                  <video\n                    src={videoPreview}\n                    className=\"upload-preview-vid\"\n                    muted\n                    playsInline\n                    controls\n                  />\n                ) : (\n                  <div className=\"upload-dropzone-inner\">\n                    <div className=\"upload-dropzone-icon\">\ud83c\udfac</div>\n                    <div className=\"upload-dropzone-title\">Tap to select video</div>\n                    <div className=\"upload-dropzone-hint\">MP4 \u00b7 MOV \u00b7 WebM \u00b7 max 200 MB</div>\n                  </div>\n                )}\n              </div>\n              <input\n                ref={videoInputRef}\n                type=\"file\"\n                accept=\"video/*\"\n                style={{ display: \"none\" }}\n                onChange={handleVideoFile}\n              />\n              {videoFile && (\n                <div className=\"upload-file-chip\">\n                  \u2705 {videoFile.name} <span className=\"upload-file-size\">({(videoFile.size / 1024 / 1024).toFixed(1)} MB)</span>\n                  <button className=\"upload-file-remove\" onClick={() => { setVideoFile(null); setVideoPreview(null); }}>\u2715</button>\n                </div>\n              )}\n              <div className=\"upload-thumb-section\">\n                <label className=\"upload-label\">Custom Thumbnail <span className=\"upload-optional\">(optional)</span></label>\n                <button className=\"upload-thumb-btn\" onClick={() => thumbInputRef.current?.click()}>\n                  {thumbnailFile ? `\u2705 ${thumbnailFile.name}` : \"\ud83d\udcf7 Choose thumbnail image\"}\n                </button>\n                <input\n                  ref={thumbInputRef}\n                  type=\"file\"\n                  accept=\"image/*\"\n                  style={{ display: \"none\" }}\n                  onChange={e => setThumbnailFile(e.target.files?.[0] || null)}\n                />\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          )}\n\n          {/* Step 3 \u2014 Review */}\n          {!banned && step === 3 && (\n            <div className=\"upload-step-body\">\n              <div className=\"upload-review-card\">\n                <div className=\"upload-review-header\">\n                  <span className=\"upload-review-cat-badge\">{form.category}</span>\n                  {form.location && <span className=\"upload-review-loc\">\ud83d\udccd {form.location}</span>}\n                </div>\n                <div className=\"upload-review-title\">{form.title}</div>\n                {form.description && (\n                  <div className=\"upload-review-desc\">{form.description}</div>\n                )}\n                {form.hashtags && (\n                  <div className=\"upload-review-tags\">\n                    {String(form.hashtags).split(/[\\s,]+/).filter(Boolean).map(h => (\n                      <span key={h} className=\"upload-review-tag\">{h.startsWith(\"#\") ? h : \"#\" + h}</span>\n                    ))}\n                  </div>\n                )}\n                <div className=\"upload-review-file-row\">\n                  <span>\ud83c\udfac</span>\n                  <span>{videoFile?.name}</span>\n                  <span className=\"upload-file-size\">({(videoFile?.size / 1024 / 1024).toFixed(1)} MB)</span>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n\n              <div className=\"upload-guidelines-box\">\n                <div className=\"upload-guidelines-title\">\ud83d\udccb Before you post</div>\n                <div className=\"upload-guideline-row\">\u2705 Wildlife, nature, animals, oceans, forests</div>\n                <div className=\"upload-guideline-row\">\u274c Non-wildlife content \u2192 instant strike</div>\n                <div className=\"upload-guideline-row\">\u274c No violence, abuse, or harmful content</div>\n                <div className=\"upload-guideline-row\">\u26a0\ufe0f 3 strikes = 30-day upload ban</div>\n              </div>\n\n              {uploading && (\n                <div className=\"upload-progress-wrap\">\n                  <div className=\"upload-progress-track\">\n                    <div className=\"upload-progress-fill\" style={{ width: `${progress}%` }} />\n                  </div>\n                  <div className=\"upload-progress-label\">Uploading\u2026 {progress}%</div>\n                </div>\n              )}\n            </div>\n          )}\n        </div>\n\n        {/* Footer \u2014 always visible */}\n        {!banned && (\n          <div className=\"upload-footer\">\n            {step > 1 && !uploading && (\n              <button className=\"upload-btn-back\" onClick={() => { setStep(s => s - 1); setError(null); }}>\n                \u2190 Back\n              </button>\n            )}\n            <div style={{ flex: 1 }} />\n            {step < 3 && !warning && (\n              <button className=\"upload-btn-next\" onClick={goNext}>\n                {step === 1 ? \"Next: Upload Video \u2192\" : \"Review \u2192\"}\n              </button>\n            )}\n            {step === 3 && (\n              <button\n                className=\"upload-btn-post\"\n                onClick={handleSubmit}\n                disabled={uploading}\n              >\n                {uploading ? `Uploading ${progress}%\u2026` : \"\ud83d\ude80 Post Reel\"}\n              </button>\n            )}\n          </div>\n        )}\n\n        {banned && (\n          <div className=\"upload-footer\">\n            <button className=\"upload-btn-back\" onClick={onClose}>Close</button>\n          </div>\n        )}\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n"}}, {"type": "tool", "name": "write", "arguments": {"file_path": "artifacts/animal-x/src/components/WildlifeAI.jsx", "content": "import { useState, useRef, useEffect, useCallback } from \"react\";\nimport { useLocation } from \"wouter\";\nimport animals from \"../data/animals\";\n\nconst APP_VERSION = \"v2.5.0\";\n\n/* \u2500\u2500\u2500 Large Knowledge Base \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500 */\nconst KB = [\n  // Greetings\n  { p: /^(hi|hello|hey|helo|hii|howdy|sup|yo)\\b/i, a: \"\ud83d\udc4b Hey there! I'm your **Wildlife AI** \ud83e\udd81\\n\\nI can answer questions about any animal, app features, national parks, zoos, conservation, or wildlife science. What would you like to know?\" },\n\n  // App version & info\n  { p: /version|app.*version|what.*version/i, a: `\u2139\ufe0f **Animal X ${APP_VERSION}**\\n\\nWildlife social media platform with:\\n\u2022 1,213+ animals & natural wonders\\n\u2022 TikTok-style wildlife Reels\\n\u2022 300+ zoos on interactive map\\n\u2022 Live animal GPS tracking\\n\u2022 200+ wildlife creators\\n\u2022 AI chatbot (that's me!)\\n\\nAll features are **100% FREE** \u2014 no premium required!` },\n  { p: /about.*app|what is animal x|what.*app/i, a: `\ud83d\udc3e **About Animal X ${APP_VERSION}**\\n\\nAnimal X is a professional wildlife social media app \u2014 like Instagram + TikTok, but 100% focused on wildlife.\\n\\n\u2022 1,213+ animals with quizzes & abilities\\n\u2022 Wildlife Reels (TikTok-style)\\n\u2022 Zoo & wildlife map\\n\u2022 Creator profiles & community\\n\u2022 AI chatbot assistance\\n\\n\ud83d\udce7 Contact: wildlifeanimalfight@gmail.com` },\n\n  // Upload Reel\n  { p: /upload.*reel|reel.*upload|post.*video|how.*reel|video.*upload/i, a: \"\ud83d\udcf9 **Upload a Wildlife Reel:**\\n1. Tap **\ud83c\udfac Reels** in the bottom nav\\n2. Tap **\u2795 Upload** (top right)\\n3. **Step 1:** Enter title, description, hashtags, category\\n4. Tap **Next: Upload Video \u2192**\\n5. **Step 2:** Select your video (max 200 MB)\\n6. Tap **Review \u2192**\\n7. **Step 3:** Confirm details \u2192 tap **\ud83d\ude80 Post Reel**\\n\\n\ud83e\udd16 AI moderation checks content \u2014 only wildlife is allowed.\\n\u26a0\ufe0f 3 violations = 30-day upload ban.\" },\n\n  // Like / double tap\n  { p: /like|heart|double.*tap|tap.*twice/i, a: \"\u2764\ufe0f **Liking Reels:**\\n\u2022 Tap the **\u2764\ufe0f** button on the right side of any reel\\n\u2022 **Double-tap** anywhere on the reel for a quick like (heart burst animation!)\\n\u2022 Like counts sync instantly to Firebase\\n\u2022 Tap again to **unlike**\" },\n\n  // Follow system\n  { p: /follow|following|unfollow/i, a: \"\ud83d\udc65 **Following Creators:**\\n\u2022 Tap **+ Follow** on any reel or profile\\n\u2022 Tap **Following** again to unfollow\\n\u2022 Visit \ud83d\udd0d Search to discover 200+ wildlife creators\\n\u2022 Your following list is saved permanently in Firebase\" },\n\n  // Search\n  { p: /search.*user|find.*user|find.*creator|user.*search|discover/i, a: \"\ud83d\udd0d **Find Creators:**\\n1. Tap the **\ud83d\udc65 icon** in the top bar\\n2. Type @username, display name, or country\\n3. Filter by category (Mammals, Birds, Aquatic\u2026)\\n4. Sort by most followers or most reels\\n5. Tap any profile card to open their full profile\" },\n\n  // Map\n  { p: /map|zoo.*map|gps|tracking|live.*track/i, a: \"\ud83d\uddfa\ufe0f **Map Features:**\\n\u2022 **Zoo Layer \ud83c\udfdb\ufe0f** \u2014 300+ real zoos with ratings & Google Maps links\\n\u2022 **Live Tracking \ud83e\udd81** \u2014 50+ GPS-tracked wild animals (lion, elephant, whale\u2026)\\n\u2022 **Migration Layer \ud83e\udd8b** \u2014 seasonal wildlife migration routes\\n\u2022 **My Location \ud83d\udccd** \u2014 animated blue dot for your GPS position\\n\u2022 Search by animal name, zoo, or country\\n\u2022 Toggle each layer on/off independently\" },\n\n  // Travel\n  { p: /travel|uber|ola|lyft|bolt|grab|flight|skyscanner|booking/i, a: \"\u2708\ufe0f **Travel Section:**\\n\ud83d\ude97 Ride apps: Uber, Ola, Lyft, Bolt, Grab\\n\u2708\ufe0f Flights: Skyscanner, Google Flights, Kayak\\n\ud83d\udee9\ufe0f Private aviation: VistaJet\\n\\nAll links deep-link to the apps on your device or open in browser.\" },\n\n  // Notifications\n  { p: /notification|bell|alerts|badge/i, a: \"\ud83d\udd14 **Notifications:**\\n\u2022 Tap the \ud83d\udd14 bell icon in the top bar\\n\u2022 You get notified when someone follows you\\n\u2022 Red badge shows unread count\\n\u2022 Tap 'Mark all read' to clear\\n\u2022 Powered by Firebase Firestore real-time updates\" },\n\n  // Ads\n  { p: /ad|advertise|advertisement|run.*ad/i, a: \"\ud83d\udce2 **Advertise on Animal X:**\\n1. Go to \u2139\ufe0f Help \u2192 tap **Run Advertisement**\\n2. Enter ad title, description, target URL\\n3. Choose target categories (Mammals, Birds\u2026)\\n4. Select plan (\u20b9149 \u2014 \u20b94,999 / month)\\n5. Pay via UPI: **nakumamit27-1@okicici**\\n   or PayPal: paypal.me/animalx\\n6. Admin reviews & activates your ad within 24h\" },\n\n  // Blue tick\n  { p: /blue.*tick|verified|verification|checkmark/i, a: \"\ud83d\udd35 **Blue Tick Verification:**\\n\u2022 **Auto:** Reach 100,000 followers \u2014 blue tick granted automatically with a congratulations popup!\\n\u2022 **Manual:** Admin can grant it directly from the admin panel\\n\u2022 Blue tick appears on profiles, reels, and search results\\n\u2022 Once granted, it's permanent unless the account violates guidelines\" },\n\n  // Profile\n  { p: /profile|edit.*profile|my.*profile|account/i, a: \"\ud83d\udc64 **Your Profile:**\\n1. Tap \ud83d\udc64 **Profile** in the bottom nav\\n2. View your posts, reels, followers, following\\n3. Tap \u270f\ufe0f **Edit Profile** to change your name or photo\\n4. Tap \ud83d\udcf7 cover photo area to update your cover image\\n5. Upload profile/cover via Object Storage (cloud) or local fallback\" },\n\n  // Stories\n  { p: /story|stories|24.*hour/i, a: \"\ud83d\udd34 **Stories:**\\n\u2022 Auto-expire after 24 hours\\n\u2022 Go to \ud83c\udfac Reels \u2192 Stories tab\\n\u2022 Tap \u2795 Add Story\\n\u2022 Choose a photo or short video\\n\u2022 Viewers can see who viewed your story\" },\n\n  // Login / signup\n  { p: /sign.?up|register|create.*account|new account/i, a: \"\ud83d\udcdd **Create Account:**\\n1. Tap \ud83d\udc64 Profile \u2192 **Login / Sign Up**\\n2. Enter your display name, email, and password (6+ chars)\\n3. Tap **Create Account**\\n\\n\u2705 All features are completely free!\" },\n  { p: /login|sign.?in|log.*in/i, a: \"\ud83d\udd11 **Login:**\\n1. Tap \ud83d\udc64 Profile\\n2. Enter email + password\\n3. Tap **Login**\\n\\nForgot password? Tap **Forgot Password?** on the login screen.\" },\n  { p: /forgot.*password|reset.*password|password.*reset/i, a: \"\ud83d\udd11 **Reset Password:**\\n1. Go to \ud83d\udc64 Profile \u2192 Login\\n2. Tap **Forgot Password?**\\n3. Enter your email address\\n4. Check inbox for the reset link\\n\\nStill need help? Email: wildlifeanimalfight@gmail.com\" },\n\n  // Guidelines / rules\n  { p: /community.*guideline|rules|guidelines|policy/i, a: \"\ud83d\udccb **Community Guidelines:**\\n\u2022 \u2705 Only wildlife, nature & animal content\\n\u2022 \u274c No hate speech, violence, or abuse\\n\u2022 \u274c No spam, misleading info, or copyrighted music\\n\u2022 \u26a0\ufe0f 3 violations = 30-day upload ban\\n\u2022 \ud83d\udeab Severe violations = permanent ban\\n\\nFull Guidelines: tap \ud83e\uddb4 FAB \u2192 Community Guidelines\" },\n\n  // Privacy\n  { p: /privacy|data.*collect|personal.*data/i, a: \"\ud83d\udd12 **Privacy Policy:**\\nWe collect:\\n\u2022 Email (for login only)\\n\u2022 Content you upload\\n\u2022 Like & follow data\\n\\nAll data stored securely on Firebase. We never sell your data to third parties.\\n\\nFull policy: tap \ud83e\uddb4 FAB \u2192 Privacy Policy\" },\n\n  // Terms\n  { p: /terms|terms.*service|terms.*condition/i, a: \"\ud83d\udcc4 **Terms of Service:**\\n\u2022 Must be 13+ to use Animal X\\n\u2022 Only wildlife content allowed on platform\\n\u2022 Admin retains right to remove violating content\\n\u2022 Account ban possible for repeat violations\\n\\nFull terms: tap \ud83e\uddb4 FAB \u2192 Terms of Service\" },\n\n  // Report\n  { p: /report|report.*reel|flag.*content|flag.*user/i, a: \"\ud83d\udea9 **Report Content:**\\n1. Tap \u22ee (three dots) on any reel\\n2. Select 'Report'\\n3. Choose violation type\\n4. Admin reviews within 24h\\n\\nFor urgent issues: wildlifeanimalfight@gmail.com\" },\n\n  // Contact / support\n  { p: /contact|support|help.*desk|email.*us/i, a: \"\ud83d\udcde **Contact Support:**\\n\ud83d\udce7 Email: wildlifeanimalfight@gmail.com\\n\ud83d\udcf8 Instagram: @wildlifeanimalfight\\n\u25b6\ufe0f YouTube: wildlifeanimalfight\\n\ud83d\udc65 Facebook: wildlifeanimalfight\\n\\nOr visit \u2753 Help in the app for full FAQ.\" },\n\n  // Admin\n  { p: /admin|super.*admin|broadcast|admin.*mode/i, a: \"\ud83d\udc51 **Admin System:**\\n\u2022 Login as the super admin email\\n\u2022 Tap the \ud83e\udd81 Animal X logo **7 times**\\n\u2022 Access broadcast panel + testing panel\\n\u2022 Send messages to all users\\n\u2022 Grant/remove blue ticks\\n\u2022 Ban users, add strikes\\n\u2022 Access testing & emergency restore modes\" },\n\n  // Chatbot / AI\n  { p: /chatbot|chat|ai.*assistant|wildlife.*ai/i, a: \"\ud83e\uddb4 I'm the **Wildlife AI** assistant!\\n\\nI can answer questions about:\\n\u2022 1,213+ animals in the app\\n\u2022 Every app feature\\n\u2022 Wildlife science & conservation\\n\u2022 National parks & zoos\\n\u2022 Travel & safari planning\\n\\nTap the \ud83e\uddb4 bone button to access me anytime!\" },\n\n  // \u2500\u2500\u2500 Wildlife Science \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n  { p: /biggest|largest.*animal|largest.*creature|biggest.*animal/i, a: \"\ud83d\udccf **Size Record Holders:**\\n\ud83d\udc0b Largest ever: Blue Whale (30 m, 200 tons)\\n\ud83d\udc18 Largest land animal: African Elephant (6,000 kg)\\n\ud83e\udd92 Tallest land animal: Giraffe (5.8 m)\\n\ud83e\udd88 Largest fish: Whale Shark (12 m)\\n\ud83d\udc0a Largest reptile: Saltwater Crocodile (7 m)\\n\ud83e\udd85 Largest wingspan: Wandering Albatross (3.5 m)\\n\ud83d\udc26 Largest bird: Ostrich (2.7 m, 156 kg)\" },\n  { p: /fastest|speed.*animal|quickest/i, a: \"\ud83c\udfc3 **Speed Records:**\\n\ud83d\udc06 Fastest land: Cheetah (112 km/h)\\n\ud83e\udd85 Fastest dive: Peregrine Falcon (389 km/h!)\\n\ud83d\udc1f Fastest fish: Sailfish (110 km/h)\\n\ud83d\udc2c Fastest marine mammal: Orca (55 km/h)\\n\ud83e\udd98 Fastest sustained: Pronghorn (90 km/h over 6 km)\\n\ud83e\udd8b Monarch Butterfly migrates 4,800 km non-stop\" },\n  { p: /smartest|most.*intelligent|intelligent.*animal/i, a: \"\ud83e\udde0 **Most Intelligent Animals:**\\n\ud83d\udc12 Chimpanzees \u2014 closest DNA to humans (98.7%), use tools\\n\ud83d\udc2c Dolphins \u2014 signature whistles (names), mirror self-recognition\\n\ud83d\udc18 Elephants \u2014 mourn dead, remember faces for decades\\n\ud83d\udc19 Octopus \u2014 can open jars, solve puzzles, change color\\n\ud83d\udc26 Crow \u2014 makes hooks from wire, plans for the future\\n\ud83d\udc37 Pigs \u2014 smarter than dogs, learn complex tricks\\n\ud83e\udd9c African Grey Parrot \u2014 vocabulary of 1,000+ words\" },\n  { p: /endangered|extinction|conservation|protect/i, a: \"\ud83c\udf0d **Wildlife Conservation:**\\n\u2022 1 million+ species face extinction risk\\n\u2022 Main threats: habitat loss, climate change, poaching\\n\\n**Critically Endangered:**\\n\ud83d\udc06 Amur Leopard (<100 wild)\\n\ud83d\udc2c Vaquita porpoise (~10 remaining!)\\n\ud83e\udd8f Javan Rhino (<80 wild)\\n\\n**Success stories:**\\n\u2705 Arabian Oryx \u2014 brought back from extinction\\n\u2705 California Condor \u2014 27 to 500+\\n\u2705 Giant Panda \u2014 upgraded from Endangered to Vulnerable\" },\n  { p: /migration|migrate|seasonal.*movement/i, a: \"\ud83e\udd8b **Wildlife Migration Highlights:**\\n\ud83e\uddac Wildebeest: 3,000 km Serengeti circuit\\n\ud83d\udc26 Arctic Tern: 70,000 km pole-to-pole each year!\\n\ud83e\udd8b Monarch Butterfly: 4,800 km across North America\\n\ud83d\udc0b Humpback Whale: 20,000 km tropical \u2194 polar\\n\ud83d\udc1f Pacific Salmon: swims upstream to birthplace to spawn\\n\ud83e\udd8c Caribou: 5,000 km Arctic migration\\n\ud83d\udc1d Monarch butterflies use Earth's magnetic field to navigate\\n\\nSee migration routes on the Map page!\" },\n  { p: /how.*many.*species|species.*count|animals.*earth|species.*earth/i, a: \"\ud83d\udd2c **Species on Earth:**\\n\u2022 Estimated total: 8.7 million species\\n\u2022 Formally described: ~1.2 million\\n\u2022 New discoveries: ~18,000 species/year\\n\u2022 Animal X includes: 1,213+ species & natural wonders\\n\u2022 Most diverse biomes: Tropical rainforests & coral reels\" },\n\n  // \u2500\u2500\u2500 Specific Animals \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n  { p: /lion|lions|pride/i, a: \"\ud83e\udd81 **Lion** *(Panthera leo)*\\n\ud83c\udfe0 African savanna & Gir Forest (India)\\n\ud83c\udf7d\ufe0f Diet: Zebra, wildebeest, buffalo\\n\u23f3 Lifespan: 12\u201316 years wild\\n\ud83d\udc65 Live in groups called **prides** (5\u201320 lions)\\n\u26a1 Roar audible up to **8 km** away\\n\ud83c\udf89 The only truly social big cat\\n\ud83d\udcf1 Search 'Lion' in Animals page for full details!\" },\n  { p: /tiger|tigers/i, a: \"\ud83d\udc05 **Tiger** *(Panthera tigris)*\\n\ud83c\udfe0 Forests of India, Russia, SE Asia\\n\ud83c\udf7d\ufe0f Diet: Deer, wild boar, water buffalo\\n\u23f3 Lifespan: 10\u201315 years wild\\n\ud83d\udd22 Only 4,500 remaining in the wild\\n\u26a1 Can swim 6 km across rivers\\n\ud83e\uddec Each tiger has unique stripe patterns (like fingerprints)\\n\ud83d\udcf1 Search 'Tiger' in Animals page!\" },\n  { p: /elephant|elephants/i, a: \"\ud83d\udc18 **Elephant** *(Elephantidae)*\\n\ud83c\udfe0 African savanna & Asian forests\\n\ud83c\udf7d\ufe0f Diet: Grass, roots, bark, fruit (200 kg/day!)\\n\u23f3 Lifespan: 60\u201370 years\\n\u26a1 They mourn their dead and have excellent long-term memory\\n\ud83d\udca7 Can sense water 12 km underground\\n\ud83d\udde3\ufe0f Communicate via seismic ground vibrations\\n\ud83d\udcf1 Find elephants in Animals \u2192 Mammals!\" },\n  { p: /cheetah|cheetahs/i, a: \"\ud83d\udc06 **Cheetah** *(Acinonyx jubatus)*\\n\ud83c\udfe0 African savanna & Iran\\n\ud83c\udf7d\ufe0f Diet: Gazelle, impalas\\n\u23f3 Lifespan: 10\u201312 years wild\\n\u26a1 **Fastest land animal: 112 km/h** in 3 seconds\\n\ud83d\ude22 Only 7,000 remain \u2014 vulnerable to extinction\\n\ud83e\uddb7 Cannot roar \u2014 only purrs and chirps!\" },\n  { p: /whale|blue whale/i, a: \"\ud83d\udc0b **Blue Whale** *(Balaenoptera musculus)*\\n\ud83c\udfe0 All oceans except Arctic\\n\ud83c\udf7d\ufe0f Diet: Krill (40 million krill/day!)\\n\u23f3 Lifespan: 80\u201390 years\\n\u26a1 **Largest animal on Earth ever** \u2014 heart the size of a car\\n\ud83d\udd0a Call louder than a jet engine (188 dB)\\n\ud83d\udcaa Tongue weighs as much as an elephant!\" },\n  { p: /dolphin|dolphins/i, a: \"\ud83d\udc2c **Dolphin** *(Delphinidae)*\\n\ud83c\udfe0 Oceans and coastal waters worldwide\\n\ud83c\udf7d\ufe0f Diet: Fish, squid, crustaceans\\n\u23f3 Lifespan: 20\u201350 years\\n\u26a1 Use **echolocation** to hunt in total darkness\\n\ud83d\udde3\ufe0f Each dolphin has a unique signature whistle (their name!)\\n\ud83e\ude9e One of few animals that pass the mirror self-recognition test\" },\n  { p: /gorilla|gorillas/i, a: \"\ud83e\udd8d **Gorilla** *(Gorilla spp.)*\\n\ud83c\udfe0 Central African rainforests\\n\ud83c\udf7d\ufe0f Diet: Leaves, fruit, stems (27 kg/day)\\n\u23f3 Lifespan: 35\u201340 years wild\\n\ud83e\uddec Share 98.3% DNA with humans\\n\u26a1 A silverback can lift 800 kg \u2014 10x their body weight\\n\ud83d\udcc9 Mountain Gorilla: only ~1,000 remaining\" },\n  { p: /shark|sharks/i, a: \"\ud83e\udd88 **Shark** *(Selachimorpha)*\\n\ud83c\udfe0 All oceans worldwide\\n\ud83c\udf7d\ufe0f Diet: Fish, seals, squid (varies by species)\\n\u23f3 Lifespan: 20\u2013500 years (Greenland Shark!)\\n\u26a1 450 million years old \u2014 older than trees!\\n\ud83e\uddb7 500+ species, from 20 cm dwarf to 12 m whale shark\\n\ud83e\ude78 Can detect 1 drop of blood in 1 million litres of water\" },\n  { p: /eagle|eagles/i, a: \"\ud83e\udd85 **Eagle** *(Accipitridae)*\\n\ud83c\udfe0 Every continent except Antarctica\\n\ud83c\udf7d\ufe0f Diet: Fish, rabbits, snakes, carrion\\n\u23f3 Lifespan: 20\u201330 years wild\\n\u26a1 Vision **4\u20138x sharper than humans** \u2014 spots prey from 3 km!\\n\ud83c\udfd4\ufe0f Bald Eagle is the USA's national bird\\n\ud83c\udf0d 60+ species worldwide including Harpy, Bald, Golden, Philippine\" },\n  { p: /polar bear|polar bears/i, a: \"\ud83d\udc3b\u200d\u2744\ufe0f **Polar Bear** *(Ursus maritimus)*\\n\ud83c\udfe0 Arctic Circle\\n\ud83c\udf7d\ufe0f Diet: Ringed seals, bearded seals\\n\u23f3 Lifespan: 25\u201330 years wild\\n\u26a1 Can swim 100 km non-stop in icy water\\n\ud83e\uddca Fur appears white but is actually transparent/hollow\\n\u26a0\ufe0f Vulnerable \u2014 climate change is melting their habitat\\n\ud83d\udc3b Largest land carnivore on Earth\" },\n  { p: /penguin|penguins/i, a: \"\ud83d\udc27 **Penguin** *(Sphenisciformes)*\\n\ud83c\udfe0 Southern Hemisphere (mainly Antarctica)\\n\ud83c\udf7d\ufe0f Diet: Fish, squid, krill\\n\u23f3 Lifespan: 15\u201320 years wild\\n\u26a1 Cannot fly but swim at 35 km/h underwater!\\n\ud83e\udd76 Emperor penguins breed in -50\u00b0C Antarctic winter\\n\ud83e\udd3f Dive 500+ m, hold breath for 20 minutes\\n\ud83c\udf0d 18 species total\" },\n  { p: /wolf|wolves|pack/i, a: \"\ud83d\udc3a **Wolf** *(Canis lupus)*\\n\ud83c\udfe0 N. America, Europe, Asia\\n\ud83c\udf7d\ufe0f Diet: Elk, deer, bison, rabbits\\n\u23f3 Lifespan: 6\u20138 years wild\\n\u26a1 Howl can be heard **10 km** away\\n\ud83d\udc65 Live in packs of 6\u201310 led by an alpha pair\\n\ud83d\udd04 Wolves were reintroduced to Yellowstone in 1995, restoring the entire ecosystem!\" },\n  { p: /snake|snakes|viper|cobra/i, a: \"\ud83d\udc0d **Snakes** *(Serpentes)*\\n\ud83c\udfe0 Every continent except Antarctica\\n\ud83c\udf7d\ufe0f Diet: Rodents, birds, eggs, insects\\n\u23f3 Lifespan: 10\u201325 years\\n\u26a1 3,000+ species \u2014 only ~600 are venomous\\n\ud83c\udfc3 Black Mamba: fastest snake at 20 km/h\\n\ud83d\udccf Reticulated Python: longest (7.5 m)\\n\ud83d\udc89 King Cobra: most venomous land snake (enough to kill an elephant)\" },\n  { p: /crocodile|alligator|croc/i, a: \"\ud83d\udc0a **Crocodile** *(Crocodylidae)*\\n\ud83c\udfe0 Africa, Asia, Australia, Americas\\n\ud83c\udf7d\ufe0f Diet: Fish, wildebeest, buffalo\\n\u23f3 Lifespan: 70\u2013100 years\\n\u26a1 **Strongest bite force on Earth** \u2014 16,000 N!\\n\ud83e\udd95 Largely unchanged for 200 million years\\n\ud83c\udfca Can hold breath for 2 hours underwater\" },\n  { p: /panda|giant panda/i, a: \"\ud83d\udc3c **Giant Panda** *(Ailuropoda melanoleuca)*\\n\ud83c\udfe0 Mountain forests of central China\\n\ud83c\udf7d\ufe0f Diet: Almost exclusively bamboo (12 kg/day!)\\n\u23f3 Lifespan: 20 years wild\\n\ud83d\udcaa Conservation success: from 1,000 to 1,800+\\n\ud83c\udf8b Must eat 12 hours a day just to get enough nutrition\\n\u26a1 Actually classified as a carnivore despite eating bamboo\" },\n  { p: /giraffe|giraffes/i, a: \"\ud83e\udd92 **Giraffe** *(Giraffa camelopardalis)*\\n\ud83c\udfe0 African savanna\\n\ud83c\udf7d\ufe0f Diet: Leaves, mainly acacia trees\\n\u23f3 Lifespan: 25 years wild\\n\u26a1 **Tallest animal on Earth** at 5.8 m\\n\u2764\ufe0f Heart weighs 11 kg and pumps blood 2 m up their neck\\n\ud83d\ude34 Only sleep 30 minutes per day (in short naps!)\" },\n  { p: /octopus|octopi|cephalopod/i, a: \"\ud83d\udc19 **Octopus** *(Octopoda)*\\n\ud83c\udfe0 All oceans, coastal zones\\n\ud83c\udf7d\ufe0f Diet: Crabs, lobsters, fish\\n\u23f3 Lifespan: 1\u20133 years\\n\u26a1 **3 hearts, blue blood, and 9 brains!**\\n\ud83c\udfa8 Change colour & texture in 200 milliseconds\\n\ud83e\udde0 Can open jars, use tools, and escape aquariums\\n\ud83d\udd8a\ufe0f 8 arms, each with independent neural control\" },\n  { p: /bee|bees|honey bee/i, a: \"\ud83d\udc1d **Honeybee** *(Apis mellifera)*\\n\ud83c\udfe0 Every continent except Antarctica\\n\ud83c\udf7d\ufe0f Diet: Nectar and pollen\\n\u23f3 Lifespan: 6 weeks (worker)\\n\u26a1 Pollinate **1/3 of all human food crops**\\n\ud83d\udc83 Communicate via the 'waggle dance' to share flower locations\\n\ud83c\udf6f A bee makes 1/12 teaspoon of honey in its lifetime\\n\ud83d\udc65 A single hive has 60,000 bees!\" },\n  { p: /butterfly|monarch butterfly/i, a: \"\ud83e\udd8b **Monarch Butterfly** *(Danaus plexippus)*\\n\ud83c\udfe0 North America (migrates to Mexico)\\n\ud83c\udf7d\ufe0f Diet: Milkweed (caterpillar), nectar (adult)\\n\u23f3 Lifespan: 2\u20136 weeks (or 8 months if migrating)\\n\u26a1 Migrates **4,800 km** from Canada to Mexico!\\n\ud83d\udc45 Tastes with its feet\\n\ud83d\udc40 Sees UV light invisible to humans\" },\n  { p: /coral|coral reef|great barrier reef/i, a: \"\ud83e\udeb8 **Coral Reefs:**\\n\u2022 Cover < 1% of the ocean floor\\n\u2022 Home to 25% of all marine species\\n\u2022 The **Great Barrier Reef** is the world's largest (2,300 km)\\n\u2022 Generate \\$375 billion in economic value per year\\n\u26a0\ufe0f 50% of the world's reels bleached since 1980 due to climate change\\n\u2022 Each coral polyp builds its skeleton over decades\" },\n\n  // \u2500\u2500\u2500 National Parks \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n  { p: /yellowstone|yellowstone.*park/i, a: \"\ud83c\udfd4\ufe0f **Yellowstone National Park (USA)**\\n\ud83d\udccd Wyoming, Montana & Idaho\\n\ud83c\udf0b World's first national park (1872)\\n\ud83e\uddac Home to the largest bison herd in the USA\\n\u26a1 Contains 60% of the world's geysers (Old Faithful!)\\n\ud83d\udc3a Wolf reintroduction in 1995 restored entire ecosystem balance\\n\ud83e\udd85 Species: bison, wolf, grizzly, elk, bald eagle\" },\n  { p: /serengeti|serengeti.*park/i, a: \"\ud83c\udf0d **Serengeti National Park (Tanzania)**\\n\ud83d\udccd Northern Tanzania\\n\ud83e\uddac Annual wildebeest migration: **1.5 million animals**\\n\ud83e\udd81 Largest lion population in Africa\\n\ud83d\udc06 Cheetah, leopard, elephant, hippo, crocodile all present\\n\u26a1 UNESCO World Heritage Site\\n\ud83c\udf05 Best visited June\u2013October for the Great Migration\" },\n  { p: /amazon|amazon.*rainforest/i, a: \"\ud83c\udf3f **Amazon Rainforest:**\\n\ud83d\udccd 9 South American countries\\n\u26a1 Covers 5.5 million km\u00b2 \u2014 40% of South America\\n\ud83d\udc26 40,000+ plant species, 1,300 bird species, 3,000 fish species\\n\ud83d\udca7 Produces 20% of Earth's oxygen\\n\ud83c\udf27\ufe0f Creates its own weather \u2014 recycles 50\u201375 billion tonnes of water daily\\n\u26a0\ufe0f 17% deforested \u2014 conservation urgent!\" },\n  { p: /masai mara|maasai mara|kenya.*wildlife/i, a: \"\ud83c\udf0d **Maasai Mara (Kenya)**\\n\ud83d\udccd Southwest Kenya\\n\ud83e\udd81 One of Africa's best big cat reserves\\n\ud83e\uddac Home to 1.5 million wildebeest during Great Migration (Jul\u2013Oct)\\n\ud83d\udc06 Highest density of leopards in any reserve\\n\u26a1 Part of the Serengeti\u2013Mara ecosystem\\n\ud83c\udf9f\ufe0f Best time to visit: July to October\" },\n  { p: /galapagos|galapagos island/i, a: \"\ud83e\udd8e **Gal\u00e1pagos Islands (Ecuador)**\\n\ud83d\udccd Pacific Ocean, 1,000 km from Ecuador\\n\ud83d\udc22 Giant tortoises live 150+ years\\n\ud83e\udd8e Marine iguanas \u2014 the only sea-going lizards\\n\ud83d\udc26 Blue-footed boobies, Darwin's finches\\n\u26a1 Where Darwin developed the theory of evolution\\n\ud83c\udf0a UNESCO World Heritage Site\\n\ud83e\udd88 One of the best shark diving destinations\" },\n\n  // \u2500\u2500\u2500 General Fallbacks \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n  { p: /national park|parks|wildlife.*reserve/i, a: \"\ud83c\udfde\ufe0f **Top Wildlife Destinations:**\\n\ud83c\udf0d Serengeti, Tanzania \u2014 Great Migration\\n\ud83c\udfd4\ufe0f Yellowstone, USA \u2014 wolves & geysers\\n\ud83c\udf3f Amazon Rainforest, Brazil \u2014 40,000+ plant species\\n\ud83e\udd81 Kruger Park, South Africa \u2014 Big Five\\n\ud83e\udd8e Gal\u00e1pagos, Ecuador \u2014 evolution in action\\n\ud83d\udc2f Ranthambore, India \u2014 Bengal tigers\\n\ud83c\udf0a Palau, Pacific \u2014 shark sanctuary\\n\\nSee 300+ real zoos on the \ud83d\uddfa\ufe0f Map page!\" },\n  { p: /zoo|zoos/i, a: \"\ud83c\udfdb\ufe0f **Zoos on Animal X:**\\nThe Map page shows **300+ real zoos** worldwide:\\n\u2022 Official name, city, country\\n\u2022 Rating & visitor info\\n\u2022 'Open in Maps' \u2192 Google Maps navigation\\n\u2022 Filter by country or search by name\\n\\nTop global zoos: San Diego, Singapore, Chester, Taronga, Berlin, Prague\" },\n  { p: /reel|reels/i, a: \"\ud83c\udfac **Wildlife Reels:**\\n\u2022 TikTok-style full-screen snap scroll\\n\u2022 1,000+ wildlife reels from 200+ creators\\n\u2022 Double-tap anywhere to like \u2764\ufe0f\\n\u2022 Right sidebar: like, comment, share, save\\n\u2022 Filter by animal category\\n\u2022 Upload your own wildlife video!\" },\n  { p: /feature|what.*can|what.*do|capabilities/i, a: `\ud83d\udc3e **Animal X ${APP_VERSION} \u2014 All Features:**\\n\u2022 \ud83d\udc3e 1,213+ animals with quizzes & special abilities\\n\u2022 \ud83c\udfac TikTok-style wildlife Reels\\n\u2022 \ud83d\uddfa\ufe0f 300+ zoo map + live animal tracking\\n\u2022 \ud83e\udd8b Wildlife migration routes overlay\\n\u2022 \ud83d\udc65 200+ creators to follow & connect with\\n\u2022 \ud83d\udcf8 Posts & 24-hour Stories\\n\u2022 \u2708\ufe0f Safari travel booking deep-links\\n\u2022 \ud83e\uddb4 AI chatbot (that's me!)\\n\u2022 \ud83d\udd35 Blue tick verification\\n\u2022 \ud83d\udd0d Advanced creator search\\n\\nAll **100% FREE** \u2014 forever!` },\n];\n\n/* Suggested questions shown initially */\nconst SUGGESTED = [\n  \"Tell me about Lions \ud83e\udd81\",\n  \"How do I upload a reel?\",\n  \"What's the fastest animal?\",\n  \"How does Live Tracking work?\",\n  \"Tell me about Polar Bears\",\n  \"What is the Great Migration?\",\n  \"How do I get a Blue Tick? \ud83d\udd35\",\n  \"Tell me about the Galapagos\",\n  \"How do ads work?\",\n  \"How do I follow users?\",\n  \"Tell me about Dolphins \ud83d\udc2c\",\n  \"What is Yellowstone Park?\",\n];\n\nconst MENU_ITEMS = [\n  { icon: \"\ud83e\udd81\", label: \"Wildlife AI Chat\", key: \"ai\" },\n  { icon: \"\u2753\", label: \"Help & Support\", key: \"help\", href: \"/help\" },\n  { icon: \"\ud83d\udd12\", label: \"Privacy Policy\", key: \"privacy\", href: \"/privacy\" },\n  { icon: \"\ud83d\udcc4\", label: \"Terms of Service\", key: \"terms\", href: \"/terms\" },\n  { icon: \"\ud83d\udccb\", label: \"Community Guidelines\", key: \"guidelines\", href: \"/guidelines\" },\n  { icon: \"\ud83d\udcde\", label: \"Contact Us\", key: \"contact\", href: \"mailto:wildlifeanimalfight@gmail.com\" },\n  { icon: \"\u2139\ufe0f\", label: `About App (${APP_VERSION})`, key: \"about\" },\n  { icon: \"\ud83d\udea9\", label: \"Report a Problem\", key: \"report\", href: \"mailto:wildlifeanimalfight@gmail.com?subject=Bug+Report+Animal+X\" },\n];\n\nfunction getAIAnswer(query) {\n  const q = query.trim();\n  if (!q) return null;\n\n  for (const entry of KB) {\n    if (entry.p.test(q)) return entry.a;\n  }\n\n  const qLow = q.toLowerCase();\n  const animalMatch = animals.find(a =>\n    qLow.includes(a.name.toLowerCase()) ||\n    (a.baseName && qLow.includes(a.baseName.toLowerCase()))\n  );\n  if (animalMatch) {\n    const a = animalMatch;\n    const catEmoji = { Mammals: \"\ud83e\udd81\", Birds: \"\ud83e\udd85\", Aquatic: \"\ud83d\udc2c\", Reptiles: \"\ud83d\udc0d\", \"Small Creatures\": \"\ud83e\udd8b\", Trees: \"\ud83c\udf33\", Mountains: \"\u26f0\ufe0f\", Sea: \"\ud83c\udf0a\", Desert: \"\ud83c\udfdc\ufe0f\" }[a.category] || \"\ud83d\udc3e\";\n    return `**${a.name}** ${catEmoji}\\n\\n\ud83c\udfe0 **Habitat:** ${a.habitat || \"Various\"}\\n\ud83c\udf7d\ufe0f **Diet:** ${a.diet || \"Unknown\"}\\n\ud83c\udf0d **Found in:** ${a.country || \"Various regions\"}\\n\u23f3 **Lifespan:** ${a.lifespan || \"Unknown\"}\\n\ud83c\udff7\ufe0f **Category:** ${a.category}\\n${a.description ? `\\n\ud83d\udcdd ${a.description.slice(0, 200)}\u2026` : \"\"}\\n\\n\ud83d\udd0d Search for **\"${a.name}\"** in the Animals page to see its full profile, special ability card, and quiz!`;\n  }\n\n  if (/zoo|zoos/i.test(q)) return \"\ud83c\udfdb\ufe0f The **Map** page shows 300+ real zoos worldwide with names, ratings, and Google Maps links!\";\n  if (/reel/i.test(q)) return \"\ud83c\udfac The **Reels** page is a TikTok-style snap-scroll feed. Upload your own wildlife video with the \u2795 button!\";\n  if (/map/i.test(q)) return \"\ud83d\uddfa\ufe0f The **Map** page shows 300+ zoos + 50+ live-tracked animals + migration routes. Toggle layers and search by name!\";\n\n  return null;\n}\n\nfunction FormattedMessage({ text }) {\n  const lines = text.split(\"\\n\");\n  return (\n    <div className=\"wai-msg-content\">\n      {lines.map((line, i) => {\n        if (!line.trim()) return <div key={i} className=\"wai-msg-spacer\" />;\n        const parts = line.split(/\\*\\*(.*?)\\*\\*/g);\n        const isListItem = line.startsWith(\"\u2022\") || line.startsWith(\"-\") || /^[\u2705\u274c\u26a0\ufe0f\ud83d\udeab\ud83d\udd35\ud83d\udfe2\ud83d\udd34]/.test(line);\n        return (\n          <div key={i} className={`wai-line ${isListItem ? \"wai-list-item\" : \"\"}`}>\n            {parts.map((p, j) => j % 2 === 1 ? <strong key={j}>{p}</strong> : p)}\n          </div>\n        );\n      })}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n\nexport default function WildlifeAI() {\n  const [, navigate] = useLocation();\n  const [mode, setMode] = useState(\"closed\"); // \"closed\" | \"menu\" | \"chat\"\n  const [messages, setMessages] = useState([\n    { role: \"ai\", text: `\ud83d\udc4b Welcome to **Wildlife AI** \ud83e\udd81\\n\\nI'm your intelligent wildlife assistant \u2014 powered by a huge local knowledge base covering 1,213+ animals, national parks, zoos, conservation, and all app features.\\n\\nWhat would you like to know?` }\n  ]);\n  const [input, setInput] = useState(\"\");\n  const [typing, setTyping] = useState(false);\n  const [searchQuery, setSearchQuery] = useState(\"\");\n  const messagesEndRef = useRef(null);\n  const inputRef = useRef(null);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (mode === \"chat\") {\n      setTimeout(() => {\n        messagesEndRef.current?.scrollIntoView({ behavior: \"smooth\" });\n        inputRef.current?.focus();\n      }, 100);\n    }\n  }, [mode, messages]);\n\n  const sendMessage = useCallback(async (text) => {\n    const q = (text || input).trim();\n    if (!q) return;\n    setInput(\"\");\n    setMessages(prev => [...prev, { role: \"user\", text: q }]);\n    setTyping(true);\n    await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, q.length > 40 ? 700 : 400));\n    const answer = getAIAnswer(q);\n    const aiText = answer || `\ud83d\udd0d I couldn't find specific info about **\"${q.slice(0, 40)}${q.length > 40 ? \"\u2026\" : \"\"}\"**.\\n\\nTry asking:\\n\u2022 A specific animal (\"Tell me about Sharks\")\\n\u2022 An app feature (\"How do I upload a reel?\")\\n\u2022 Wildlife facts (\"What is migration?\")\\n\u2022 National parks (\"Tell me about Yellowstone\")\\n\\n\ud83d\udce7 For other help: wildlifeanimalfight@gmail.com`;\n    setMessages(prev => [...prev, { role: \"ai\", text: aiText }]);\n    setTyping(false);\n  }, [input]);\n\n  function handleMenuAction(item) {\n    if (item.key === \"ai\") {\n      setMode(\"chat\");\n    } else if (item.key === \"about\") {\n      sendMessage(\"about app\");\n      setMode(\"chat\");\n    } else if (item.href?.startsWith(\"mailto:\")) {\n      window.open(item.href, \"_blank\");\n      setMode(\"closed\");\n    } else if (item.href) {\n      navigate(item.href);\n      setMode(\"closed\");\n    }\n  }\n\n  const filtered = messages.filter(m =>\n    !searchQuery || m.text.toLowerCase().includes(searchQuery.toLowerCase())\n  );\n\n  return (\n    <>\n      {/* Backdrop overlay when menu open */}\n      {mode === \"menu\" && (\n        <div className=\"wai-menu-backdrop\" onClick={() => setMode(\"closed\")} />\n      )}\n\n      {/* FAB Button */}\n      {mode !== \"chat\" && (\n        <button\n          className={`wai-fab ${mode === \"menu\" ? \"wai-fab-active\" : \"\"}`}\n          onClick={() => setMode(m => m === \"menu\" ? \"closed\" : \"menu\")}\n          title=\"Wildlife AI & Quick Access\"\n          aria-label=\"Open Wildlife AI menu\"\n        >\n          {mode === \"menu\" ? <span className=\"wai-fab-close\">\u2715</span> : <span className=\"wai-fab-bone\">\ud83e\uddb4</span>}\n        </button>\n      )}\n\n      {/* Animated Menu */}\n      {mode === \"menu\" && (\n        <div className=\"wai-menu\">\n          {MENU_ITEMS.map((item, i) => (\n            <button\n              key={item.key}\n              className=\"wai-menu-item\"\n              style={{ animationDelay: `${i * 40}ms` }}\n              onClick={() => handleMenuAction(item)}\n            >\n              <span className=\"wai-menu-icon\">{item.icon}</span>\n              <span className=\"wai-menu-label\">{item.label}</span>\n            </button>\n          ))}\n        </div>\n      )}\n\n      {/* Chat Panel */}\n      {mode === \"chat\" && (\n        <div className=\"wai-panel\" role=\"dialog\" aria-label=\"Wildlife AI Chat\">\n          {/* Header */}\n          <div className=\"wai-panel-header\">\n            <button className=\"wai-back-btn\" onClick={() => setMode(\"menu\")} title=\"Back to menu\">\u2190</button>\n            <div className=\"wai-header-info\">\n              <div className=\"wai-header-avatar\">\ud83e\uddb4</div>\n              <div>\n                <div className=\"wai-header-title\">Wildlife AI</div>\n                <div className=\"wai-header-sub\">\ud83d\udfe2 Online \u00b7 Instant answers</div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n            <button className=\"wai-close-btn\" onClick={() => setMode(\"closed\")} aria-label=\"Close\">\u2715</button>\n          </div>\n\n          {/* Search in conversation */}\n          {messages.length > 5 && (\n            <div className=\"wai-chat-search\">\n              <span>\ud83d\udd0d</span>\n              <input\n                placeholder=\"Search conversation\u2026\"\n                value={searchQuery}\n                onChange={e => setSearchQuery(e.target.value)}\n                className=\"wai-search-input\"\n              />\n              {searchQuery && <button onClick={() => setSearchQuery(\"\")} className=\"wai-search-clear\">\u2715</button>}\n            </div>\n          )}\n\n          {/* Messages */}\n          <div className=\"wai-messages\">\n            {filtered.map((m, i) => (\n              <div key={i} className={`wai-msg-row ${m.role}`}>\n                {m.role === \"ai\" && (\n                  <div className=\"wai-msg-avatar-sm\">\ud83e\uddb4</div>\n                )}\n                <div className={`wai-bubble ${m.role}`}>\n                  <FormattedMessage text={m.text} />\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            ))}\n            {typing && (\n              <div className=\"wai-msg-row ai\">\n                <div className=\"wai-msg-avatar-sm\">\ud83e\uddb4</div>\n                <div className=\"wai-bubble ai wai-typing\">\n                  <span className=\"wai-dot\" /><span className=\"wai-dot\" /><span className=\"wai-dot\" />\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            )}\n            <div ref={messagesEndRef} />\n          </div>\n\n          {/* Suggested questions */}\n          {messages.length <= 2 && !typing && (\n            <div className=\"wai-suggestions\">\n              <div className=\"wai-suggestions-label\">\ud83d\udca1 Try asking:</div>\n              <div className=\"wai-suggestions-scroll\">\n                {SUGGESTED.map((s, i) => (\n                  <button key={i} className=\"wai-chip\" onClick={() => sendMessage(s)}>\n                    {s}\n                  </button>\n                ))}\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          )}\n\n          {/* Input row */}\n          <div className=\"wai-input-row\">\n            <input\n              ref={inputRef}\n              className=\"wai-input\"\n              placeholder=\"Ask about animals, app features, conservation\u2026\"\n              value={input}\n              onChange={e => setInput(e.target.value)}\n              onKeyDown={e => {\n                if (e.key === \"Enter\" && !e.shiftKey) { e.preventDefault(); sendMessage(); }\n              }}\n            />\n            <button\n              className=\"wai-send-btn\"\n              onClick={() => sendMessage()}\n              disabled={!input.trim() || typing}\n              aria-label=\"Send\"\n            >\n              \u27a4\n            </button>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      )}\n    </>\n  );\n}\n"}}, {"type": "tool", "name": "write", "arguments": {"file_path": "artifacts/animal-x/src/pages/PrivacyPolicy.jsx", "content": "import { useLocation } from \"wouter\";\n\nexport default function PrivacyPolicy() {\n  const [, navigate] = useLocation();\n  return (\n    <div className=\"policy-page\">\n      <div className=\"policy-header\">\n        <button className=\"policy-back\" onClick={() => navigate(-1)}>\u2190 Back</button>\n        <div className=\"policy-header-icon\">\ud83d\udd12</div>\n        <h1 className=\"policy-title\">Privacy Policy</h1>\n        <p className=\"policy-subtitle\">Last updated: June 2026 \u00b7 Animal X v2.5</p>\n      </div>\n\n      <div className=\"policy-body\">\n\n        <div className=\"policy-section\">\n          <h2>1. Introduction</h2>\n          <p>\n            Welcome to <strong>Animal X</strong> (\"we,\" \"our,\" or \"us\"). We are committed to protecting your personal information and your right to privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, store, and share information when you use our wildlife social media application.\n          </p>\n          <p>By using Animal X, you agree to the collection and use of information in accordance with this policy.</p>\n        </div>\n\n        <div className=\"policy-section\">\n          <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>\n          <div className=\"policy-card green\">\n            <h3>\u2705 Information You Provide</h3>\n            <ul>\n              <li><strong>Account Information:</strong> Email address, display name, and password (password stored as encrypted hash only)</li>\n              <li><strong>Profile Data:</strong> Profile photo, cover image, bio, country, and username</li>\n              <li><strong>Content:</strong> Wildlife videos, photos, captions, hashtags, and comments you upload</li>\n              <li><strong>Interactions:</strong> Likes, follows, shares, and comments on other users' content</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n          <div className=\"policy-card blue\">\n            <h3>\ud83d\udd35 Information Collected Automatically</h3>\n            <ul>\n              <li><strong>Usage data:</strong> Pages visited, time spent, features used</li>\n              <li><strong>Device data:</strong> Browser type, operating system, device type</li>\n              <li><strong>Location:</strong> GPS location (only when you use the Map feature, with your permission)</li>\n              <li><strong>Log data:</strong> IP address, crash reports, and performance data</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div className=\"policy-section\">\n          <h2>3. How We Use Your Information</h2>\n          <ul className=\"policy-list\">\n            <li>\ud83e\udd81 To provide, operate, and improve Animal X services</li>\n            <li>\ud83d\udd10 To authenticate your account and keep it secure</li>\n            <li>\ud83d\udd14 To send notifications about follows, likes, and platform updates</li>\n            <li>\ud83e\udd16 To power AI content moderation ensuring only wildlife content is posted</li>\n            <li>\ud83d\udcca To analyse usage patterns and improve user experience</li>\n            <li>\ud83d\udce2 To display relevant wildlife content in your personalised feed</li>\n            <li>\u2696\ufe0f To enforce our Community Guidelines and Terms of Service</li>\n          </ul>\n        </div>\n\n        <div className=\"policy-section\">\n          <h2>4. Data Storage & Security</h2>\n          <div className=\"policy-card green\">\n            <h3>\ud83d\udee1\ufe0f Firebase Security</h3>\n            <p>All your data is stored on <strong>Google Firebase</strong> \u2014 one of the world's most secure cloud platforms:</p>\n            <ul>\n              <li>All data encrypted in transit (HTTPS/TLS)</li>\n              <li>Passwords are never stored in plain text</li>\n              <li>Firebase Firestore Security Rules restrict data access to authorised users only</li>\n              <li>Object Storage uses signed URLs with limited-time access</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div className=\"policy-section\">\n          <h2>5. Data Sharing</h2>\n          <div className=\"policy-card red\">\n            <h3>\ud83d\udeab What We Never Do</h3>\n            <ul>\n              <li>We <strong>never sell</strong> your personal data to advertisers or third parties</li>\n              <li>We <strong>never share</strong> your email with other users (only admin sees emails)</li>\n              <li>We <strong>never track</strong> you across other websites or apps</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n          <h3 style={{ marginTop: 16 }}>Limited Sharing:</h3>\n          <ul className=\"policy-list\">\n            <li><strong>Public content:</strong> Reels, posts, and profile info you make public are visible to all users</li>\n            <li><strong>Service providers:</strong> Google Firebase for data storage and authentication</li>\n            <li><strong>Legal compliance:</strong> If required by law, court order, or to protect safety</li>\n          </ul>\n        </div>\n\n        <div className=\"policy-section\">\n          <h2>6. Your Rights</h2>\n          <ul className=\"policy-list\">\n            <li>\ud83d\udccb <strong>Access:</strong> Request a copy of your personal data</li>\n            <li>\u270f\ufe0f <strong>Correction:</strong> Update your profile data at any time</li>\n            <li>\ud83d\uddd1\ufe0f <strong>Deletion:</strong> Request deletion of your account and data</li>\n            <li>\u23f8\ufe0f <strong>Restriction:</strong> Limit how we process your data</li>\n            <li>\ud83d\udce6 <strong>Portability:</strong> Receive your data in a portable format</li>\n          </ul>\n          <p>To exercise any of these rights, contact us at: <a href=\"mailto:wildlifeanimalfight@gmail.com\" className=\"policy-link\">wildlifeanimalfight@gmail.com</a></p>\n        </div>\n\n        <div className=\"policy-section\">\n          <h2>7. Children's Privacy</h2>\n          <p>Animal X is not intended for children under the age of <strong>13</strong>. We do not knowingly collect personal data from children under 13. If you believe a child under 13 has provided us with personal information, please contact us immediately.</p>\n        </div>\n\n        <div className=\"policy-section\">\n          <h2>8. Cookies & Local Storage</h2>\n          <p>We use browser local storage to:</p>\n          <ul className=\"policy-list\">\n            <li>Save your login session (Firebase Auth token)</li>\n            <li>Cache liked reels for instant UI response</li>\n            <li>Store your app preferences (theme, saved reels)</li>\n          </ul>\n          <p>We do not use third-party advertising cookies.</p>\n        </div>\n\n        <div className=\"policy-section\">\n          <h2>9. Changes to This Policy</h2>\n          <p>We may update this Privacy Policy periodically. We will notify you of significant changes via an in-app broadcast or notification. Continued use of Animal X after changes constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.</p>\n        </div>\n\n        <div className=\"policy-section\">\n          <h2>10. Contact Us</h2>\n          <div className=\"policy-contact-box\">\n            <div>\ud83d\udce7 <strong>Email:</strong> <a href=\"mailto:wildlifeanimalfight@gmail.com\" className=\"policy-link\">wildlifeanimalfight@gmail.com</a></div>\n            <div>\ud83d\udcf8 <strong>Instagram:</strong> @wildlifeanimalfight</div>\n            <div>\u25b6\ufe0f <strong>YouTube:</strong> wildlifeanimalfight</div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div className=\"policy-footer-note\">\n          \u00a9 2026 Animal X \u00b7 All rights reserved \u00b7 <a href=\"mailto:wildlifeanimalfight@gmail.com\" className=\"policy-link\">Contact Us</a>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n"}}, {"type": "tool", "name": "write", "arguments": {"file_path": "artifacts/animal-x/src/pages/TermsOfService.jsx", "content": "import { useLocation } from \"wouter\";\n\nexport default function TermsOfService() {\n  const [, navigate] = useLocation();\n  return (\n    <div className=\"policy-page\">\n      <div className=\"policy-header\">\n        <button className=\"policy-back\" onClick={() => navigate(-1)}>\u2190 Back</button>\n        <div className=\"policy-header-icon\">\ud83d\udcc4</div>\n        <h1 className=\"policy-title\">Terms of Service</h1>\n        <p className=\"policy-subtitle\">Last updated: June 2026 \u00b7 Animal X v2.5</p>\n      </div>\n\n      <div className=\"policy-body\">\n\n        <div className=\"policy-section\">\n          <h2>1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>\n          <p>By accessing or using <strong>Animal X</strong>, you agree to be bound by these Terms of Service (\"Terms\"). If you do not agree to these Terms, you may not use the app. These Terms apply to all users, visitors, and contributors of Animal X.</p>\n          <div className=\"policy-card blue\">\n            <p><strong>Age requirement:</strong> You must be at least <strong>13 years old</strong> to create an account. Users under 18 require parental consent.</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div className=\"policy-section\">\n          <h2>2. Account Responsibilities</h2>\n          <ul className=\"policy-list\">\n            <li>You are responsible for maintaining the confidentiality of your account credentials</li>\n            <li>You must provide accurate information when creating your account</li>\n            <li>You may not share your account with others or use another person's account</li>\n            <li>You are responsible for all activity that occurs under your account</li>\n            <li>You must notify us immediately if you suspect unauthorised access</li>\n          </ul>\n        </div>\n\n        <div className=\"policy-section\">\n          <h2>3. Permitted Use</h2>\n          <div className=\"policy-card green\">\n            <h3>\u2705 What You Can Do</h3>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Upload and share wildlife, nature, and animal-related content</li>\n              <li>Follow other wildlife creators and like their content</li>\n              <li>Comment respectfully on reels and posts</li>\n              <li>Use the Map to find zoos, track animals, and explore migration routes</li>\n              <li>Run wildlife-related advertisements through our Ads platform</li>\n              <li>Use the AI chatbot for wildlife information</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div className=\"policy-section\">\n          <h2>4. Prohibited Content & Behaviour</h2>\n          <div className=\"policy-card red\">\n            <h3>\ud83d\udeab Strictly Prohibited</h3>\n            <ul>\n              <li><strong>Non-wildlife content:</strong> Videos, photos, or posts unrelated to animals, nature, or wildlife</li>\n              <li><strong>Harmful content:</strong> Violence, animal cruelty, abuse, or exploitation of any kind</li>\n              <li><strong>Hate speech:</strong> Content promoting discrimination based on race, religion, gender, or other characteristics</li>\n              <li><strong>Spam:</strong> Automated posting, fake engagement, or repeated unwanted messages</li>\n              <li><strong>Misinformation:</strong> Deliberately false wildlife facts or dangerous advice</li>\n              <li><strong>Copyright infringement:</strong> Posting content you do not own without permission</li>\n              <li><strong>Illegal activity:</strong> Poaching, illegal wildlife trade, or any content promoting illegal acts</li>\n              <li><strong>Privacy violations:</strong> Sharing others' private information without consent</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div className=\"policy-section\">\n          <h2>5. Violation Consequences</h2>\n          <div className=\"policy-card orange\">\n            <h3>\u26a0\ufe0f Enforcement Actions</h3>\n            <ul>\n              <li><strong>Strike 1:</strong> Warning issued, content removed</li>\n              <li><strong>Strike 2:</strong> Second warning, content removed, temporary restrictions</li>\n              <li><strong>Strike 3:</strong> 30-day upload ban</li>\n              <li><strong>Severe violation:</strong> Immediate permanent account ban</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n          <p>Animal X reserves the right to remove any content and suspend or terminate any account at our discretion, with or without prior notice, for violations of these Terms.</p>\n        </div>\n\n        <div className=\"policy-section\">\n          <h2>6. Content Ownership & Licence</h2>\n          <ul className=\"policy-list\">\n            <li>You retain ownership of content you upload to Animal X</li>\n            <li>By uploading content, you grant Animal X a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free licence to display and distribute your content on the platform</li>\n            <li>You confirm you have the right to upload all content you post (no copyright infringement)</li>\n            <li>Animal X's own content, design, and branding remain our intellectual property</li>\n          </ul>\n        </div>\n\n        <div className=\"policy-section\">\n          <h2>7. Advertisements</h2>\n          <ul className=\"policy-list\">\n            <li>Advertisements must be wildlife-related and comply with all content guidelines</li>\n            <li>Payments are non-refundable once an ad campaign is activated</li>\n            <li>Animal X reserves the right to reject any advertisement that violates our policies</li>\n            <li>Ad placement and timing are at Animal X's discretion</li>\n          </ul>\n        </div>\n\n        <div className=\"policy-section\">\n          <h2>8. Disclaimers & Limitation of Liability</h2>\n          <p>Animal X is provided \"as is\" without warranty of any kind. We do not guarantee:</p>\n          <ul className=\"policy-list\">\n            <li>Uninterrupted or error-free service</li>\n            <li>The accuracy of all wildlife information presented</li>\n            <li>The availability of any specific feature at any time</li>\n          </ul>\n          <p>To the maximum extent permitted by law, Animal X shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, or consequential damages arising from your use of the app.</p>\n        </div>\n\n        <div className=\"policy-section\">\n          <h2>9. Governing Law</h2>\n          <p>These Terms shall be governed by applicable laws. Any disputes shall be resolved through good-faith negotiation. If unresolved, disputes shall be subject to binding arbitration.</p>\n        </div>\n\n        <div className=\"policy-section\">\n          <h2>10. Changes to Terms</h2>\n          <p>We reserve the right to modify these Terms at any time. We will notify users of material changes via in-app notifications. Continued use of Animal X after changes constitutes acceptance.</p>\n        </div>\n\n        <div className=\"policy-section\">\n          <h2>11. Contact</h2>\n          <div className=\"policy-contact-box\">\n            <div>\ud83d\udce7 <strong>Email:</strong> <a href=\"mailto:wildlifeanimalfight@gmail.com\" className=\"policy-link\">wildlifeanimalfight@gmail.com</a></div>\n            <div>\ud83d\udcf8 <strong>Instagram:</strong> @wildlifeanimalfight</div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div className=\"policy-footer-note\">\n          \u00a9 2026 Animal X \u00b7 All rights reserved\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n"}}, {"type": "tool", "name": "write", "arguments": {"file_path": "artifacts/animal-x/src/pages/CommunityGuidelines.jsx", "content": "import { useLocation } from \"wouter\";\n\nexport default function CommunityGuidelines() {\n  const [, navigate] = useLocation();\n  return (\n    <div className=\"policy-page\">\n      <div className=\"policy-header\">\n        <button className=\"policy-back\" onClick={() => navigate(-1)}>\u2190 Back</button>\n        <div className=\"policy-header-icon\">\ud83d\udccb</div>\n        <h1 className=\"policy-title\">Community Guidelines</h1>\n        <p className=\"policy-subtitle\">Last updated: June 2026 \u00b7 Animal X v2.5</p>\n      </div>\n\n      <div className=\"policy-body\">\n\n        <div className=\"policy-section\">\n          <div className=\"policy-intro-card\">\n            <div style={{ fontSize: \"2.5rem\" }}>\ud83e\udd81</div>\n            <p>Animal X is a community built around <strong>wildlife, nature, and conservation</strong>. Our guidelines exist to protect animals, creators, and the environment we all love. Every user has a responsibility to uphold these standards.</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div className=\"policy-section\">\n          <h2>\u2705 What We Celebrate</h2>\n          <div className=\"policy-grid\">\n            <div className=\"policy-good-card\">\n              <div className=\"policy-good-icon\">\ud83c\udfac</div>\n              <h3>Wildlife Content</h3>\n              <p>Videos, photos, and stories of animals in their natural habitat, zoos, sanctuaries, or wildlife reserves.</p>\n            </div>\n            <div className=\"policy-good-card\">\n              <div className=\"policy-good-icon\">\ud83c\udf3f</div>\n              <h3>Nature & Ecosystems</h3>\n              <p>Forests, oceans, mountains, deserts, rainforests, and the incredible biodiversity they support.</p>\n            </div>\n            <div className=\"policy-good-card\">\n              <div className=\"policy-good-icon\">\ud83d\udd2c</div>\n              <h3>Wildlife Science</h3>\n              <p>Conservation research, animal behaviour studies, migration patterns, and ecological discoveries.</p>\n            </div>\n            <div className=\"policy-good-card\">\n              <div className=\"policy-good-icon\">\ud83d\udc9a</div>\n              <h3>Conservation Efforts</h3>\n              <p>Anti-poaching campaigns, habitat restoration, endangered species protection, and community programmes.</p>\n            </div>\n            <div className=\"policy-good-card\">\n              <div className=\"policy-good-icon\">\ud83e\udded</div>\n              <h3>Safari & Travel</h3>\n              <p>Responsible wildlife tourism, national park visits, and eco-friendly travel experiences.</p>\n            </div>\n            <div className=\"policy-good-card\">\n              <div className=\"policy-good-icon\">\ud83d\udcda</div>\n              <h3>Education</h3>\n              <p>Animal facts, wildlife quizzes, habitat guides, and educational content for all ages.</p>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div className=\"policy-section\">\n          <h2>\ud83d\udeab What Is Not Allowed</h2>\n\n          <div className=\"policy-rule-block\">\n            <div className=\"policy-rule-badge red\">\ud83d\udeab Critical</div>\n            <h3>Animal Cruelty & Harm</h3>\n            <p>Any content depicting, promoting, or glorifying harm, abuse, torture, or exploitation of animals. This includes poaching, illegal wildlife trade, or any acts of violence toward animals. Immediate permanent ban.</p>\n          </div>\n\n          <div className=\"policy-rule-block\">\n            <div className=\"policy-rule-badge red\">\ud83d\udeab Prohibited</div>\n            <h3>Non-Wildlife Content</h3>\n            <p>Music videos, personal vlogs, gaming clips, cooking videos, fashion content, or anything unrelated to wildlife, nature, or animals. First offence = Strike. Third offence = 30-day upload ban.</p>\n          </div>\n\n          <div className=\"policy-rule-block\">\n            <div className=\"policy-rule-badge red\">\ud83d\udeab Prohibited</div>\n            <h3>Hate Speech & Discrimination</h3>\n            <p>Content targeting individuals or groups based on race, ethnicity, religion, gender, sexuality, disability, or nationality. Zero tolerance \u2014 immediate account suspension.</p>\n          </div>\n\n          <div className=\"policy-rule-block\">\n            <div className=\"policy-rule-badge orange\">\u26a0\ufe0f Restricted</div>\n            <h3>Misinformation</h3>\n            <p>Deliberately false animal facts, misleading conservation claims, or dangerous misinformation about wildlife. Content will be removed and fact-checked.</p>\n          </div>\n\n          <div className=\"policy-rule-block\">\n            <div className=\"policy-rule-badge orange\">\u26a0\ufe0f Restricted</div>\n            <h3>Spam & Fake Engagement</h3>\n            <p>Automated likes, fake followers, repetitive comments, or any form of artificial engagement manipulation. Account may be suspended.</p>\n          </div>\n\n          <div className=\"policy-rule-block\">\n            <div className=\"policy-rule-badge orange\">\u26a0\ufe0f Restricted</div>\n            <h3>Copyright Violations</h3>\n            <p>Uploading copyrighted video, music, or photos without permission. Always use content you own or have rights to.</p>\n          </div>\n\n          <div className=\"policy-rule-block\">\n            <div className=\"policy-rule-badge orange\">\u26a0\ufe0f Restricted</div>\n            <h3>Privacy Violations</h3>\n            <p>Sharing private information, photos, or location data of individuals without their consent.</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div className=\"policy-section\">\n          <h2>\u26a0\ufe0f Strike System</h2>\n          <div className=\"policy-strike-timeline\">\n            <div className=\"policy-strike-step green\">\n              <div className=\"policy-strike-num\">1</div>\n              <div>\n                <strong>First Violation</strong>\n                <p>Content removed + warning issued. Strike recorded on your account.</p>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n            <div className=\"policy-strike-step orange\">\n              <div className=\"policy-strike-num\">2</div>\n              <div>\n                <strong>Second Violation</strong>\n                <p>Content removed + final warning. Restricted features may apply.</p>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n            <div className=\"policy-strike-step red\">\n              <div className=\"policy-strike-num\">3</div>\n              <div>\n                <strong>Third Violation</strong>\n                <p>30-day upload ban. All new content blocked for one month.</p>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n            <div className=\"policy-strike-step black\">\n              <div className=\"policy-strike-num\">\ud83d\udeab</div>\n              <div>\n                <strong>Severe Violation</strong>\n                <p>Immediate permanent account ban, regardless of strike count.</p>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div className=\"policy-section\">\n          <h2>\ud83d\udea9 How to Report</h2>\n          <div className=\"policy-card blue\">\n            <h3>Reporting Content</h3>\n            <ol className=\"policy-list\">\n              <li>Tap \u22ee (three dots) on any reel, post, or comment</li>\n              <li>Select <strong>\"Report\"</strong></li>\n              <li>Choose the violation type from the list</li>\n              <li>Submit your report</li>\n            </ol>\n            <p style={{ marginTop: 10 }}>Our moderation team reviews all reports within <strong>24 hours</strong>. Severe violations are acted upon immediately.</p>\n          </div>\n          <p style={{ marginTop: 12 }}>For urgent reports: <a href=\"mailto:wildlifeanimalfight@gmail.com\" className=\"policy-link\">wildlifeanimalfight@gmail.com</a></p>\n        </div>\n\n        <div className=\"policy-section\">\n          <h2>\ud83c\udf0d Our Mission</h2>\n          <div className=\"policy-intro-card\">\n            <p>Animal X exists to build the world's most passionate wildlife community \u2014 where every post celebrates life on Earth, educates future conservationists, and protects the species we share our planet with.</p>\n            <p style={{ marginTop: 10 }}><strong>Together, we make a difference.</strong> \ud83c\udf3f</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div className=\"policy-footer-note\">\n          \u00a9 2026 Animal X \u00b7 <a href=\"mailto:wildlifeanimalfight@gmail.com\" className=\"policy-link\">wildlifeanimalfight@gmail.com</a>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n"}}, {"type": "tool", "name": "write", "arguments": {"file_path": "artifacts/animal-x/src/components/AdminTestingPanel.jsx", "content": "import { useState, useEffect, useCallback } from \"react\";\n\nconst MODES = {\n  live: { label: \"\ud83d\udfe2 Public Live Mode\", desc: \"Normal operation \u2014 all users see stable features\", color: \"#22c55e\" },\n  testing: { label: \"\ud83e\uddea Testing Mode\", desc: \"Beta features visible only to super admin\", color: \"#f59e0b\" },\n  emergency: { label: \"\ud83c\udd98 Emergency Mode\", desc: \"Last stable backup restored \u2014 broken features disabled\", color: \"#ef4444\" },\n};\n\nfunction getBackups() {\n  try { return JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(\"ax_backups\") || \"[]\"); } catch { return []; }\n}\n\nfunction createBackup() {\n  const snap = {\n    timestamp: Date.now(),\n    version: \"2.5.0\",\n    mode: localStorage.getItem(\"ax_mode\") || \"live\",\n    customAnimals: JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(\"ax_custom_animals\") || \"[]\"),\n    savedReels: JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(\"ax_saved_reels\") || \"{}\"),\n    theme: localStorage.getItem(\"ax_theme\") || \"dark\",\n    profile: JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(\"ax_profile_cache\") || \"{}\"),\n  };\n  const backups = getBackups();\n  backups.unshift(snap);\n  if (backups.length > 10) backups.splice(10);\n  localStorage.setItem(\"ax_backups\", JSON.stringify(backups));\n  localStorage.setItem(\"ax_last_backup\", String(Date.now()));\n  return snap;\n}\n\nfunction restoreBackup(snap) {\n  if (!snap) return false;\n  try {\n    if (snap.customAnimals) localStorage.setItem(\"ax_custom_animals\", JSON.stringify(snap.customAnimals));\n    if (snap.savedReels) localStorage.setItem(\"ax_saved_reels\", JSON.stringify(snap.savedReels));\n    if (snap.theme) localStorage.setItem(\"ax_theme\", snap.theme);\n    localStorage.setItem(\"ax_mode\", \"live\");\n    return true;\n  } catch { return false; }\n}\n\nfunction downloadJSON(data, filename) {\n  const blob = new Blob([JSON.stringify(data, null, 2)], { type: \"application/json\" });\n  const url = URL.createObjectURL(blob);\n  const a = document.createElement(\"a\");\n  a.href = url;\n  a.download = filename;\n  a.click();\n  URL.revokeObjectURL(url);\n}\n\nfunction timeAgo(ts) {\n  if (!ts) return \"never\";\n  const diff = Date.now() - ts;\n  if (diff < 60000) return \"just now\";\n  if (diff < 3600000) return Math.floor(diff / 60000) + \"m ago\";\n  if (diff < 86400000) return Math.floor(diff / 3600000) + \"h ago\";\n  return Math.floor(diff / 86400000) + \"d ago\";\n}\n\nexport default function AdminTestingPanel({ open, onClose }) {\n  const [mode, setMode] = useState(() => localStorage.getItem(\"ax_mode\") || \"live\");\n  const [backups, setBackups] = useState(getBackups);\n  const [lastBackup, setLastBackup] = useState(() => Number(localStorage.getItem(\"ax_last_backup\") || 0));\n  const [activeTab, setActiveTab] = useState(\"modes\");\n  const [toast, setToast] = useState(null);\n  const [restoreLoading, setRestoreLoading] = useState(false);\n  const [betaFeatures, setBetaFeatures] = useState(() => {\n    try { return JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(\"ax_beta_features\") || \"{}\"); } catch { return {}; }\n  });\n\n  const BETA_FEATURES = [\n    { key: \"advancedReelAnalytics\", label: \"Advanced Reel Analytics\", desc: \"Show view duration, engagement rate, and drop-off data\" },\n    { key: \"aiTagging\", label: \"AI Auto-Tagging\", desc: \"Automatically tag animal species in uploaded videos\" },\n    { key: \"liveStreaming\", label: \"Live Streaming\", desc: \"Allow users to stream wildlife events live\" },\n    { key: \"collaborativeReels\", label: \"Collaborative Reels\", desc: \"Two creators can merge their reels into one\" },\n    { key: \"augmentedReality\", label: \"AR Animal Overlays\", desc: \"View 3D animal models in your camera\" },\n  ];\n\n  const showToast = useCallback((msg) => {\n    setToast(msg);\n    setTimeout(() => setToast(null), 3000);\n  }, []);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (!open) return;\n    const now = Date.now();\n    const last = Number(localStorage.getItem(\"ax_last_backup\") || 0);\n    if (now - last > 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000) {\n      const snap = createBackup();\n      setBackups(getBackups());\n      setLastBackup(snap.timestamp);\n      showToast(\"\ud83d\uddc2\ufe0f Auto daily backup created\");\n    }\n  }, [open, showToast]);\n\n  function applyMode(newMode) {\n    setMode(newMode);\n    localStorage.setItem(\"ax_mode\", newMode);\n    showToast(`${MODES[newMode].label} activated!`);\n  }\n\n  function handleManualBackup() {\n    const snap = createBackup();\n    setBackups(getBackups());\n    setLastBackup(snap.timestamp);\n    showToast(\"\u2705 Backup created successfully!\");\n  }\n\n  function handleDownloadBackup() {\n    const backupData = {\n      timestamp: Date.now(),\n      version: \"2.5.0\",\n      backups: getBackups(),\n      settings: {\n        mode: localStorage.getItem(\"ax_mode\"),\n        theme: localStorage.getItem(\"ax_theme\"),\n        betaFeatures: JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(\"ax_beta_features\") || \"{}\"),\n        customAnimals: JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(\"ax_custom_animals\") || \"[]\"),\n        savedReels: JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(\"ax_saved_reels\") || \"{}\"),\n      }\n    };\n    downloadJSON(backupData, `animalx-backup-${new Date().toISOString().slice(0,10)}.json`);\n    showToast(\"\ud83d\udce6 Backup downloaded!\");\n  }\n\n  function handleRestoreFile(e) {\n    const file = e.target.files?.[0];\n    if (!file) return;\n    setRestoreLoading(true);\n    const reader = new FileReader();\n    reader.onload = (ev) => {\n      try {\n        const data = JSON.parse(ev.target.result);\n        const snap = data.backups?.[0] || data.settings;\n        if (!snap) throw new Error(\"Invalid backup file format\");\n        const ok = restoreBackup(snap);\n        if (ok) {\n          setBackups(getBackups());\n          setMode(\"live\");\n          showToast(\"\u2705 Backup restored successfully! Refresh the app.\");\n        } else {\n          showToast(\"\u274c Restore failed \u2014 invalid backup\");\n        }\n      } catch {\n        showToast(\"\u274c Invalid backup file\");\n      }\n      setRestoreLoading(false);\n    };\n    reader.readAsText(file);\n    e.target.value = \"\";\n  }\n\n  function handleEmergencyRestore() {\n    if (!window.confirm(\"\ud83c\udd98 Emergency Restore will:\\n\\n\u2022 Switch to the last stable backup\\n\u2022 Disable broken features\\n\u2022 Preserve all user accounts and reels\\n\\nContinue?\")) return;\n    const bkps = getBackups();\n    if (bkps.length === 0) {\n      const snap = createBackup();\n      setBackups(getBackups());\n      setLastBackup(snap.timestamp);\n      showToast(\"\u26a0\ufe0f No prior backup \u2014 created fresh backup and set live mode\");\n      applyMode(\"live\");\n      return;\n    }\n    restoreBackup(bkps[0]);\n    setBackups(getBackups());\n    applyMode(\"emergency\");\n    setTimeout(() => {\n      applyMode(\"live\");\n      showToast(\"\u2705 Emergency restore complete \u2014 switched to Live mode\");\n    }, 2000);\n  }\n\n  function toggleBetaFeature(key) {\n    const next = { ...betaFeatures, [key]: !betaFeatures[key] };\n    setBetaFeatures(next);\n    localStorage.setItem(\"ax_beta_features\", JSON.stringify(next));\n  }\n\n  if (!open) return null;\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"atp-backdrop\" onClick={e => e.target === e.currentTarget && onClose()}>\n      <div className=\"atp-panel\">\n\n        {/* Header */}\n        <div className=\"atp-header\">\n          <div className=\"atp-header-icon\">\ud83e\uddea</div>\n          <div>\n            <div className=\"atp-header-title\">Admin Testing Panel</div>\n            <div className=\"atp-header-sub\">Super Admin \u00b7 Animal X v2.5</div>\n          </div>\n          <button className=\"atp-close\" onClick={onClose}>\u2715</button>\n        </div>\n\n        {/* Mode indicator */}\n        <div className=\"atp-mode-banner\" style={{ borderColor: MODES[mode].color + \"40\", background: MODES[mode].color + \"15\" }}>\n          <span style={{ color: MODES[mode].color, fontWeight: 700 }}>{MODES[mode].label}</span>\n          <span className=\"atp-mode-desc\">{MODES[mode].desc}</span>\n        </div>\n\n        {/* Tabs */}\n        <div className=\"atp-tabs\">\n          {[\n            { key: \"modes\", label: \"\ud83d\uddc2\ufe0f Modes\" },\n            { key: \"testing\", label: \"\ud83e\uddea Beta\" },\n            { key: \"backup\", label: \"\ud83d\udcbe Backup\" },\n          ].map(t => (\n            <button\n              key={t.key}\n              className={`atp-tab ${activeTab === t.key ? \"active\" : \"\"}`}\n              onClick={() => setActiveTab(t.key)}\n            >\n              {t.label}\n            </button>\n          ))}\n        </div>\n\n        {/* Tab: Modes */}\n        {activeTab === \"modes\" && (\n          <div className=\"atp-tab-body\">\n            <div className=\"atp-section-label\">Select App Mode</div>\n            {Object.entries(MODES).map(([key, info]) => (\n              <button\n                key={key}\n                className={`atp-mode-btn ${mode === key ? \"active\" : \"\"}`}\n                style={mode === key ? { borderColor: info.color, background: info.color + \"20\" } : {}}\n                onClick={() => applyMode(key)}\n              >\n                <span className=\"atp-mode-btn-label\" style={mode === key ? { color: info.color } : {}}>{info.label}</span>\n                <span className=\"atp-mode-btn-desc\">{info.desc}</span>\n                {mode === key && <span className=\"atp-mode-active-badge\">\u25cf ACTIVE</span>}\n              </button>\n            ))}\n\n            <div className=\"atp-action-row\">\n              <button\n                className=\"atp-action-btn testing\"\n                onClick={() => applyMode(\"testing\")}\n              >\n                \ud83e\uddea Enable Testing\n              </button>\n              <button\n                className=\"atp-action-btn live\"\n                onClick={() => applyMode(\"live\")}\n              >\n                \ud83d\ude80 Push To Public\n              </button>\n            </div>\n            <button\n              className=\"atp-action-btn emergency\"\n              onClick={handleEmergencyRestore}\n            >\n              \ud83c\udd98 Emergency Restore\n            </button>\n\n            <div className=\"atp-mode-help\">\n              <strong>Testing Mode:</strong> Only super admin sees beta features. Public users see normal app.<br />\n              <strong>Push To Public:</strong> Activates all tested features for all users immediately.<br />\n              <strong>Emergency Restore:</strong> Reverts to last stable backup and disables broken features.\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        )}\n\n        {/* Tab: Beta Features */}\n        {activeTab === \"testing\" && (\n          <div className=\"atp-tab-body\">\n            <div className=\"atp-section-label\">\n              Beta Features\n              {mode !== \"testing\" && (\n                <span className=\"atp-beta-note\"> \u2014 switch to Testing Mode to preview</span>\n              )}\n            </div>\n            {BETA_FEATURES.map(f => (\n              <div key={f.key} className={`atp-feature-row ${betaFeatures[f.key] ? \"on\" : \"\"}`}>\n                <div className=\"atp-feature-info\">\n                  <div className=\"atp-feature-label\">{f.label}</div>\n                  <div className=\"atp-feature-desc\">{f.desc}</div>\n                </div>\n                <label className=\"atp-toggle-switch\">\n                  <input\n                    type=\"checkbox\"\n                    checked={!!betaFeatures[f.key]}\n                    onChange={() => toggleBetaFeature(f.key)}\n                  />\n                  <span className=\"atp-toggle-track\" />\n                </label>\n              </div>\n            ))}\n            <div className=\"atp-mode-help\">\n              Beta features are visible only when in Testing Mode and only to the super admin account. Push To Public to enable for all users.\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        )}\n\n        {/* Tab: Backup */}\n        {activeTab === \"backup\" && (\n          <div className=\"atp-tab-body\">\n            <div className=\"atp-backup-status\">\n              <span>Last backup: <strong>{timeAgo(lastBackup)}</strong></span>\n              <span className=\"atp-backup-count\">{backups.length} snapshots saved</span>\n            </div>\n\n            <div className=\"atp-action-row\">\n              <button className=\"atp-action-btn live\" onClick={handleManualBackup}>\n                \ud83d\uddc2\ufe0f Create Backup\n              </button>\n              <button className=\"atp-action-btn testing\" onClick={handleDownloadBackup}>\n                \ud83d\udce6 Download ZIP\n              </button>\n            </div>\n\n            <label className={`atp-action-btn ${restoreLoading ? \"disabled\" : \"emergency\"}`} style={{ cursor: restoreLoading ? \"default\" : \"pointer\" }}>\n              {restoreLoading ? \"Restoring\u2026\" : \"\ud83d\udcc2 Restore Backup\"}\n              <input type=\"file\" accept=\".json\" style={{ display: \"none\" }} onChange={handleRestoreFile} disabled={restoreLoading} />\n            </label>\n\n            {backups.length > 0 && (\n              <>\n                <div className=\"atp-section-label\" style={{ marginTop: 16 }}>Backup History</div>\n                <div className=\"atp-backup-list\">\n                  {backups.slice(0, 5).map((b, i) => (\n                    <div key={i} className=\"atp-backup-item\">\n                      <span className=\"atp-backup-time\">{timeAgo(b.timestamp)}</span>\n                      <span className=\"atp-backup-mode\">{MODES[b.mode]?.label || b.mode}</span>\n                      <button\n                        className=\"atp-backup-restore-btn\"\n                        onClick={() => {\n                          if (window.confirm(\"Restore this backup? Current data will be overwritten.\")) {\n                            restoreBackup(b);\n                            setMode(\"live\");\n                            showToast(\"\u2705 Restored \u2014 refresh to apply changes\");\n                          }\n                        }}\n                      >\n                        Restore\n                      </button>\n                    </div>\n                  ))}\n                </div>\n              </>\n            )}\n\n            <div className=\"atp-mode-help\">\n              Auto daily backup runs when you open the Admin panel. Backups include local settings, saved reels, custom animals, and preferences. Firebase data (accounts, posts) is always safe in Firebase and not included in local backups.\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        )}\n\n        {/* Toast */}\n        {toast && (\n          <div className=\"atp-toast\">{toast}</div>\n        )}\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "File rewritten successfully at: artifacts/animal-x/src/components/UploadReel.jsx"}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "File rewritten successfully at: artifacts/animal-x/src/components/WildlifeAI.jsx"}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "File created successfully at: artifacts/animal-x/src/pages/PrivacyPolicy.jsx"}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "File created successfully at: artifacts/animal-x/src/pages/TermsOfService.jsx"}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "File created successfully at: artifacts/animal-x/src/pages/CommunityGuidelines.jsx"}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "File created successfully at: artifacts/animal-x/src/components/AdminTestingPanel.jsx"}]}]}
{"memory_id": 379, "messages": [{"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Now writing the remaining files in parallel \u2014 Navbar update, App.tsx routes, Reels fix, and all the new CSS:"}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": [], "tool_calls": [{"type": "tool", "name": "write", "arguments": {"file_path": "artifacts/animal-x/src/components/Navbar.jsx", "content": "import { useState, useRef } from \"react\";\nimport { Link, useLocation } from \"wouter\";\nimport { useAuth } from \"../context/AuthContext\";\nimport { useSocial } from \"../context/SocialContext\";\nimport NotificationBell from \"./NotificationBell\";\nimport AdminDebugPanel from \"./AdminDebugPanel\";\nimport AdminTestingPanel from \"./AdminTestingPanel\";\n\nconst bottomItems = [\n  { href: \"/\", label: \"Home\", icon: \"\ud83c\udfe0\" },\n  { href: \"/animals\", label: \"Animals\", icon: \"\ud83d\udc3e\" },\n  { href: \"/reels\", label: \"Reels\", icon: \"\ud83c\udfac\" },\n  { href: \"/map\", label: \"Map\", icon: \"\ud83d\uddfa\ufe0f\" },\n  { href: \"/travel\", label: \"Travel\", icon: \"\u2708\ufe0f\" },\n  { href: \"/profile\", label: \"Profile\", icon: \"\ud83d\udc64\" },\n];\n\nexport default function Navbar() {\n  const [location, navigate] = useLocation();\n  const { user, isSuperAdmin, adminMode, unlockAdminMode, lockAdminMode } = useAuth();\n  const { broadcast, dismissBroadcast, sendBroadcast } = useSocial();\n  const [searchValue, setSearchValue] = useState(\"\");\n  const [tapCount, setTapCount] = useState(0);\n  const [adminPanelOpen, setAdminPanelOpen] = useState(false);\n  const [panelTab, setPanelTab] = useState(\"broadcast\"); // \"broadcast\" | \"testing\"\n  const [broadcastMsg, setBroadcastMsg] = useState(\"\");\n  const [debugOpen, setDebugOpen] = useState(false);\n  const [testingPanelOpen, setTestingPanelOpen] = useState(false);\n  const tapTimer = useRef(null);\n  const searchInputRef = useRef(null);\n\n  function submitSearch(e) {\n    e.preventDefault();\n    const q = searchValue.trim();\n    if (!q) return;\n    navigate(`/search?q=${encodeURIComponent(q)}`);\n    setSearchValue(\"\");\n    searchInputRef.current?.blur();\n  }\n\n  function handleLogoTap() {\n    const next = tapCount + 1;\n    setTapCount(next);\n    if (tapTimer.current) clearTimeout(tapTimer.current);\n    tapTimer.current = setTimeout(() => setTapCount(0), 1500);\n    if (next >= 7) {\n      setTapCount(0);\n      if (!user) { alert(\"Please login first.\"); return; }\n      if (!isSuperAdmin) { alert(\"Admin access restricted to super admin.\"); return; }\n      if (!adminMode) unlockAdminMode();\n      setAdminPanelOpen(v => !v);\n    }\n  }\n\n  async function handleSendBroadcast() {\n    if (!broadcastMsg.trim()) return;\n    await sendBroadcast(broadcastMsg.trim());\n    setBroadcastMsg(\"\");\n    setAdminPanelOpen(false);\n    alert(\"\u2705 Broadcast sent to all users!\");\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <>\n      {broadcast && (\n        <div className=\"broadcast-banner\">\n          <span className=\"broadcast-icon\">\ud83d\udce2</span>\n          <span className=\"broadcast-msg\">{broadcast.message}</span>\n          <button className=\"broadcast-dismiss\" onClick={() => dismissBroadcast(broadcast.id)}>\u2715</button>\n        </div>\n      )}\n\n      <header className=\"topbar\">\n        <button\n          className=\"brand-link\"\n          onClick={handleLogoTap}\n          style={{ background: \"none\", border: \"none\", cursor: \"pointer\" }}\n          title=\"Animal X (tap 7x for admin)\"\n        >\n          <span className=\"brand-icon\">\ud83e\udd81</span>\n          <span className=\"brand-name\">Animal X</span>\n        </button>\n\n        <form className=\"topbar-search\" onSubmit={submitSearch} role=\"search\">\n          <span className=\"topbar-search-icon\">\ud83d\udd0d</span>\n          <input\n            ref={searchInputRef}\n            type=\"search\"\n            value={searchValue}\n            onChange={e => setSearchValue(e.target.value)}\n            placeholder=\"Search animals or @users\u2026\"\n            aria-label=\"Search\"\n          />\n        </form>\n\n        <div className=\"topbar-actions\">\n          <Link href=\"/search\" className=\"topbar-search-btn\" title=\"Search creators\">\ud83d\udc65</Link>\n          <NotificationBell />\n          {adminMode && isSuperAdmin && (\n            <>\n              <button\n                className=\"debug-panel-btn\"\n                onClick={() => { setTestingPanelOpen(true); }}\n                title=\"Admin Testing Panel\"\n              >\n                \ud83e\uddea\n              </button>\n              <button\n                className=\"debug-panel-btn\"\n                onClick={() => setDebugOpen(true)}\n                title=\"Firebase Debug Panel\"\n              >\n                \ud83d\udee0\ufe0f\n              </button>\n            </>\n          )}\n          {!user && (\n            <Link href=\"/auth\" className=\"top-pill top-pill-primary\" title=\"Login\">Login</Link>\n          )}\n        </div>\n      </header>\n\n      {/* Admin Panel (Broadcast + Testing tabs) */}\n      {adminPanelOpen && isSuperAdmin && adminMode && (\n        <div className=\"admin-panel-overlay\">\n          <div className=\"admin-panel-sheet\">\n            <div className=\"admin-panel-header\">\n              <div className=\"admin-panel-tabs\">\n                <button\n                  className={`admin-panel-tab ${panelTab === \"broadcast\" ? \"active\" : \"\"}`}\n                  onClick={() => setPanelTab(\"broadcast\")}\n                >\n                  \ud83d\udce2 Broadcast\n                </button>\n                <button\n                  className={`admin-panel-tab ${panelTab === \"testing\" ? \"active\" : \"\"}`}\n                  onClick={() => setPanelTab(\"testing\")}\n                >\n                  \ud83e\uddea Testing\n                </button>\n              </div>\n              <button className=\"admin-panel-close\" onClick={() => setAdminPanelOpen(false)}>\u2715</button>\n            </div>\n\n            {panelTab === \"broadcast\" && (\n              <div className=\"admin-panel-body\">\n                <p className=\"admin-panel-hint\">Send a message to all Animal X users instantly.</p>\n                <textarea\n                  className=\"broadcast-input\"\n                  rows={3}\n                  placeholder=\"Type a message for ALL users\u2026\"\n                  value={broadcastMsg}\n                  onChange={e => setBroadcastMsg(e.target.value)}\n                />\n                <div className=\"admin-panel-actions\">\n                  <button\n                    className=\"auth-btn\"\n                    style={{ background: \"var(--surface2)\", flex: 1 }}\n                    onClick={() => { lockAdminMode(); setAdminPanelOpen(false); }}\n                  >\n                    \ud83d\udd12 Lock Admin\n                  </button>\n                  <button\n                    className=\"auth-btn\"\n                    style={{ flex: 1 }}\n                    onClick={handleSendBroadcast}\n                    disabled={!broadcastMsg.trim()}\n                  >\n                    \ud83d\udce2 Send to All\n                  </button>\n                </div>\n                <button\n                  className=\"admin-panel-debug-btn\"\n                  onClick={() => { setDebugOpen(true); setAdminPanelOpen(false); }}\n                >\n                  \ud83d\udee0\ufe0f Open Firebase Debug Panel\n                </button>\n              </div>\n            )}\n\n            {panelTab === \"testing\" && (\n              <div className=\"admin-panel-body\" style={{ padding: \"12px 0 0\" }}>\n                <p className=\"admin-panel-hint\" style={{ padding: \"0 16px\" }}>\n                  Control app modes, manage beta features, and backup/restore app data.\n                </p>\n                <button\n                  className=\"auth-btn\"\n                  style={{ margin: \"12px 16px 4px\", width: \"calc(100% - 32px)\" }}\n                  onClick={() => { setAdminPanelOpen(false); setTestingPanelOpen(true); }}\n                >\n                  \ud83e\uddea Open Full Testing Panel\n                </button>\n              </div>\n            )}\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      )}\n\n      <AdminDebugPanel open={debugOpen} onClose={() => setDebugOpen(false)} />\n      <AdminTestingPanel open={testingPanelOpen} onClose={() => setTestingPanelOpen(false)} />\n\n      <nav className=\"bottom-nav\">\n        {bottomItems.map((item) => {\n          const active = item.href === \"/\" ? location === \"/\" : location === item.href || location.startsWith(item.href + \"/\");\n          return (\n            <Link key={item.href} href={item.href} className={`bn-item ${active ? \"active\" : \"\"}`}>\n              <span className=\"bn-icon\">{item.icon}</span>\n              <span className=\"bn-label\">{item.label}</span>\n            </Link>\n          );\n        })}\n      </nav>\n    </>\n  );\n}\n"}}, {"type": "tool", "name": "write", "arguments": {"file_path": "artifacts/animal-x/src/App.tsx", "content": "import { useState, useEffect, lazy, Suspense, startTransition } from \"react\";\nimport { Switch, Route, Router as WouterRouter } from \"wouter\";\nimport { QueryClient, QueryClientProvider } from \"@tanstack/react-query\";\nimport { AuthProvider } from \"./context/AuthContext\";\nimport { SocialProvider } from \"./context/SocialContext\";\nimport { ThemeProvider } from \"./context/ThemeContext\";\nimport Navbar from \"./components/Navbar\";\nimport FirebaseStatusBanner from \"./components/FirebaseStatusBanner\";\nimport AutoTickPopup from \"./components/AutoTickPopup\";\nimport WildlifeAI from \"./components/WildlifeAI\";\n\n// Lazy load every page \u2014 each becomes its own JS chunk, loaded only when visited\nconst Home             = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/Home\"));\nconst Animals          = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/Animals\"));\nconst AnimalDetail     = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/AnimalDetail\"));\nconst Map              = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/Map\"));\nconst Reels            = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/Reels\"));\nconst Travel           = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/Travel\"));\nconst Chatbot          = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/Chatbot\"));\nconst HelpDesk         = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/HelpDesk\"));\nconst Auth             = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/Auth\"));\nconst Profile          = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/Profile\"));\nconst UserProfile      = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/UserProfile\"));\nconst Ads              = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/Ads\"));\nconst Search           = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/Search\"));\nconst PrivacyPolicy    = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/PrivacyPolicy\"));\nconst TermsOfService   = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/TermsOfService\"));\nconst CommunityGuidelines = lazy(() => import(\"./pages/CommunityGuidelines\"));\n\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient({\n  defaultOptions: {\n    queries: {\n      staleTime: 5 * 60 * 1000,\n      retry: 1,\n      refetchOnWindowFocus: false,\n    },\n  },\n});\n\nfunction PageFallback() {\n  return (\n    <div className=\"page-loading\">\n      <div className=\"page-loading-dot\" />\n      <div className=\"page-loading-dot\" />\n      <div className=\"page-loading-dot\" />\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n\nfunction NotFound() {\n  return (\n    <div style={{ textAlign: \"center\", padding: \"80px 20px\" }}>\n      <div style={{ fontSize: \"80px\" }}>\ud83d\udd0d</div>\n      <h2 style={{ fontSize: \"24px\", marginTop: \"16px\" }}>Page Not Found</h2>\n      <a href=\"/\" style={{ color: \"#22c55e\", marginTop: \"16px\", display: \"inline-block\" }}>\u2190 Go Home</a>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n\nfunction SplashScreen() {\n  return (\n    <div className=\"splash\">\n      <div className=\"splash-inner\">\n        <div className=\"splash-icon\">\ud83d\udc3e</div>\n        <h1 className=\"splash-title\">Animal X</h1>\n        <p className=\"splash-sub\">Wildlife Explorer</p>\n        <div className=\"splash-loader\">\n          <div className=\"splash-dot\" />\n          <div className=\"splash-dot\" />\n          <div className=\"splash-dot\" />\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n\nfunction Router() {\n  return (\n    <div className=\"app-layout\">\n      <Navbar />\n      <AutoTickPopup />\n      <main className=\"app-main\">\n        <Suspense fallback={<PageFallback />}>\n          <Switch>\n            <Route path=\"/\" component={Home} />\n            <Route path=\"/animals\" component={Animals} />\n            <Route path=\"/animals/:id\" component={AnimalDetail} />\n            <Route path=\"/map\" component={Map} />\n            <Route path=\"/reels\" component={Reels} />\n            <Route path=\"/travel\" component={Travel} />\n            <Route path=\"/chat\" component={Chatbot} />\n            <Route path=\"/help\" component={HelpDesk} />\n            <Route path=\"/auth\" component={Auth} />\n            <Route path=\"/profile\" component={Profile} />\n            <Route path=\"/user/:userId\" component={UserProfile} />\n            <Route path=\"/ads\" component={Ads} />\n            <Route path=\"/search\" component={Search} />\n            <Route path=\"/live-tracking\" component={Map} />\n            {/* Policy pages */}\n            <Route path=\"/privacy\" component={PrivacyPolicy} />\n            <Route path=\"/terms\" component={TermsOfService} />\n            <Route path=\"/guidelines\" component={CommunityGuidelines} />\n            <Route component={NotFound} />\n          </Switch>\n        </Suspense>\n      </main>\n      <WildlifeAI />\n      <FirebaseStatusBanner />\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n\nfunction App() {\n  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const timer = setTimeout(() => {\n      startTransition(() => setLoading(false));\n    }, 400);\n    return () => clearTimeout(timer);\n  }, []);\n\n  if (loading) return <SplashScreen />;\n\n  return (\n    <QueryClientProvider client={queryClient}>\n      <ThemeProvider>\n        <AuthProvider>\n          <SocialProvider>\n            <WouterRouter base={import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\\/$/, \"\")}>\n              <Router />\n            </WouterRouter>\n          </SocialProvider>\n        </AuthProvider>\n      </ThemeProvider>\n    </QueryClientProvider>\n  );\n}\n\nexport default App;\n"}}, {"type": "tool", "name": "edit", "arguments": {"file_path": "artifacts/animal-x/src/pages/Reels.jsx", "old_string": "  const [muted, setMuted] = useState(true);", "new_string": "  const [muted, setMuted] = useState(false);"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "File rewritten successfully at: artifacts/animal-x/src/components/Navbar.jsx"}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "File rewritten successfully at: artifacts/animal-x/src/App.tsx"}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The file artifacts/animal-x/src/pages/Reels.jsx has been edited. Here's the result of running `cat -n` on a snippet of artifacts/animal-x/src/pages/Reels.jsx:\n    61\u2192  const [liveReels, setLiveReels] = useState([]);\n    62\u2192  const [feed, setFeed] = useState([]);\n    63\u2192  const [catFilter, setCatFilter] = useState(\"All\");\n    64\u2192  const [activeIdx, setActiveIdx] = useState(0);\n    65\u2192  const [muted, setMuted] = useState(false);\n    66\u2192  const [commentsReel, setCommentsReel] = useState(null);\n    67\u2192  const [uploadOpen, setUploadOpen] = useState(false);\n    68\u2192  const [heartAnims, setHeartAnims] = useState({});\n    69\u2192  const [savedReels, setSavedReels] = useState(() => {\nReview the changes and make sure they are as expected (correct indentation, no duplicate lines, etc). Edit the file again if necessary."}]}]}
